ces. Entries 1, 2 and the line of entry 3 from round 2 are now strictly equal.\\n22: \\n23: **No entry fails E1, so there was nothing to stop at.** E1 was not loosened. The oracle fixture is unchanged: SHA-256 `5aee6d10…` before and after, and the JVM regeneration is identical.\\n24: \\n25: **Platform:** macOS arm64 only. Linux x86_64 is NOT RUN.\\n26: **Worktree:** `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c` (branch `jolt-j0c`, base HEAD `29986f9a`). Nothing is staged or committed.\\n27: **Logs:** `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/build/j0c/logs/r3-*`.\\n28: \\n29: **Spec text assumed.** E1 exactly as `collab/1792491122000-architect-j0c-error-parity.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md` \\\"The standard (E1)\\\" defines it. That ruling reads §7.8 J0c \\\"canonical CST/diagnostic packet equality\\\" as E1. **The owner has not confirmed that amendment, and I did not edit the design document.** One choice deviates from the ruling: it says the per-host pins are \\\"recorded in the fixture\\\", but your brief says to state them in the harness, so I followed the brief. The pins are in `src/dev/jolt_j0c_parity.clj` `helper-pins`, and the oracle fixture is untouched.\\n30: \\n31: ## Item → change\\n32: \\n33: | item | change |\\n34: |---|---|\\n35: | (1) Required helper patch (Architect (d)) | `antlr/python3/manifest.edn` `:targets :cpp :patches \\\"Cpp/Python3LexerBase.cpp\\\"`, the same exact-text mechanism as the other targets. (a) `commonToken`'s factory call, used for INDENT and the end-of-input EOF, now takes `getLine(), getCharPositionInLine()` from the lexer instead of `lastToken ? … : 0`, matching Java's `new CommonToken(_tokenFactorySourcePair, …)`. (b) The existing positioned-DEDENT replacement gains `if (lastToken) dedent->setLine(lastToken->getLine());`, matching Java's `createDedent`. Java dereferences unconditionally; the guard only keeps a null from crashing the process, which is disclosed in the manifest comment. Regenerated with `clojure -M:antlr-gen --target cpp`. The first run failed closed on the digest check as expected (exit 1). I recorded the new digest; re-runs exit 0. Rebuilt with `bb build:jolt-native` |\\n36: | (2) E1 parity harness | `src/dev/jolt_j0c_parity.clj`, detailed below |\\n37: | (2, prerequisite) offending token type | Telling a helper-fabricated token from a real one needs the offending token's type, which round 2 did not marshal. `jolt_parser.cpp`: each JPX1 error record gains `i32 offending token type` (−2 when there is no token), and the layout version goes **1 → 2**. `cst.jolt` accepts only layout 2 and decodes `:type`. Round-1 `jolt_parser_parse`/JPT1 is unchanged |\\n38: | (3) cmd G1 | `cst.jolt` `platform`: `(or (System/getProperty \\\"os.name\\\") \\\"\\\")`. nil reads as Linux, as `jolt.socket.native/os` decides; a nil `os.arch` reads as x86_64. I chose the nil guard over requiring `jolt.socket.native`, so the adapter's load closure stays `yang.antlr.cst` + `export` + `packet` (the harness asserts this) |\\n39: | (4) Re-run | All in the foreground on macOS; see the command table |\\n40: \\n41: ### The E1 harness (item 2)\\n42: \\n43: **Strict checks:**\\n44: - every field of an ok packet;\\n45: - for error packets, every field except `:yang.cst/errors` (outcome, version, unit, grammar, complete);\\n46: - `cst/first-failure`;\\n47: - every probe answer and its `first-failure` call sequence.\\n48: \\n49: **Every jolt packet passes `(packet/validate! p {:source source})`.**\\n50: \\n51: **Error packets also require:**\\n52: - at least one error;\\n53: - the first error's `:kind` and `:span` equal to the JVM's;\\n54: - the first error's `:message` is a non-empty string;\\n55: - the first error's `:line`/`:column` equal to the JVM's when the offending token is real. When it is helper-fabricated, they must equal the pinned constant.\\n56:   - Helper-fabricated means INDENT, DEDENT, EOF, or a zero-width NEWLINE. This is decided from jolt's own record of the offending token's type.\\n57:   - An unpinned helper-token entry fails, a pin on an entry with a real-token first error fails, and a pin that names no corpus entry fails.\\n58: \\n59: **Exempt:** message text, expecting-sets, and errors after the first.\\n60: \\n61: **Pinned jolt constants,** one-line reasons in the harness. They all equal the JVM's now, because the patch gives the C++ helper the Java helper's coordinates.\\n62: \\n63: | entry | [line col] |\\n64: |---|---|\\n65: | `blank-lines` | [3 2] |\\n66: | `missing-final-newline` | [1 5] |\\n67: | `malformed-unexpected-indent` | [1 2] |\\n68: | `malformed-unexpected-dedent` | [2 0] |\\n69: | `incomplete-def-header` | [2 0] |\\n70: | `incomplete-decorator` | [2 0] |\\n71: | `incomplete-continuation` | [2 0] |\\n72: | `bracket-list-open` | [3 0] |\\n73: | `bracket-dict-open` | [2 0] |\\n74: \\n75: I found these 9 entries with a discovery pass (`r3-discover.log`): the first errors whose offending type is INDENT, DEDENT or EOF. The one NEWLINE first error, `malformed-unexpected-newline`, has width, so it is real and checked against the JVM.\\n76: \\n77: **E1 self-test (7 PASS), so the checker is not vacuous.** Mutated jolt packets are refused for:\\n78: - an INDENT at line 0, which is the round-2 C++ helper's value: flagged `:validate!` and `:helper-pin-drift`;\\n79: - a helper-token column off its pin;\\n80: - a real-token line off the JVM's;\\n81: - a first-error span off the JVM's;\\n82: - an empty message;\\n83: - no errors;\\n84: - an ok packet with one node changed.\\n85: \\n86: ## Digests before → after\\n87: \\n88: **manifest `:cpp :generated`:** only `Python3LexerBase.cpp` changed, from `65027edf9cf43a5d09c745b4936576d3bd5da466b733f337420f73ae368a4bed` to `2483e344297051efebf6f8228647eda53186b143874699e4062f1b8c9c3c5660`. The other 7 cpp files are unchanged (`a8be1b51…`, `a1cb6339…`, `8548fd2c…`, `d30cc4df…`, `5e62a9c3…`, `38a2790b…`, `59afaba9…`).\\n89: \\n90: **Java/JS/Dart byte-identical to base** (`r