":{\"source\":\"tool\",\"messageId\":\"e55fc800-60e8-4261-9cb0-055a7dfc3af3\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Okay, now let me adversarially read through the C++ — worker ownership, busy guard, SourceStream BOM fix, Oversize, seam gating, non-allocating paths. The file is currently probably around 700 lines. Going to read it.\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now the wrapper source, the key adversarial target.\\n\\n\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_ac06bcfc4a574f019818ed5f\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/native/jolt-parser/jolt_parser.cpp\"}}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"model\",\"createdAt\":1792508093589,\"messageId\":\"59fe5c36-19ff-47e7-b381-e0c9d2e66b4c\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_ac06bcfc4a574f019818ed5f\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 1/1 file, 694 lines\\n1: // jolt-parser: the extern \\\"C\\\" boundary between jolt and the ANTLR4 C++\\n2: // Python3 parser (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md §7.3).\\n3: //\\n4: // J0c round 1 probe surface. Bytes in, bytes out: the caller passes UTF-8\\n5: // source by pointer and length and receives one private marshalling buffer,\\n6: // which it copies and returns through jolt_parser_free. No C++ class, layout\\n7: // or exception crosses this boundary; every entry catches std::exception and\\n8: // (...) and answers an explicit status. This is process-local marshalling (like\\n9: // a sockaddr), not a value codec: it never enters a stream. Packets are built\\n10: // by the shared jolt/Clojure exporter from these records, never here.\\n11: //\\n12: // Buffer layout, all integers little-endian:\\n13: //\\n14: //   magic   \\\"JPT1\\\"\\n15: //   u32     layout version (1)\\n16: //   u32     status (0 ok, 1 syntax errors)\\n17: //   u32     rule-name count R,     then R  x (u32 len, UTF-8 bytes)\\n18: //   u32     symbolic-name count S, then S  x (u32 len, UTF-8 bytes)\\n19: //   u32     node count N, then N preorder records:\\n20: //             u8  kind (0 rule, 1 token)\\n21: //             rule:  u32 rule index, u32 child count\\n22: //             token: i32 token type, u32 start, u32 stop (code-point indexes,\\n23: //                    0xFFFFFFFF = none), u32 text len, UTF-8 text\\n24: //   u32     error count E, then E x (u32 line, u32 column, u32 len, UTF-8 msg)\\n25: //\\n26: // Status codes returned by jolt_parser_parse:\\n27: //    0  parsed, buffer written (status field says whether errors occurred)\\n28: //   -1  invalid arguments\\n29: //   -2  C++ exception (std::exception); *out holds its message, UTF-8\\n30: //   -3  unknown exception\\n31: // On -2/-3 the message buffer is built without anything that can throw\\n32: // (strlen/malloc/memcpy only); if even that malloc fails, *out stays NULL and\\n33: // only the status reports the failure. No handler can throw.\\n34: //\\n35: //   -4  output would exceed the bound (64 MiB), checked while the buffer\\n36: //       grows, so an oversize answer is never built in full\\n37: //   -5  the worker is in use by another call (a worker serves one thread at\\n38: //       a time; this call did nothing)\\n39: //\\n40: // jolt_parser_parse (J0c round 1) recognizes with the generated static\\n41: // caches. jolt_parser_export takes a worker (§7.4, round 4): an opaque handle\\n42: // from jolt_parser_worker_new that owns its lexer and parser DFA vectors and\\n43: // PredictionContextCaches; each call installs fresh Lexer/ParserATNSimulators\\n44: // over them in place of the generated defaults (which point at the static\\n45: // caches) before recognition. The ATNs are the generated immutable tables and\\n46: // stay shared. jolt_parser_worker_free disposes the handle.\\n47: //\\n48: // TEST SEAMS, compiled only with -DJOLT_PARSER_TEST_SEAMS=ON (CMake option,\\n49: // default OFF): jolt_parser_inject_fault makes the next parses fail\\n50: // deterministically so the containment paths can be shown without\\n51: // exhausting memory; jolt_parser_static_cache_stats and\\n52: // jolt_parser_worker_cache_stats count cache contents;\\n53: // jolt_parser_thread_info reports the calling thread's stack;\\n54: // jolt_parser_heap_in_use reports malloc's bytes in use.\\n55: //\\n56: // jolt_parser_export answers the records the jolt yang.antlr.cst adapter\\n57: // hands to the shared exporter (§7.3). Indexes are i32, -1 for ANTLR's\\n58: // \\\"none\\\" (INVALID_INDEX, a stop before a zero-width start), as the JVM\\n59: // reports them. Its layout (version from jolt_parser_export_layout_version):\\n60: //\\n61: //   magic   \\\"JPX1\\\"\\n62: //   u32     layout version (2; 2 added the offending token type)\\n63: //   u32     status (0 ok, 1 syntax errors)\\n64: //   u32     rule-name count R,     then R x (u32 len, UTF-8 bytes)\\n65: //   u32     symbolic-name count S, then S x (u32 len, UTF-8 bytes; \\\"\\\" none)\\n66: //   u32     literal-name count S,  then S x (u32 len, UTF-8 bytes; \\\"\\\" none)\\n67: //   u32     node count N, then N preorder records:\\n68: //             u8  kind (0 rule, 1 token)\\n69: //             rule:  u32 rule index, u32 child count,\\n70: //                    u8 has-start, i32 context start (start token's start)\\n71: //             token: i32 type, i32 start, i32 stop, i32 token index,\\n72: //                    u32 text len, UTF-8 text\\n73: //   u32     error count E, then E x\\n74: //             u32 line, u32 column, u32 len, UTF-8 message,\\n75: //             u8 span kind (0 none, 1 offending token, 2 lexer),\\n76: //             i32 a, i32 b (token start/stop, or lexer token-start char\\n77: //             index / input index when the error was reported),\\n78: //             i32 offending token type (-2 when there is no token)\\n79: //   first-failure evidence (the first error reported, lexer or parser):\\n80: //             u8 kind (0 none, 1 lexical, 2 token), u8 no-viable-alt,\\n81: //             i32 offending token index, u32 tokens buffered at the report\\n82: //   u32     buffered token count T after the parse, then T x\\n83: //             (i32 type, i32 token index, i32 start, i32 stop)\\n84: \\n85: #include <atomic>\\n86: #include <cstdint>\\n87: #include <cstdlib>\\n88: #include <cstring>\\n89: #include <limits>\\n90: #include <string>\\n91: #include <string_view>\\n92: #include <vector>\\n93: \\n94: #include \\\"antlr4-runtime.h\\\"\\n95: #include \\\"support/Utf8.h\\\"\\n96: #include \\\"Python3Lexer.h\\\"\\n97: #include \\\"Python3Parser.h\\\"\\n98: \\n99: // After the generated headers: Mach's headers define TRUE/FALSE, which are\\n100: // also generated token names.\\n101: #include <pthread.h>\\n102: #if defined(__APPLE__)\\n103: #include <malloc/malloc.h>\\n104: #elif defined(__GLIBC__)\\n105: #include <malloc.h>\\n106: #include <sys/syscall.h>\\n107: #include <unistd.h>\\n108: #endif\\n109: \\n110: #define JOLT_EXPORT extern \\\"C\\\" __attribute__((visibility(\\\"default\\\")))\\n111: \\n112: namespace {\\n113: \\n114: constexpr size_t kMaxOutput = 64u * 1024u * 1024u;\\n115: \\n116: #ifdef JOLT_PARSER_TEST_SEAMS\\n117: // 0 off; 1 throw std::bad_alloc inside the parse; 2 throw a non-std\\n118: // exception; 3 as 1, and the failure handler's malloc fails too.\\n119: std::atomic<int32_t> g_fault{0};\\n120: \\n121: void maybe_fault() {\\n122:   switch (g_fault.load()) {\\n123:     case 1:\\n124:     case 3: throw std::bad_alloc();\\n125:     case 2: throw 42;\\n126:     default: break;\\n127:   }\\n128: }\\n129: \\n130: bool fail_handler_malloc() { return g_fault.load() == 3; }\\n131: #else\\n132: void maybe_fault() {}\\n133: bool fail_handler_malloc() { return false; }\\n134: #endif\\n135: \\n136: // Thrown (and caught by the entries) when the buffer would pass kMaxOutput.\\n137: struct Oversize {};\\n138: \\n139: struct Out {\\n140:   std::vector<uint8_t> buf;\\n141:   void room(size_t n) {\\n142:     if (n > kMaxOutput - buf.size()) throw Oversize{};\\n143:   }\\n144:   void u8(uint8_t v) {\\n145:     room(1);\\n146:     buf.push_back(v);\\n147:   }\\n148:   void u32(uint32_t v) {\\n149:     room(4);\\n150:     for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i) buf.push_back(static_cast<uint8_t>(v >> (8 * i)));\\n151:   }\\n152:   void str(std::string_view s) {\\n153:     u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(s.size()));\\n154:     room(s.size());\\n155:     buf.insert(buf.end(), s.begin(), s.end());\\n156:   }\\n157: };\\n158: \\n159: uint32_t idx(size_t i) {\\n160:   return i > std::numeric_limits<uint32_t>::max()\\n161:              ? std::numeric_limits<uint32_t>::max()\\n162:              : static_cast<uint32_t>(i);\\n163: }\\n164: \\n165: struct Error {\\n166:   uint32_t line, column;\\n167:   std::string msg;\\n168: };\\n169: \\n170: class Collect : public antlr4::BaseErrorListener {\\n171:  public:\\n172:   std::vector<Error> errors;\\n173:   void syntaxError(antlr4::Recognizer*, antlr4::Token*, size_t line,\\n174:                    size_t column, const std::string& msg,\\n175:                    std::exception_ptr) override {\\n176:     errors.push_back({idx(line), idx(column), msg});\\n177:   }\\n178: };\\n179: \\n180: void walk(antlr4::tree::ParseTree* t, Out& out, uint32_t& count) {\\n181:   ++count;\\n182:   if (auto* term = dynamic_cast<antlr4::tree::TerminalNode*>(t)) {\\n183:     antlr4::Token* tok = term->getSymbol();\\n184:     out.u8(1);\\n185:     out.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(static_cast<int32_t>(tok->getType())));\\n186:     out.u32(idx(tok->getStartIndex()));\\n187:     out.u32(idx(tok->getStopIndex()));\\n188:     out.str(tok->getText());\\n189:     return;\\n190:   }\\n191:   auto* ctx = dynamic_cast<antlr4::ParserRuleContext*>(t);\\n192:   out.u8(0);\\n193:   out.u32(idx(ctx->getRuleIndex()));\\n194:   out.u32(idx(ctx->children.size()));\\n195:   for (auto* c : ctx->children) walk(c, out, count);\\n196: }\\n197: \\n198: int32_t hand_off(const std::vector<uint8_t>& bytes, uint8_t** out,\\n199:                  size_t* out_len) {\\n200:   if (bytes.size() > kMaxOutput) return -4;\\n201:   auto* p = static_cast<uint8_t*>(std::malloc(bytes.empty() ? 1 : bytes.size()));\\n202:   if (!p) return -3;\\n203:   if (!bytes.empty()) std::memcpy(p, bytes.data(), bytes.size());\\n204:   *out = p;\\n205:   *out_len = bytes.size();\\n206:   return 0;\\n207: }\\n208: \\n209: // The failure answer: `status`, plus the message copied into a malloc'd\\n210: // buffer when that is possible. Nonallocating apart from that one malloc,\\n211: // whose failure leaves *out NULL. Never throws.\\n212: int32_t message(const char* what, int32_t status, uint8_t** out,\\n213:                 size_t* out_len) noexcept {\\n214:   *out = nullptr;\\n215:   *out_len = 0;\\n216:   const char* m = what ? what : \\\"\\\";\\n217:   size_t n = std::strlen(m);\\n218:   void* p = fail_handler_malloc() ? nullptr : std::malloc(n == 0 ? 1 : n);\\n219:   if (p) {\\n220:     std::memcpy(p, m, n);\\n221:     *out = static_cast<uint8_t*>(p);\\n222:     *out_len = n;\\n223:   }\\n224:   return status;\\n225: }\\n226: \\n227: // --- jolt_parser_export ------------------------------------------------------\\n228: \\n229: int32_t sidx(size_t i) {\\n230:   if (i == std::numeric_limits<size_t>::max()) return -1;  // INVALID_INDEX\\n231:   return i > static_cast<size_t>(std::numeric_limits<int32_t>::max())\\n232:              ? std::numeric_limits<int32_t>::max()\\n233:              : static_cast<int32_t>(i);\\n234: }\\n235: \\n236: struct ExportError {\\n237:   uint32_t line, column;\\n238:   std::string msg;\\n239:   uint8_t span_kind;\\n240:   int32_t a, b;\\n241:   int32_t type;\\n242: };\\n243: \\n244: class ExportCollect : public antlr4::BaseErrorListener {\\n245:  public:\\n246:   explicit ExportCollect(antlr4::CommonTokenStream* tokens) : tokens_(tokens) {}\\n247:   std::vector<ExportError> errors;\\n248:   uint8_t failure_kind = 0;  // 0 none, 1 lexical, 2 token\\n249:   uint8_t no_viable = 0;\\n250:   int32_t failure_index = -1;\\n251:   uint32_t buffered = 0;\\n252: \\n253:   void syntaxError(antlr4::Recognizer* recognizer, antlr4::Token* offending,\\n254:                    size_t line, size_t column, const std::string& msg,\\n255:                    std::exception_ptr e) override {\\n256:     ExportError err{idx(line), idx(column), msg, 0, -1, -1, -2};\\n257:     auto* lexer = dynamic_cast<antlr4::Lexer*>(recognizer);\\n258:     if (offending) {\\n259:       err.span_kind = 1;\\n260:       err.a = sidx(offending->getStartIndex());\\n261:       err.b = sidx(offending->getStopIndex());\\n262:       err.type = static_cast<int32_t>(offending->getType());\\n263:     } else if (lexer) {\\n264:       err.span_kind = 2;\\n265:       err.a = sidx(lexer->tokenStartCharIndex);\\n266:       err.b = sidx(lexer->getInputStream()->index());\\n267:     }\\n268:     if (failure_kind == 0) {\\n269:       if (!offending) {\\n270:         failure_kind = 1;\\n271:       } else {\\n272:         failure_kind = 2;\\n273:         failure_index = sidx(offending->getTokenIndex());\\n274:         if (e) {\\n275:           try {\\n276:             std::rethrow_exception(e);\\n277:           } catch (const antlr4::NoViableAltException&) {\\n278:             no_viable = 1;\\n279:           } catch (...) {\\n280:           }\\n281:         }\\n282:       }\\n283:       buffered = idx(tokens_->getTokens().size());\\n284:     }\\n285:     errors.push_back(std::move(err));\\n286:   }\\n287: \\n288:  private:\\n289:   antlr4::CommonTokenStream* tokens_;\\n290: };\\n291: \\n292: void walk_export(antlr4::tree::ParseTree* t, Out& out, uint32_t& count) {\\n293:   ++count;\\n294:   if (auto* term = dynamic_cast<antlr4::tree::TerminalNode*>(t)) {\\n295:     antlr4::Token* tok = term->getSymbol();\\n296:     out.u8(1);\\n297:     out.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(static_cast<int32_t>(tok->getType())));\\n298:     out.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(sidx(tok->getStartIndex())));\\n299:     out.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(sidx(tok->getStopIndex())));\\n300:     out.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(sidx(tok->getTokenIndex())));\\n301:     out.str(tok->getText());\\n302:     return;\\n303:   }\\n304:   auto* ctx = dynamic_cast<antlr4::ParserRuleContext*>(t);\\n305:   out.u8(0);\\n306:   out.u32(idx(ctx->getRuleIndex()));\\n307:   out.u32(idx(ctx->children.size()));\\n308:   out.u8(ctx->start ? 1 : 0);\\n309:   out.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(ctx->start ? sidx(ctx->start->getStartIndex()) : -1));\\n310:   for (auto* c : ctx->children) walk_export(c, out, count);\\n311: }\\n312: \\n313: // The source as code points, exactly: a strict UTF-8 decode that throws on an\\n314: // illegal sequence (as ANTLRInputStream's own does) but keeps a leading\\n315: // U+FEFF. ANTLRInputStream::load strips a UTF-8 BOM\\n316: // (runtime/src/ANTLRInputStream.cpp:43-48); the JVM's CharStreams.fromString\\n317: // does not, and a stripped BOM shifts every index against the source the\\n318: // exporter maps spans onto (J0c round 4 input policy).\\n319: class SourceStream : public antlr4::ANTLRInputStream {\\n320:  public:\\n321:   explicit SourceStream(std::string_view utf8) {\\n322:     auto cps = antlrcpp::Utf8::strictDecode(utf8);\\n323:     if (!cps.has_value())\\n324:       throw antlr4::IllegalArgumentException(\\n325:           \\\"UTF-8 string contains an illegal byte sequence\\\");\\n326:     _data = std::move(cps).value();\\n327:     p = 0;\\n328:   }\\n329: };\\n330: \\n331: // --- workers (§7.4) -----------------------------------------------------------\\n332: \\n333: constexpr uint64_t kWorkerTag = 0x4a504152534552ull;  // \\\"JPARSER\\\"\\n334: \\n335: std::vector<antlr4::dfa::DFA> fresh_dfa(const antlr4::atn::ATN& atn) {\\n336:   std::vector<antlr4::dfa::DFA> dfa;\\n337:   const size_t n = atn.getNumberOfDecisions();\\n338:   dfa.reserve(n);\\n339:   for (size_t i = 0; i < n; ++i) dfa.emplace_back(atn.getDecisionState(i), i);\\n340:   return dfa;\\n341: }\\n342: \\n343: // The generated, immutable ATNs (static data initialized once by the\\n344: // generated constructors).\\n345: struct Atns {\\n346:   const antlr4::atn::ATN* lexer;\\n347:   const antlr4::atn::ATN* parser;\\n348: };\\n349: \\n350: Atns generated_atns() {\\n351:   antlr4::ANTLRInputStream input(\\\"\\\");\\n352:   Python3Lexer lexer(&input);\\n353:   antlr4::CommonTokenStream tokens(&lexer);\\n354:   Python3Parser parser(&tokens);\\n355:   return {&lexer.getATN(), &parser.getATN()};\\n356: }\\n357: \\n358: struct Worker {\\n359:   uint64_t tag = kWorkerTag;\\n360:   const antlr4::atn::ATN* lexer_atn;\\n361:   const antlr4::atn::ATN* parser_atn;\\n362:   std::vector<antlr4::dfa::DFA> lexer_dfa;\\n363:   std::vector<antlr4::dfa::DFA> parser_dfa;\\n364:   antlr4::atn::PredictionContextCache lexer_ctx;\\n365:   antlr4::atn::PredictionContextCache parser_ctx;\\n366:   std::atomic<bool> busy{false};\\n367: \\n368:   explicit Worker(Atns atns)\\n369:       : lexer_atn(atns.lexer),\\n370:         parser_atn(atns.parser),\\n371:         lexer_dfa(fresh_dfa(*atns.lexer)),\\n372:         parser_dfa(fresh_dfa(*atns.parser)) {}\\n373: };\\n374: \\n375: Worker* as_worker(void* w) {\\n376:   auto* worker = static_cast<Worker*>(w);\\n377:   return worker && worker->tag == kWorkerTag ? worker : nullptr;\\n378: }\\n379: \\n380: // Holds a worker for one call; a second concurrent call is refused.\\n381: struct Hold {\\n382:   Worker* w;\\n383:   bool held;\\n384:   explicit Hold(Worker* worker) : w(worker) {\\n385:     bool expected = false;\\n386:     held = w->busy.compare_exchange_strong(expected, true);\\n387:   }\\n388:   ~Hold() {\\n389:     if (held) w->busy.store(false);\\n390:   }\\n391: };\\n392: \\n393: }  // namespace\\n394: \\n395: // A new worker owning fresh DFA vectors and PredictionContextCaches. NULL when\\n396: // it cannot be made (nothing throws across the boundary).\\n397: JOLT_EXPORT void* jolt_parser_worker_new(void) {\\n398:   try {\\n399:     return new Worker(generated_atns());\\n400:   } catch (...) {\\n401:     return nullptr;\\n402:   }\\n403: }\\n404: \\n405: // Dispose a worker and its caches. NULL is accepted. The caller must not use\\n406: // the handle again, nor free it while a call on it runs.\\n407: JOLT_EXPORT void jolt_parser_worker_free(void* w) {\\n408:   if (Worker* worker = as_worker(w)) {\\n409:     worker->tag = 0;\\n410:     delete worker;\\n411:   }\\n412: }\\n413: \\n414: // Parse UTF-8 `src[0, len)` from `file_input` with `worker`'s caches and\\n415: // answer the exporter's records (layout \\\"JPX1\\\" above). Statuses as\\n416: // jolt_parser_parse, plus -5; -1 also for a NULL or unrecognized worker.\\n417: JOLT_EXPORT int32_t jolt_parser_export(void* worker, const uint8_t* src,\\n418:                                        size_t len, uint8_t** out,\\n419:                                        size_t* out_len) {\\n420:   if (!out || !out_len || (!src && len != 0)) return -1;\\n421:   *out = nullptr;\\n422:   *out_len = 0;\\n423:   Worker* w = as_worker(worker);\\n424:   if (!w) return -1;\\n425:   Hold hold(w);\\n426:   if (!hold.held) return -5;\\n427:   try {\\n428:     maybe_fault();\\n429:     SourceStream input(\\n430:         std::string_view(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(src), len));\\n431:     Python3Lexer lexer(&input);\\n432:     // setInterpreter deletes the generated default simulator, the one over\\n433:     // the static caches; the generated destructors delete these at scope exit\\n434:     lexer.setInterpreter(new antlr4::atn::LexerATNSimulator(\\n435:         &lexer, *w->lexer_atn, w->lexer_dfa, w->lexer_ctx));\\n436:     antlr4::CommonTokenStream tokens(&lexer);\\n437:     Python3Parser parser(&tokens);\\n438:     parser.setInterpreter(new antlr4::atn::ParserATNSimulator(\\n439:         &parser, *w->parser_atn, w->parser_dfa, w->parser_ctx));\\n440:     ExportCollect errors(&tokens);\\n441:     lexer.removeErrorListeners();\\n442:     parser.removeErrorListeners();\\n443:     lexer.addErrorListener(&errors);\\n444:     parser.addErrorListener(&errors);\\n445: \\n446:     antlr4::tree::ParseTree* tree = parser.file_input();\\n447: \\n448:     Out o;\\n449:     o.buf.insert(o.buf.end(), {'J', 'P', 'X', '1'});\\n450:     o.u32(2);\\n451:     o.u32(errors.errors.empty() ? 0 : 1);\\n452:     const auto& rules = parser.getRuleNames();\\n453:     o.u32(idx(rules.size()));\\n454:     for (const auto& r : rules) o.str(r);\\n455:     const auto& vocab = parser.getVocabulary();\\n456:     size_t max_type = vocab.getMaxTokenType();\\n457:     o.u32(idx(max_type + 1));\\n458:     for (size_t i = 0; i <= max_type; ++i) o.str(vocab.getSymbolicName(i));\\n459:     o.u32(idx(max_type + 1));\\n460:     for (size_t i = 0; i <= max_type; ++i) o.str(vocab.getLiteralName(i));\\n461:     size_t count_at = o.buf.size();\\n462:     o.u32(0);\\n463:     uint32_t count = 0;\\n464:     walk_export(tree, o, count);\\n465:     for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i)\\n466:       o.buf[count_at + i] = static_cast<uint8_t>(count >> (8 * i));\\n467:     o.u32(idx(errors.errors.size()));\\n468:     for (const auto& e : errors.errors) {\\n469:       o.u32(e.line);\\n470:       o.u32(e.column);\\n471:       o.str(e.msg);\\n472:       o.u8(e.span_kind);\\n473:       o.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(e.a));\\n474:       o.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(e.b));\\n475:       o.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(e.type));\\n476:     }\\n477:     o.u8(errors.failure_kind);\\n478:     o.u8(errors.no_viable);\\n479:     o.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(errors.failure_index));\\n480:     o.u32(errors.buffered);\\n481:     const auto buffered = tokens.getTokens();\\n482:     o.u32(idx(buffered.size()));\\n483:     for (auto* t : buffered) {\\n484:       o.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(static_cast<int32_t>(t->getType())));\\n485:       o.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(sidx(t->getTokenIndex())));\\n486:       o.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(sidx(t->getStartIndex())));\\n487:       o.u32(static_cast<uint32_t>(sidx(t->getStopIndex())));\\n488:     }\\n489:     return hand_off(o.buf, out, out_len);\\n490:   } catch (const Oversize&) {\\n491:     return -4;\\n492:   } catch (const std::exception& e) {\\n493:     return message(e.what(), -2, out, out_len);\\n494:   } catch (...) {\\n495:     return message(\\\"unknown exception\\\", -3, out, out_len);\\n496:   }\\n497: }\\n498: \\n499: // Parse UTF-8 `src[0, len)` from the `file_input` rule, with the generated\\n500: // static caches (the round-1 probe surface).\\n501: JOLT_EXPORT int32_t jolt_parser_parse(const uint8_t* src, size_t len,\\n502:                                       uint8_t** out, size_t* out_len) {\\n503:   if (!out || !out_len || (!src && len != 0)) return -1;\\n504:   *out = nullptr;\\n505:   *out_len = 0;\\n506:   try {\\n507:     maybe_fault();\\n508:     SourceStream input(\\n509:         std::string_view(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(src), len));\\n510:     Python3Lexer lexer(&input);\\n511:     antlr4::CommonTokenStream tokens(&lexer);\\n512:     Python3Parser parser(&tokens);\\n513:     Collect errors;\\n514:     lexer.removeErrorListeners();\\n515:     parser.removeErrorListeners();\\n516:     lexer.addErrorListener(&errors);\\n517:     parser.addErrorListener(&errors);\\n518: \\n519:     antlr4::tree::ParseTree* tree = parser.file_input();\\n520: \\n521:     Out o;\\n522:     o.buf.insert(o.buf.end(), {'J', 'P', 'T', '1'});\\n523:     o.u32(1);\\n524:     o.u32(errors.errors.empty() ? 0 : 1);\\n525:     const auto& rules = parser.getRuleNames();\\n526:     o.u32(idx(rules.size()));\\n527:     for (const auto& r : rules) o.str(r);\\n528:     const auto& vocab = parser.getVocabulary();\\n529:     size_t max_type = vocab.getMaxTokenType();\\n530:     o.u32(idx(max_type + 1));\\n531:     for (size_t i = 0; i <= max_type; ++i) o.str(vocab.getSymbolicName(i));\\n532:     size_t count_at = o.buf.size();\\n533:     o.u32(0);\\n534:     uint32_t count = 0;\\n535:     walk(tree, o, count);\\n536:     for (int i = 0; i < 4; ++i)\\n537:       o.buf[count_at + i] = static_cast<uint8_t>(count >> (8 * i));\\n538:     o.u32(idx(errors.errors.size()));\\n539:     for (const auto& e : errors.errors) {\\n540:       o.u32(e.line);\\n541:       o.u32(e.column);\\n542:       o.str(e.msg);\\n543:     }\\n544:     return hand_off(o.buf, out, out_len);\\n545:   } catch (const Oversize&) {\\n546:     return -4;\\n547:   } catch (const std::exception& e) {\\n548:     return message(e.what(), -2, out, out_len);\\n549:   } catch (...) {\\n550:     return message(\\\"unknown exception\\\", -3, out, out_len);\\n551:   }\\n552: }\\n553: \\n554: // Release a buffer jolt_parser_parse handed out. NULL is accepted.\\n555: JOLT_EXPORT void jolt_parser_free(uint8_t* p) { std::free(p); }\\n556: \\n557: // The JPT1 layout version jolt_parser_parse writes.\\n558: JOLT_EXPORT int32_t jolt_parser_layout_version(void) { return 1; }\\n559: \\n560: // The JPX1 layout version jolt_parser_export writes.\\n561: JOLT_EXPORT int32_t jolt_parser_export_layout_version(void) { return 2; }\\n562: \\n563: #ifdef JOLT_PARSER_TEST_SEAMS\\n564: \\n565: // TEST SEAM: set the fault mode (0 off, 1-3 as g_fault above) for later\\n566: // parses. Answers the previous mode.\\n567: JOLT_EXPORT int32_t jolt_parser_inject_fault(int32_t mode) {\\n568:   return g_fault.exchange(mode);\\n569: }\\n570: \\n571: namespace {\\n572: \\n573: // Reading two private counters for the stats below, through the standard\\n574: // explicit-instantiation access idiom (test seam only; reads, never writes).\\n575: template <auto M, typename Tag>\\n576: struct Peek {\\n577:   friend auto peek(Tag) { return M; }\\n578: };\\n579: struct CtxData {};\\n580: struct NextUpdated {};\\n581: auto peek(CtxData);\\n582: auto peek(NextUpdated);\\n583: template struct Peek<&antlr4::atn::PredictionContextCache::_data, CtxData>;\\n584: template struct Peek<&antlr4::atn::ATNState::_nextTokenUpdated, NextUpdated>;\\n585: \\n586: void dfa_counts(const std::vector<antlr4::dfa::DFA>& dfas, uint64_t& states,\\n587:                 uint64_t& edges) {\\n588:   for (const auto& d : dfas) {\\n589:     states += d.states.size() + (d.s0 ? 1 : 0);\\n590:     if (d.s0) edges += d.s0->edges.size();\\n591:     for (const auto* st : d.states) edges += st->edges.size();\\n592:   }\\n593: }\\n594: \\n595: uint64_t ctx_size(const antlr4::atn::PredictionContextCache& c) {\\n596:   return (c.*peek(CtxData{})).size();\\n597: }\\n598: \\n599: uint64_t memo_count(const antlr4::atn::ATN& atn) {\\n600:   uint64_t n = 0;\\n601:   for (auto* st : atn.states)\\n602:     if (st && (st->*peek(NextUpdated{})).load()) ++n;\\n603:   return n;\\n604: }\\n605: \\n606: }  // namespace\\n607: \\n608: // TEST SEAM: the generated static caches and the shared ATNs' lazily filled\\n609: // next-token memo. out[0..7] = lexer DFA states, lexer DFA edges, lexer\\n610: // context-cache entries, parser DFA states, parser DFA edges, parser\\n611: // context-cache entries, lexer ATN states with a filled next-token memo,\\n612: // parser ATN states with one. Call with no parse running.\\n613: JOLT_EXPORT int32_t jolt_parser_static_cache_stats(uint64_t* out) {\\n614:   if (!out) return -1;\\n615:   try {\\n616:     antlr4::ANTLRInputStream input(\\\"\\\");\\n617:     Python3Lexer lexer(&input);\\n618:     antlr4::CommonTokenStream tokens(&lexer);\\n619:     Python3Parser parser(&tokens);\\n620:     auto* ls = lexer.getInterpreter<antlr4::atn::LexerATNSimulator>();\\n621:     auto* ps = parser.getInterpreter<antlr4::atn::ParserATNSimulator>();\\n622:     for (int i = 0; i < 8; ++i) out[i] = 0;\\n623:     dfa_counts(ls->_decisionToDFA, out[0], out[1]);\\n624:     out[2] = ctx_size(ls->getSharedContextCache());\\n625:     dfa_counts(ps->decisionToDFA, out[3], out[4]);\\n626:     out[5] = ctx_size(ps->getSharedContextCache());\\n627:     out[6] = memo_count(lexer.getATN());\\n628:     out[7] = memo_count(parser.getATN());\\n629:     return 0;\\n630:   } catch (...) {\\n631:     return -3;\\n632:   }\\n633: }\\n634: \\n635: // TEST SEAM: a worker's own caches, out[0..5] as out[0..5] above.\\n636: JOLT_EXPORT int32_t jolt_parser_worker_cache_stats(void* worker, uint64_t* out) {\\n637:   Worker* w = as_worker(worker);\\n638:   if (!w || !out) return -1;\\n639:   for (int i = 0; i < 6; ++i) out[i] = 0;\\n640:   dfa_counts(w->lexer_dfa, out[0], out[1]);\\n641:   out[2] = ctx_size(w->lexer_ctx);\\n642:   dfa_counts(w->parser_dfa, out[3], out[4]);\\n643:   out[5] = ctx_size(w->parser_ctx);\\n644:   return 0;\\n645: }\\n646: \\n647: // TEST SEAM: the calling thread's stack. out[0..4] = stack size in bytes,\\n648: // lowest and highest stack address, the current stack position, 1 when it is\\n649: // the process's main thread.\\n650: JOLT_EXPORT int32_t jolt_parser_thread_info(uint64_t* out) {\\n651:   if (!out) return -1;\\n652:   volatile char here = 0;\\n653:   out[3] = reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(&here);\\n654: #if defined(__APPLE__)\\n655:   pthread_t self = pthread_self();\\n656:   uint64_t size = pthread_get_stacksize_np(self);\\n657:   uint64_t high = reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(pthread_get_stackaddr_np(self));\\n658:   out[0] = size;\\n659:   out[1] = high - size;\\n660:   out[2] = high;\\n661:   out[4] = pthread_main_np() == 1 ? 1 : 0;\\n662:   return 0;\\n663: #elif defined(__GLIBC__)\\n664:   pthread_attr_t attr;\\n665:   if (pthread_getattr_np(pthread_self(), &attr) != 0) return -3;\\n666:   void* low = nullptr;\\n667:   size_t size = 0;\\n668:   pthread_attr_getstack(&attr, &low, &size);\\n669:   pthread_attr_destroy(&attr);\\n670:   out[0] = size;\\n671:   out[1] = reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(low);\\n672:   out[2] = reinterpret_cast<uint64_t>(low) + size;\\n673:   out[4] = getpid() == static_cast<pid_t>(syscall(SYS_gettid)) ? 1 : 0;\\n674:   return 0;\\n675: #else\\n676:   return -3;\\n677: #endif\\n678: }\\n679: \\n680: // TEST SEAM: bytes malloc reports in use (all zones on macOS, glibc's\\n681: // mallinfo2 on Linux; 0 elsewhere).\\n682: JOLT_EXPORT uint64_t jolt_parser_heap_in_use(void) {\\n683: #if defined(__APPLE__)\\n684:   malloc_statistics_t st;\\n685:   malloc_zone_statistics(nullptr, &st);\\n686:   return st.size_in_use;\\n687: #elif defined(__GLIBC__) && (__GLIBC__ > 2 || (__GLIBC__ == 2 && __GLIBC_MINOR__ >= 33))\\n688:   return mallinfo2().uordblks;\\n689: #else\\n690:   return 0;\\n691: #endif\\n692: }\\n693: \\n694: #endif  // JOLT_PARSER_TEST_SEAMS\"}]}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"tool\",\"messageId\":\"5cf0051a-6316-4d3a-9af1-cfe7402afbac\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"C++ looks robust. Adversarial observations:\\n\\n1. Worker ownership: Worker owns DFA vector + PredictionContextCache; per-call a new simulator is installed via setInterpreter. Need to verify that LexerATNSimulator/ParserATNSimulator constructors take a DFA vector reference + ctx cache — yes, standard ANTLR C++ signatures. setInterpreter deletes the previous one (Recognizer.cpp claim). At scope exit the generated destructor deletes the interpreter — in the ANTLR C++ generated lexer/parser destructors, is it `delete _interpreter;`? Lexer's destructor: generated Python3Lexer::~Python3Lexer() { delete _interpreter; }? In the actual ANTLR C++ runtime, the Lexer base class destructor doesn't delete the interpreter; does the generated code have `~Python3Lexer() override { delete getInterpreter(); }`? Hmm. Actually, generated ANTLR C++ lexer: `Python3Lexer::~Python3Lexer() { delete _interpreter; }`? As I recall, generated lexers/parsers in C++ have destructors that delete the interpreter they created in the constructor. Right — generated code pattern:\\n\\n```cpp\\nPython3Lexer::Python3Lexer(CharStream *input) : Lexer(input) {\\n  _interpreter = new atn::LexerATNSimulator(this, _atn, _decisionToDFA, _sharedContextCache);\\n}\\nPython3Lexer::~Python3Lexer() { delete _interpreter; }\\n```\\nSo the destructor deletes whatever interpreter is installed. And setInterpreter deletes the old one. Therefore no leak/double-delete. The ASan+leaks run (50 cycles including worker new/free) backs this up empirically. Good.\\n\\n2. generated_atns(): creates a throwaway lexer/parser on each worker_new call to obtain ATN pointers — a bit heavy but fine; the ATN comes from static data initialized via call_once. Note: Python3Parser's constructor creates the default interpreter (deleted? no — the throwaway parser is destructed at return and deletes its own interpreter). OK.\\n\\n3. Hold busy guard: compare_exchange_strong; released in the destructor. Exception safety: Hold is declared before try → on return/exception the destructor runs ✓. Caveat: -5 is returned when busy; but worker_free while busy is not guarded (documented: \\\"the caller must not free while a call is running\\\"). cst.jolt's close-worker uses CAS once; but close during a running parse on another thread = UB; the single-threaded guest usage assumption is disclosed in a comment. The design states a worker is used by one thread at a time. Acceptable, documented.\\n\\n4. Worker tag check: the tag field is read after static_cast — a garbage non-null pointer would be dereferenced (UB), and if that memory happens to match the tag it would be accepted. The tag reduces risk but cannot fully prevent arbitrary-pointer dereference; inherent to opaque-handle C APIs. Zeroed memory is tested (rejected). Info-level at best.\\n\\n5. worker_free: sets tag=0 then deletes — a double free would be use-after-free anyway; tag=0 does not protect against freed memory being reused. cst.jolt's idempotent close (CAS) is the real guard. Documented. OK.\\n\\n6. SourceStream BOM fix: strictDecode throws → wrapped in IllegalArgumentException (std::exception → -2 with message). Preserves U+FEFF. Used at both entry points ✓ (export :429, parse :508). Fix is correct: decode to code points itself, completely bypassing ANTLRInputStream::load. Complete? ANTLRInputStream's _data is UTF-32? In the C++ runtime ANTLRInputStream stores std::vector<uint32_t>? Actually it stores UTF-32 code points as a UTF32Array (u32 string?). strictDecode returns vector<uint32_t> — assigned to _data, p=0. size() etc. work. Reasonable. Also invalid UTF-8 → -2 \\\"illegal byte sequence\\\" — matches report (6/6 fail-closed). The oversize-limit enforcement during growth is done via room() inside Out ✓; hand_off still rechecks. room() computes kMaxOutput - buf.size() — can buf.size() exceed kMaxOutput? No: room throws before the excess; buf.size() ≤ kMaxOutput is preserved. `n > kMaxOutput - buf.size()` is unsigned and safe since buf.size() ≤ kMaxOutput. ✓.\\n\\n7. Seams gated by #ifdef; release exports are 7 (orchestrator-verified via nm). maybe_fault/fail_handler_malloc are no-ops in release ✓. Non-allocating message() is retained ✓. Oversize catch allocates nothing ✓. Busy -5 allocates nothing ✓.\\n\\n8. export_layout_version entry = 2; cst.jolt checks it at load time (to be verified in cst.jolt).\\n\\n9. Peek idiom reading private members — test seam only, reads only; no UB concern beyond the standard explicit-instantiation trick; gated.\\n\\nNext, verification: cst.jolt changes (worker handle, close-worker, layout check), stack harness child-process approach, gc log numbers, cycles log, sanitize log, workers log, input oracle/corpus, and that the round-2 oracle is unchanged + manifest is unchanged. Additionally parity 132 PASS in the log. Spot-check via grep rather than full reads to save budget.\\n\\nMain grep:\\n- cst.jolt: worker_new/close-worker/layout-version check.\\n- r4-workers-final.log: PASS count, static-growth RECORD, busy -5.\\n- r4-stack.log or stack-budget.edn: verify the report's numbers (main parens 10752/11264, thread 544/576, unary 93.5s@1024).\\n- r4-gc.log: 200ms → 271ms, 35826ms call, tick 5237.\\n- r4-parity-final.log: SUMMARY + 132 PASS count + input section.\\n- r4-sanitize.log tail: HARNESS ok exit 0.\\n- r4-cycles-20000.log: numbers 1,304,240 → 1,416,912.\\n- manifest unchanged: digest still 2483e344, etc. (should be unchanged; grep quickly).\\n- input oracle header is JVM-generated; corpus is 13 sources.\\n\\nLet's run these in batched greps.\\n\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now spot-verify cst.jolt's worker handling and the key log numbers.\\n\\n\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_a6444ace79fe48b185d0187d\",\"name\":\"grep\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"worker|layout_version|close-worker|closed\",\"path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"-n\":true}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_e6054373c30c4fc69cd4fdbf\",\"name\":\"grep\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"10752|11264|93\\\\.5|544|576|SIGILL|SIGSEGV|unary\",\"path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/build/j0c/logs/r4-stack.log\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"-n\":true,\"head_limit\":40}}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"model\",\"createdAt\":1792508170744,\"messageId\":\"7052a16d-7e43-4e92-b02b-07911f8e3b5d\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_a6444ace79fe48b185d0187d\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\".claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:4:   (`make-worker`, `parse-unit`, `parse-transform`, `utf8-bytes`,\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:17:   A worker (§7.4) holds an opaque native handle that owns the lexer and\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:20:   `close-worker` (a jolt-only addition: the other hosts' workers are\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:21:   collected). A worker serves one thread at a time; a concurrent call on the\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:22:   same worker is refused by the wrapper (status -5) and throws here.\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:24:   Disclosed limits: the native library is the one Python3 grammar the\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:27:   qualified unavailable-parser result (J5); a worker nobody closes keeps its\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:60:(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-worker-new \\\"jolt_parser_worker_new\\\" [] :pointer)\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:61:(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-worker-free \\\"jolt_parser_worker_free\\\" [:pointer] :void)\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:62:(ffi/defcfn ^:private c-export-layout-version \\\"jolt_parser_export_layout_version\\\" [] :int)\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:202:  [worker]\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:203:  (or (some-> (::native worker) deref)\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:204:      (throw (ex-info \\\"jolt parser worker is closed\\\" {}))))\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:208:  \\\"Parse UTF-8 `source` natively with `worker` and answer the checked\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:212:  [worker source]\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:213:  (let [[status bs] (call-export (handle worker) (.getBytes ^String source \\\"UTF-8\\\"))]\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:241:(defn make-worker\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:242:  \\\"A host worker for `profile`, owning a native handle with its own DFA and\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:244:   state with another worker. Host state owned by one parser stage; it is not\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:245:   data and never crosses a stream. Dispose it with `close-worker`.\\\"\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:247:  (let [h (c-worker-new)]\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:249:      (throw (ex-info \\\"jolt parser worker could not be made\\\" {})))\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:253:(defn close-worker\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:254:  \\\"Dispose `worker`'s native handle and caches. Idempotent; a closed worker\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:256:  [worker]\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:257:  (when-let [box (::native worker)]\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:261:        (c-worker-free h))))\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:276:  \\\"Parse one sealed unit's `source` with `worker`; return its CST packet.\\\"\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:277:  [worker unit source]\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:280:        records (export-records worker source)]\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:281:    (export/result (:profile worker) unit\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:288:  [worker]\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:289:  (packet/transform parse-unit worker))\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:308:  [worker source]\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/src/jolt/yang/antlr/cst.jolt:309:  (let [{:keys [failure tokens]} (export-records worker source)\"}]},{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_e6054373c30c4fc69cd4fdbf\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\".claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/build/j0c/logs/r4-stack.log:1:{:fails 11264, :fail-errs [], :fresh-full-at-passes {:ok \\\"ok\\\", :ms 2124}, :fail-exit 139, :passes 10752, :main-thread true, :bytes-per-level 890, :thread \\\"main\\\", :fail-stderr \\\"\\\", :shape \\\"parens\\\", :stack-bytes 10027008}\\n.claude/worktrees/jolt-j0c/build/j0c/logs/r4-stack.log:2:{:fails 576, :fail-errs [], :fresh-full-at-passes {:ok \\\"ok\\\", :ms 102}, :fail-exit 132, :passes 544, :main-thread false, :bytes-per-level 931, :thread \\\"thread\\\", :fail-stderr \\\"\\\", :shape \\\"parens\\\", :stack-bytes 536576}\\n.claude/worktrees/jol