 denied in plan mode). The change is UNCOMMITTED in the worktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0 (branch host-h0, base eacaed90): new src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj, src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj, test/dao/host/gate_test.clj, docs/design/host-boundary/closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn, docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn. Spec: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md (r6; the H0 row in section 8, sections 3.1-3.3, 8.1 list 1, 8.3). Author report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792518355000-engineer-host-boundary-h0.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md. The orchestrator re-ran in the worktree: clojure -M:test -n dao.host.gate-test rc 0 (10 tests, 65 assertions, 0 failures); host-boundary.closure --check rc 0 (clj 142 / cljs 140 / cljd 141 files, shared 133); corpus_hashes.clj --check rc 0 (18 files identical). The opus author ran the three quick-tier lanes (JVM 4121->4131 tests, +65 assertions; Node 4112; Dart 4060, all passing); the orchestrator did not re-run the full lanes.\\nCheck: (a) the closure tool: is the traversal faithful to the design (lane features, resolution order src/<lane> before src/cljc, :as-alias and string libspecs not dependencies); is the independent second traversal REALLY independent (shares no code with tools.namespace) and does the agreement claim hold; could the tool silently under-include (the author's own predecessor script dropped requires inside #?@ arms: check that the new tool handles them); (b) the gate test: do the two negative tests really fail the gate for the right reason (an injected #?(:clj outside list 1; an injected (random-uuid) outside list 2), done IN MEMORY without editing real source; does zero-files / unreadable-file give a scan-failure distinct from a pass; are the exemptions of 3.3 applied by reading forms and not by text; is list 1 / list 2 construction honest: the author recorded 16 closure files with real host arms that 8.1 does not name as :h0-unlisted on list 1 so the gate passes; is that an acceptable H0 behaviour or does it weaken the freeze; (c) corpus hashes: 18 files, regeneration command, a JVM test that asserts each digest; (d) the author reports four mismatches between the design and the measured closure (F1 list 1 vs 8.1; F2 random-uuid 21 in the closure vs the 26 the design says, the other five in dao/await.cljc and yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve.cljc which no file in src requires; F3 namespaces in the 3.1 table rows that are not in the closure; F4 main.cljc 13 resolved print calls not 19, antlr/repl.cljc:71 is inside a quoted yin program): verify two of them against the code (e.g. grep the random-uuid sites and the requirers of dao.await) and say whether the author reported them honestly rather than adjusting the tool to fit; (e) scope: nothing under src/ other than src/dev/host_boundary changed, no codec-track or jolt file touched, no design doc edited, deps.edn and bb.edn unchanged (the tool runs via an inline -Sdeps alias: acceptable?). Under 700 words, final response only, header fields, verdict SIGNED OFF / SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES / NOT SIGNED OFF, findings table (id, severity, file:line, evidence, correction), and what you could not verify.\"}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"user\",\"createdAt\":1792522579829,\"messageId\":\"47fe4434-6663-423c-83ab-09cc5ed32beb\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"This is a pretty large-scale review. Files to read:\\n\\n1. Report: collab/1792518355000-engineer-host-boundary-h0.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md\\n2. Spec: docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md — the H0 row in §8, 3.1–3.3, list 1 of 8.1, 8.3. Need to locate the sections.\\n3. src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj\\n4. src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj\\n5. test/dao/host/gate_test.clj\\n6. Closure output (just spot-check)\\n7. F2 verification: grep for random-uuid within src/cljc etc., and grep for the require source of dao.await.\\n\\nFirst, let's kick off the report and the spec headings in parallel.\\n\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I'll read the author report and locate the spec sections first.\\n\\n\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_0155ddd060614844bed79c2b\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792518355000-engineer-host-boundary-h0.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md\"}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_f11e6d647dbc436b86073d18\",\"name\":\"grep\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"^#{1,3} \",\"path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"-n\":true}}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"model\",\"createdAt\":1792522616367,\"messageId\":\"a29dc805-1e71-4fc9-82ae-bc2049238879\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_0155ddd060614844bed79c2b\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 1/1 file, 447 lines\\n1: Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 18:15:00 GMT\\n2: Created-Local: 2026-10-21 01:15:00 +07\\n3: Coding-Agent: claude\\n4: Model: claude-opus-5-5\\n5: Role: QA & Verification engineer (H0 freeze: tooling and tests, no behaviour change)\\n6: Prompt: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792518355000-engineer-host-boundary-h0.claude-opus-5-5.prompt.md\\n7: Design: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md (r6; §2, §3.1-3.3, §8 H0, §8.1, §8.3, §12-14)\\n8: Worktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0 (branch host-h0, base eacaed90 = local master with codec C0/C1)\\n9: Status: DONE, nothing staged, committed or pushed. One H0 finding must be resolved before H1: list 1 differs from the §8.1 baseline (F1 below).\\n10: \\n11: # Host-boundary H0: the freeze\\n12: \\n13: ## Summary\\n14: \\n15: - **No `src/` behaviour change.** Seven new files, all untracked (listed\\n16:   below). No file under `src/cljc`, `src/clj`, `src/cljs` or `src/cljd` was\\n17:   touched. No codec-track file, no `dao.stream.*` source, no jolt file and\\n18:   no design doc was touched.\\n19: - **(a) Closure totals match exactly**: clj **142**, cljs **140**, cljd\\n20:   **141**, shared **133**. The lane-specific lists are file-for-file the\\n21:   §3.1 table (9 / 7 / 8). An independent second traversal agrees on every\\n22:   file of every lane.\\n23: - **(b) The gate passes on the current tree** (155 files scanned, 0 errors,\\n24:   0 violations). Each negative test fails the gate for exactly the injected\\n25:   reason and nothing else. Reading zero files, or failing to read one, gives\\n26:   `:scan-failure`, not `:pass`.\\n27: - **(c) Counts**: the per-lane table is below. JVM goes from 4121 tests to\\n28:   4131, which is +10, the new `dao.host.gate-test`. Node and Dart are\\n29:   unchanged.\\n30: - **(d) Corpus hash set**: 18 files, SHA-256, in\\n31:   `docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn`, with a regenerate/check\\n32:   script and a JVM test that asserts the bytes.\\n33: - **Findings** (F1-F4) are differences between the design text and the\\n34:   tree. They are recorded, not massaged.\\n35: \\n36: ## Files created (absolute paths; all untracked in the worktree)\\n37: \\n38: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj`: the closure tool (ns `host-boundary.closure`).\\n39: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj`: the corpus hash set generator/checker (babashka).\\n40: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/docs/design/host-boundary/closure-clj.edn`\\n41: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/docs/design/host-boundary/closure-cljs.edn`\\n42: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/docs/design/host-boundary/closure-cljd.edn`\\n43: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn`\\n44: - `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/test/dao/host/gate_test.clj`: ns `dao.host.gate-test`, 10 deftests.\\n45: \\n46: Files changed: none.\\n47: \\n48: Scratch files live under `target/h0/` (gitignored): lane logs, probes and\\n49: `gate-evidence.txt`. They are not deliverables.\\n50: \\n51: ### Location of the tool: `src/dev/`, not `dev/` (justified deviation)\\n52: \\n53: §8 names `dev/host_boundary/closure.clj`. The repo has no top-level `dev/`\\n54: directory. Every dev tool lives in `src/dev/`: `affected.clj`,\\n55: `dep_graph.clj`, `cljd_agg.clj`, `tasks.clj` and `yang_antlr_gen.clj`.\\n56: `deps.edn` puts `src/dev` on the classpath of `:dev`, `:fmt`, `:clean`,\\n57: `:antlr-gen`, `:dep-graph` and `:cljs`. The closest precedent is\\n58: `dep_graph.clj`, which also uses `clojure.tools.namespace.parse`; its\\n59: `:dep-graph` alias adds tools.namespace 1.5.0. A top-level `dev/` would be\\n60: on no alias.\\n61: \\n62: I added no alias, because a `deps.edn` change is a \\\"wide\\\" change for\\n63: `bb test:changed`. The tool therefore runs with an inline alias:\\n64: \\n65: ```sh\\n66: clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:hb {:extra-paths [\\\"src/dev\\\"] :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace {:mvn/version \\\"1.5.0\\\"}}}}}' \\\\\\n67:   -M:hb -m host-boundary.closure [--check]\\n68: ```\\n69: \\n70: The same command is in the ns docstring. Consequence: `src/dev/` is in\\n71: `affected.clj`'s wide prefixes, so `bb test:changed` on this branch exits 2\\n72: (wide) and asks for `bb test`. If the orchestrator prefers the design's\\n73: literal path, moving the two files to `dev/host_boundary/` and changing\\n74: the `-Sdeps` path is mechanical. The gate test does not depend on the\\n75: tool's location.\\n76: \\n77: ## (a) Closure tool and output\\n78: \\n79: Method, as §3.1 states it:\\n80: \\n81: - The traversal starts at `yin.repl.main`.\\n82: - `clojure.tools.namespace.parse/read-ns-decl` reads the ns form with the\\n83:   lane's features: `:clj #{:clj}`, `:cljs #{:cljs}`, `:cljd #{:cljd :clj}`.\\n84:   The first matching arm wins, as in tools.reader.\\n85: - `deps-from-ns-decl` collects the `:require`, `:use` and `:require-macros`\\n86:   clauses.\\n87: - A namespace resolves to `src/<lane>/<path>.<lane>` first, then to\\n88:   `src/cljc/<path>.cljc`. A namespace with neither file (core, a library)\\n89:   is outside the closure.\\n90: \\n91: One adaptation was needed: `#?(:cljd nil :clj [...])` reads as `nil` on\\n92: cljd, and `deps-from-ns-decl` throws \\\"Unparsable namespace form\\\" on a nil\\n93: libspec. `strip-nils` drops it, which matches what the compilers do.\\n94: \\n95: Output is deterministic and has no timestamp. `--check` exits 1 if a\\n96: committed file is stale; I ran it and it exited 0.\\n97: \\n98: ```\\n99: clj   total 142 shared 133 lane-specific 9\\n100: cljs  total 140 shared 133 lane-specific 7\\n101: cljd  total 141 shared 133 lane-specific 8\\n102: shared (all three lanes): 133\\n103: ```\\n104: \\n105: Lane-specific files, identical to the §3.1 table:\\n106: \\n107: - **clj**: `clj/dao/jing/content/driver.clj`, `clj/dao/stream/datagram/jvm.clj`,\\n108:   `clj/dao/stream/waitset/driver.clj`, `clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj`,\\n109:   `clj/yang/antlr/cst.clj`, `clj/yin/repl/host/jvm.clj`,\\n110:   `cljc/yin/repl/host.cljc`, `cljc/dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`,\\n111:   `cljc/dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc`.\\n112: - **cljs**: `cljs/dao/stream/datagram/node.cljs`, `cljs/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljs`,\\n113:   `cljs/dao/stream/ws/node.cljs`, `cljs/yang/antlr/cst.cljs`,\\n114:   `cljs/yin/repl/host.cljs`, and the two `boring.cljc`.\\n115: - **cljd**: `cljd/dao/stream/cbor/cljd.cljd`, `cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd`,\\n116:   `cljd/dao/stream/datagram/dart.cljd`, `cljd/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljd`,\\n117:   `cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd`, `cljd/yang/antlr/cst.cljd`,\\n118:   `cljd/yin/repl/host.cljd`, `cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`.\\n119: \\n120: **Class tags.** Each file entry has the shape\\n121: `{:file :ns :shared :classes #{...}}`. `:classes` is a set because the\\n122: §3.1 table puts some namespaces in several rows. For example,\\n123: `yin.vm.values` is both `:profile-internal-pure` and `:consumer`, and\\n124: `yin.repl` is both `:driver` and `:deferred-entropy`. A file with no host\\n125: contact beyond §3.3 syntax is tagged `:none`, which makes \\\"the remaining\\n126: files\\\" checkable. Each lane file carries a class legend that gives each\\n127: class's slice. Three tagging choices go beyond the table and are marked in\\n128: the source:\\n129: \\n130: - `:codec-track` also covers the §8.3 codec files (`ws`, `remote-channel`,\\n131:   `ws-project`, `jing.stream`, `dao.data`, the ws adapters,\\n132:   `yin.repl.serve` and `yin.repl.connect`).\\n133: - `yang.python.antlr.*` is tagged `:deferred-stage`, by prefix.\\n134: - The three `dao.stream.waitset.driver` files are tagged\\n135:   `:external-stream-seam` (see F3).\\n136: \\n137: ### Independent second traversal (agreement)\\n138: \\n139: Traversal B is in `dao.host.gate-test` (`traverse`, `select-arms`,\\n140: `libspec-deps`, `ns-deps`) and shares no code with tools.namespace. It\\n141: works differently:\\n142: \\n143: - It reads every form with tools.reader in `:read-cond :preserve` mode.\\n144: - It selects arms itself, splicing `#?@` arms. This is the r3 script's\\n145:   defect class, which under-counted 141/140/139.\\n146: - It parses libspecs itself.\\n147: \\n148: Only the §3.1 resolution rule is shared, because the design fixes it.\\n149: Result, also asserted by the test\\n150: `independent-traversal-agrees-with-the-committed-closure`:\\n151: \\n152: ```\\n153: traversal B :clj 142 committed 142 equal? true\\n154: traversal B :cljs 140 committed 140 equal? true\\n155: traversal B :cljd 141 committed 141 equal? true\\n156: ```\\n157: \\n158: The sets are equal file by file, not just in count. They also agree with\\n159: astra's r3 reviewer totals in the design (142/140/141/133).\\n160: \\n161: ## (b) The gate test `dao.host.gate-test`\\n162: \\n163: **Lane.** `test/dao/host/gate_test.clj` runs on the JVM lane only. The\\n164: gate checks source text, which is the same on every lane, and §8.2 has it\\n165: read files \\\"with the Clojure reader per lane feature\\\". `:preserve` reads\\n166: all arms of all lanes in one pass. The Node runner and the Dart aggregator\\n167: do not compile `.clj` files (`cljd_agg.clj:42` matches `_test.clj[cd]`),\\n168: so the Node and Dart counts are unaffected.\\n169: \\n170: **Input.** The input is the union of the three committed closure files:\\n171: 155 distinct files (133 shared, plus 9 + 7 + 8 lane-specific, minus the\\n172: two `boring.cljc` files shared by clj and cljs).\\n173: \\n174: **Host arms.** For every reader conditional, with every lane's arms\\n175: walked:\\n176: \\n177: - A conditional is exempt by a §3.3 pattern if it is:\\n178:   - inside the `ns` form (require arms);\\n179:   - a catch-type position (`(catch #?(...) e ...)`);\\n180:   - all arms equal under `=` (hint-only, e.g. `#?(:clj ^long n :cljs n)`);\\n181:   - a splicing protocol block that is a direct child of\\n182:     `deftype`/`defrecord`/`reify`/`extend-type`/`extend-protocol`/`specify`;\\n183:   - a `print-method` defmethod;\\n184:   - `exists?`;\\n185:   - `(Object.)`/`(js-obj)` sentinels.\\n186: - `(comment ...)` is skipped.\\n187: - Every other conditional is a host arm.\\n188: - A lane-specific `.clj`/`.cljs`/`.cljd` file counts as one host arm in\\n189:   its entirety. `.clj` files cannot hold `#?` at all, and §8.1 lists every\\n190:   lane file.\\n191: - Observed exemption counts over the closure: catch-type 174, ns 49,\\n192:   hint-only 35, sentinel 10, protocol-block 8.\\n193: \\n194: **Effect calls (list 2).** The kinds are the §3.2 categories:\\n195: \\n196: - `:random-uuid`;\\n197: - `:rand` (`rand`, `rand-int`, `rand-nth`, `shuffle`, `random-sample`);\\n198: - `:secure-random` (`SecureRandom`, `Random.secure`, `randomUUID`,\\n199:   `js/crypto*`, `getRandomValues`, `randomBytes`, `generateKey`);\\n200: - `:gensym`;\\n201: - `:clock` (`System/currentTimeMillis`/`nanoTime`, `js/Date*`,\\n202:   `js/performance*`, `DateTime.now*`, `Instant/now`);\\n203: - `:ambient` (`System/getenv`/`getProperty`, `js/process*`, `Platform.*`);\\n204: - `:print` (`println`, `print`, `prn`, `pr`, `printf`, `newline`,\\n205:   `js/console*`);\\n206: - `:timer` (`js/setTimeout`/`setInterval`/`setImmediate`/`queueMicrotask`,\\n207:   `Timer*`, `Thread/sleep`, `Future.delayed*`);\\n208: - `:m-entry`: a symbol that resolves through the file's ns aliases or\\n209:   refers to `dao.data.arrays` or `dao.host.bytes`, named `aset`, `acopy`,\\n210:   `asort`, `set!` or `copy!`.\\n211: \\n212: Calls are resolved lexically:\\n213: \\n214: - A symbol bound by `let`/`loop`/`for`/`doseq`/`when-let`/... , by fn,\\n215:   defn or defmethod params, by `letfn`, by `catch`, or by deftype fields\\n216:   and method params is a local, not the core function.\\n217: - So is a name the file defines or `declare`s, or excludes with\\n218:   `:refer-clojure`.\\n219: - Quoted forms and `comment` are data.\\n220: \\n221: This removes three false positives a name match would give.\\n222: `yin/vm/engine.cljc` declares its own `gensym`, `yin/vm/macro.cljc` binds\\n223: a param named `gensym`, and `yin/vm/linker/authority.cljc:366-369` binds a\\n224: local named `pr`.\\n225: \\n226: List 2 is `{file {kind ceiling}}`. One more call of a kind in a file\\n227: fails the gate.\\n228: \\n229: **Verdict.** The verdict is `:pass`, `:fail` or `:scan-failure`.\\n230: `:scan-failure` means zero files were read, or a file could not be read or\\n231: parsed. It is distinct from a pass with zero matches.\\n232: \\n233: Evidence, from `target/h0/gate-evidence.txt`, produced by loading the\\n234: test ns and printing the gate's results:\\n235: \\n236: ```\\n237: CURRENT TREE verdict :pass scanned 155 errors [] arm-violations [] effect-violations []\\n238: files with non-exempt arms 76 of which lane-specific 19\\n239: files with effect calls 32\\n240: NEG1 target src/cljc/dao/data.cljc verdict :fail arm-violations [{:file src/cljc/dao/data.cljc, :lines [130]}] effect-violations []\\n241: NEG2 target src/cljc/dao/data.cljc verdict :fail arm-violations [] effect-violations [{:file src/cljc/dao/data.cljc, :kind :random-uuid, :count 1, :allowed 0, :lines [130]}]\\n242: EMPTY verdict :scan-failure scanned 0\\n243: by category {:h0-unlisted 16, :deferred-scope 15, :migration-source 15, :seam-driver 21, :profile 1, :codec-track 5, :runtime-prereq 3}\\n244: effects by kind {:secure-random 6, :timer 5, :rand 4, :print 13, :gensym 4, :m-entry 33, :ambient 13, :clock 10, :random-uuid 21}\\n245: ```\\n246: \\n247: (After that run, the unreadable-file case was changed to report \\\"cannot\\n248: read file\\\" instead of a tools.reader protocol error. The test asserts\\n249: `:scan-failure` and names the file.)\\n250: \\n251: The negative tests are in memory: the gate takes `{file text}`. The\\n252: target file is chosen programmatically: the first closure `.cljc` file\\n253: outside the list with no arms and no effect calls, which is\\n254: `src/cljc/dao/data.cljc`. Text is appended to its in-memory copy only. No\\n255: real source is edited.\\n256: \\n257: - **NEG1** appends `(def injected #?(:clj (java.lang.Math/abs -1) :cljs 1))`.\\n258:   The verdict is `:fail`, with exactly one arm violation (that file) and\\n259:   zero effect violations.\\n260: - **NEG2** appends `(def injected (random-uuid))`. The verdict is `:fail`,\\n261:   with exactly one effect violation (`:random-uuid`, count 1, allowed 0)\\n262:   and zero arm violations.\\n263: \\n264: Each test asserts that exact violation list, so it fails for the right\\n265: reason and only that reason.\\n266: \\n267: The 10 deftests are:\\n268: \\n269: - `closure-totals-are-the-design-totals`\\n270: - `independent-traversal-agrees-with-the-committed-closure`\\n271: - `gate-passes-on-the-current-tree`\\n272: - `list-1-equals-the-observed-arms` (no stale or missing list-1 entry)\\n273: - `list-2-equals-the-observed-calls` (no slack in any ceiling)\\n274: - `an-injected-host-arm-outside-list-1-fails-the-gate`\\n275: - `an-injected-random-uuid-outside-list-2-fails-the-gate`\\n276: - `a-scan-failure-is-not-a-pass` (empty input, and an unreadable file)\\n277: - `corpus-bytes-match-the-frozen-hash-set`\\n278: - `exemptions-and-resolution` (unit checks of the §3.3 patterns and the\\n279:   lexical resolution)\\n280: \\n281: Run alone: `clojure -M:test -n dao.host.gate-test` gives\\n282: `Ran 10 tests containing 65 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.`\\n283: clj-kondo reports 0 errors and 0 warnings; cljstyle check is clean.\\n284: \\n285: Library mode (§8.2) was **not** built. It belongs to H2.\\n286: \\n287: ### List 1 as generated (76 files) vs the §8.1 baseline: finding F1\\n288: \\n289: List 1 in the test is the observed set, by §8.1 category: migration\\n290: sources 15, profile 1, runtime prerequisites 3, codec track 5, seams and\\n291: driver 21, deferred scope 15. That is 60 files, matching §8.1's existing\\n292: files after the corrections below. It also holds **16 `:h0-unlisted`\\n293: files**: real, non-exempt host arms in closure files that §8.1 does not\\n294: name. Each one is commented with its line in the test:\\n295: \\n296: | File | Site | Arm |\\n297: |---|---|---|\\n298: | `dao/space/index.cljc` | :78 | `instance? Long/Double`, `js/isNaN`, `dart/is?` |\\n299: | `dao/space/query.cljc` | :808 | runtime type name |\\n300: | `dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc` | :168 | host atom type |\\n301: | `dao/stream/rpc.cljc` | :114 | `rand` (§9.1 entropy) |\\n302: | `yang/antlr/packet.cljc` | :67 | code points |\\n303: | `yang/clojure.cljc` | :375 | runtime type name |\\n304: | `yang/php.cljc` | :95, :98 | `Double/parseDouble`, `js/parseFloat`, `int/parse` |\\n305: | `yin/repl/adapter.cljc` | :58 | edn reader |\\n306: | `yin/repl/dht.cljc` | :104 | edn reader |\\n307: | `yin/repl/query.cljc` | :460 | byte length |\\n308: | `yin/vm.cljc` | :404 | `bytes->str`: `String.` / `fromCharCode` / `String.fromCharCodes` |\\n309: | `yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc` | :439 | `js/Number.isSafeInteger` |\\n310: | `yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc` | :130 | `js/Number.isSafeInteger` |\\n311: | `yin/vm/engine.cljc` | :929 | runtime type name |\\n312: | `yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc` | :32 | byte length |\\n313: | `yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc` | :282 | byte length |\\n314: \\n315: In the other direction, §8.1 names files that are **not** on the generated\\n316: list 1:\\n317: \\n318: - Outside the adopted closure (required by no `src` file):\\n319:   `dao/jing/content/async.cljc`, `dao/stream/udp.cljc`,\\n320:   `dao/space/schema.cljc` and `dao/jing/stream.cljc`.\\n321: - In the closure, but every arm is catch-type and exempt:\\n322:   `dao/stream/remote_channel.cljc:399,440,920` and\\n323:   `dao/stream/ws_project.cljc:376,435`.\\n324: \\n325: §8.1 says a difference either way is an H0 finding to resolve before H1.\\n326: The Architect has to decide the following:\\n327: \\n328: - (i) Do the 16 files get §8.1 categories? Several look like H1/H2 profile\\n329:   material: byte length, `bytes->str`, number parsing, safe-integer.\\n330:   Others look like dialect semantics: the runtime type name in error text,\\n331:   and the edn reader.\\n332: - (ii) Should §8.1 drop the six names that are absent or exempt-only?\\n333: \\n334: Until then, the 16 sit on list 1 tagged `:h0-unlisted`, so the gate passes\\n335: on today's tree and still catches any new arm.\\n336: \\n337: ## Other findings (design text vs tree; R claims checked, nothing massaged)\\n338: \\n339: - **F2. §3.2 random-uuid: 21 in the closure, not 26.** `dao/await.cljc:235,240`\\n340:   and `yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve.cljc:417,604,606` exist and do call\\n341:   `random-uuid`, but no `src` file requires `dao.await` or\\n342:   `yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve`, so both are outside the adopted closure.\\n343:   26 - 5 = 21. The other 19 §3.2 lines match exactly.\\n344: - **F3. §3.1 rows that name namespaces outside the closure:**\\n345:   `dao.stream.udp`, `dao.stream.ws.browser` (expected: the browser is not\\n346:   a lane), `dao.await`, `yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve`, `dao.jing.content.async`\\n347:   and `dao.space.schema`. The reverse case: the `dao.stream.waitset.driver`\\n348:   files (`setTimeout`/`Timer`) are in §3.1's lane-specific list but in no\\n349:   class row. I tagged them `:external-stream-seam`, following §8.1's\\n350:   \\\"Seams and driver\\\" row.\\n351: - **F4. §3.2 sites the resolved scan sees differently:**\\n352:   - **Printing.** `yin/repl/main.cljc` has **13** resolved print calls\\n353:     (`println`/`print`/`prn`/`pr`/`printf`/`newline`/`js/console*`), not\\n354:     19. §3.2 does not say what its 19 counted, so this is unreconciled (R).\\n355:     `yang/python/antlr/repl.cljc:71` is `println` inside a quoted yin\\n356:     program (`'(let ...)`, `run-form`), so it is the yin VM's primitive,\\n357:     not a host call. The gate does not count it.\\n358:   - **Timers.** `btree/storage.cljc:224-227` is a promise facade\\n359:     (`CompletableFuture`/`Completer`/`js/Promise.`), which is not a timer.\\n360:     It is on list 1 as runtime prereq or deferred. `main.cljc:1321,1343`\\n361:     construct `Thread.`s, which is also not a timer kind. Timer calls the\\n362:     gate does see: `driver.clj:173`, `datagram/jvm.clj:70`, and the\\n363:     waitset drivers.\\n364:   - **Clocks.** Besides `main.cljc` (5 lines: 1242, 1275, 1408, 1435, 1542)\\n365:     and `driver.clj:169,206`, the ws seams also read clocks:\\n366:     `ws/jvm.clj:422`, `ws/node.cljs:249` and `ws/dart.cljd:176`. §3.1\\n367:     mentions these; §3.2 does not list them.\\n368:   - **Secure-random.** `sign.cljc:79` is `jvm-pair`'s seed-replay\\n369:     `SecureRandom` proxy. §2.5 rules it deterministic and internal, but it\\n370:     matches by name, so it is in list 2's ceiling for `sign.cljc` with a\\n371:     comment.\\n372:   - **M-entry callers (§2.4).** Only `dao.data.btree` resolves today, with\\n373:     33 calls through `dao.data.arrays`. `chunks`, `cbor` and `sign` mutate\\n374:     host arrays directly inside arms (`System/arraycopy`, `.setRange`,\\n375:     `.set`) and call no M entry yet; `bytes/set!`/`copy!` do not exist\\n376:     until H1. After H2 migrates them, list 2 must gain them as `:m-entry`\\n377:     callers. That is the §2.4 (iv) audit point.\\n378: \\n379: ## (c) Per-lane counts (quick tier, one lane at a time, CMAKE_BUILD_PARALLEL_LEVEL=4)\\n380: \\n381: The Dart peer (`bb build:yin-repl-peer`) was built first, so the JVM lane\\n382: ran the Dart-peer tests.\\n383: \\n384: | Lane | Before (base eacaed90) | After (H0) | Delta |\\n385: |---|---|---|---|\\n386: | JVM `bb test:clj` | 4121 tests, 286038 assertions, 0 fail, 0 err | 4131 tests, 286103 assertions, 0 fail, 0 err | +10 tests, +65 assertions: exactly `dao.host.gate-test` (10 deftests, 65 assertions run alone) |\\n387: | Node `bb test:cljs` | 4112 tests, 150444 assertions, 0 fail, 0 err | same run (see below) | 0 |\\n388: | Dart `bb test:cljd` | 4060 tests, \\\"All tests passed!\\\" (flutter prints no assertion count) | same run (see below) | 0 |\\n389: \\n390: Logs: `target/h0/{clj-before,clj-after,cljs-before,cljd-before}.log`.\\n391: \\n392: **How each run relates to the tree.**\\n393: \\n394: - The JVM \\\"before\\\" run started on the clean base, before any new file\\n395:   existed. Its log does not mention `dao.host.gate-test`.\\n396: - The Node and Dart runs started after all seven files existed. Neither\\n397:   lane compiles any of them: shadow's `:node-test` only takes cljs/cljc\\n398:   sources, and `cljd_agg.clj:42` only takes `_test.clj[cd]`. Neither log\\n399:   mentions `dao.host.gate-test`, and no file they compile differs from eacaed90.\\n400:   So each of those runs is both the before and the after measurement.\\n401:   I did not run them a second time, because the second run would have the\\n402:   same input (about 25 minutes for Node and 7 for Dart on this laptop).\\n403:   If the orchestrator wants a literal second run, it is\\n404:   `bb test:cljs` / `bb test:cljd` in the worktree.\\n405: - The first Node attempt was killed at the tool's 20-minute background\\n406:   limit while running alongside my JVM probes. I reran it alone, and that\\n407:   rerun's counts are the ones above.\\n408: \\n409: ## (d) Corpus hash set\\n410: \\n411: `docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn`: SHA-256 of all **18**\\n412: files under `test/resources/dao/jing/` (6) and `test/fixtures/codec/` (12).\\n413: \\n414: - `test/resources/dao/jing/` holds `cbor-v1.json`, `cbor-v1.errata.md`,\\n415:   `cbor-v1.README.md`, `cbor-v1.generate.py`, `digest-table.edn` and\\n416:   `blake3-vectors.edn`.\\n417: - `test/fixtures/codec/` holds `{cbor,transit}/{descriptors,envelopes,exceptions,jing,negotiation,rejections}.edn`.\\n418: \\n419: To regenerate or check, run `bb src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj [--check]`.\\n420: `--check` exits 1 and lists the differing files. Two spot checks against\\n421: `shasum -a 256` agree (`cbor/jing.edn` 27aac4fb…, `cbor-v1.json`\\n422: 831a1d31…). `corpus-bytes-match-the-frozen-hash-set` in the gate test\\n423: asserts both the file set and every digest on the JVM lane.\\n424: \\n425: SHA-256 was chosen because the prompt names it, `shasum` is on every host,\\n426: and these are tooling checksums, not system identities. If the owner's\\n427: BLAKE3-everywhere rule should cover tooling checksums too, switching is a\\n428: one-function change.\\n429: \\n430: Other goldens that §8 H4 and Appendix A mention are **not** in the set,\\n431: because the prompt scoped (d) to the two trees: `sign_vectors.edn`,\\n432: `integer_v3_fixtures.cljc`, `int-contract-v1.txt`, and the DHT and linker\\n433: image goldens. Adding their paths to `roots` would include them.\\n434: \\n435: ## Not done (by scope)\\n436: \\n437: - Nothing from H1 onward: no `dao.host.*` source, no library mode of the\\n438:   gate (§8.2, H2), no consumer changes.\\n439: - No commit, stage or push. No change to `deps.edn` or `bb.edn` (no alias\\n440:   or bb task for the tool; see the location note).\\n441: - F1 is not resolved. That is the Architect's decision before H1.\\n442: - `bb test:changed` was not run. Because of `src/dev/`, it would report a\\n443:   wide change (exit 2). The quick-tier lanes above stand in for it.\\n444: - Slow tier: not run (H0 is not a phase boundary; the design runs the slow\\n445:   tier once after H4).\\n446: \\n447: Report: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1792518355000-engineer-host-boundary-h0.claude-opus-5-5.findings.md\"}]},{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_f11e6d647dbc436b86073d18\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1:# dao.stream.host-boundary: dao.stream wherever the boundary can be an IO action\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:76:## 1. Problem\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:134:## 2. The governing rule\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:136:### 2.1 The boundary, defined first (review R1)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:150:### 2.2 Statement\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:161:### 2.3 \\\"Can be an IO action\\\", operationally\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:202:### 2.4 Ownership and mutation laws for the profile\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:266:### 2.5 Borderline cases, decided\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:305:### 2.6 Where the owner's original sentence is and is not met\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:314:## 3. Classification over the adopted closure\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:316:### 3.1 The transitive closure, per lane (R, computed)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:417:### 3.2 Resolved effect calls, corrected (V)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:438:### 3.3 Exempt dialect syntax\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:445:## 4. The host-implementation contract\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:447:### 4.1 Stream implementations and their seams (external contact)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:481:### 4.2 The primitive profile: exact manifest (P)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:573:### 4.3 Oracle coverage matrix (table D)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:642:### 4.4 The driver\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:648:### 4.5 Relation to the conformance kit and the wasm surface\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:655:## 5. What porting a host consists of (after H0-H4)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:667:## 6. Verifiability\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:677:## 7. Consequence for wasm\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:685:## 8. Slices H0-H4 (commissionable)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:754:### 8.1 List 1: the files permitted non-exempt host arms, baseline and final\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:813:### 8.2 The host-library gate (H2, H3): executable references within the closure\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:838:### 8.3 File-disjointness from the codec track, including tests (re-checked, V)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:873:## 9. DEFERRED scope (not commissionable under this document)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:882:### 9.1 Entropy, identities, scheduling, ambient facts, printing (reserved H5)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:915:### 9.2 The durable-storage seam (reserved H6)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:929:### 9.3 The parser stage (reserved H7)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:935:### 9.4 Stream-implementation conformance and the wasm import gate (reserved H8)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:942:## 10. Cost and what would reverse this (H0-H4)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:975:## 11. Decision record\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:999:### 11.1 Owner decisions recorded (2026-10-20)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1024:## 12. OWNER PROPOSAL: amendment to datom.world.abi.md (not doctrine; not applied)\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1072:## 13. Open owner decisions\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1088:## 14. For a successor orchestrator\\ndocs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md:1134:## Appendix A. Citations opened for this document (2026-10-20, read only)\"}]}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"tool\",\"messageId\":\"3edf9b74-ee97-42e3-8f23-562bb5bf44bd\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Now, let me read each section of the spec: 3.1-3.3 (lines 314-445), the H0 row in §8 (lines 685-754), 8.1 (lines 754-813), 8.3 (lines 838-873). After that, the tool + gate test + corpus hash. It's a lot in terms of volume, but let me read spec 314-445 and 685-873.\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_d00b20dcc946455fb9407b0e\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md\",\"offset\":314,\"limit\":131}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_9b248d06fc734c758d06c85e\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md\",\"offset\":685,\"limit\":188}}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"model\",\"createdAt\":1792522631941,\"messageId\":\"2a2dcf3a-c9f0-48af-b841-6a13b84d9c6d\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_d00b20dcc946455fb9407b0e\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 1/1 file, 131 lines\\nNote: showing lines 314-444. More of the file remains. Use offset=445 to continue.\\n314: ## 3. Classification over the adopted closure\\n315: \\n316: ### 3.1 The transitive closure, per lane (R, computed)\\n317: \\n318: Method: a require-form traversal from `yin.repl.main`, choosing each lane's\\n319: reader arms (`:cljd` also reads `:clj`) and resolving each namespace to its\\n320: file under `src/<lane>` first (shadow resolution: `yin.repl.host` is\\n321: `host.cljc` on the JVM and the `host.cljs`/`host.cljd` shadows elsewhere),\\n322: then `src/cljc`. It is not a compiler-resolved call graph: it can\\n323: over-include a namespace required but unused on a path, cannot see dynamic\\n324: loading, and **can under-include** when its reader-arm parsing fails; the\\n325: r3 script did exactly that (it dropped requires inside `#?@` arms and\\n326: reported 141/140/139). The r3 claim that it \\\"cannot under-include\\\" is\\n327: withdrawn. The reconciled totals, counted by **file** and confirmed by the\\n328: r3 reviewer's independent traversal (R):\\n329: \\n330: +-------+-------+----------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n331: | Lane  | Total | Shared   | Lane-specific files (V, the files exist)                                                                            |\\n332: +=======+=======+==========+=====================================================================================================================+\\n333: | clj   | 142   | 133      | `clj/dao/jing/content/driver.clj` (blocking driver: clock, sleep, `locking`), `clj/dao/stream/datagram/jvm.clj`,    |\\n334: |       |       |          | `clj/dao/stream/waitset/driver.clj`, `clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj` (clock, `CompletableFuture`), `clj/yang/antlr/     |\\n335: |       |       |          | cst.clj`, `clj/yin/repl/host/jvm.clj`, `cljc/yin/repl/host.cljc` (the JVM selector),                                |\\n336: |       |       |          | `cljc/dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`, `cljc/dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc`. Nine.                                         |\\n337: +-------+-------+----------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+\\n338: | cljs  | 140   | 133      | `cljs/dao/st