           |\\n797: |                            | is **not** on list 1 (it is exempt by pattern).                                                 |                             |\\n798: +----------------------------+-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+-----------------------------+\\n799: \\n800: **Baseline versus additions and deletions.** The H0 baseline is the set of\\n801: **existing** files above (every entry except the planned additions named\\n802: in the profile row). The planned additions are the seven `dao/host/*.cljc`\\n803: files (five in H1, two in H3), which join list 1 when their slices land. The deletions are\\n804: three: `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc` (H2), `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc` (H4, the\\n805: JVM/JS Boring wrapper) and `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd` (H4, the Dart\\n806: Jing writer, a lane-specific file that the seams row excludes and the first\\n807: row lists, so that the lane-specific category cannot silently retain it).\\n808: The final list 1 after H4 is therefore: the baseline minus the first row\\n809: (except `sign.cljc` for `generate`), both deleted Jing writers included in\\n810: that subtraction, plus the seven profile files. The host-library gate of\\n811: §8.2 is consistent with it.\\n812: \\n813: ### 8.2 The host-library gate (H2, H3): executable references within the closure\\n814: \\n815: A literal `grep` over `src/cljc` is **not** the gate: it matches a docstring\\n816: in the untouched `dao/data.cljc:54` (\\\"a BigInt/BigDecimal\\\", V) and the\\n817: out-of-scope `dao/postgraphics/lowering.cljc:587` (`:rgba8unorm`, V), so\\n818: its asserted result would be false. The gate is instead `dao.host.gate-test`\\n819: run in **library mode**, which **lands with H2**, not H0: H0 is a freeze\\n820: with no source change and the library mode has no consumer before H2's\\n821: deletion, so building it in H0 would add a deliverable nothing exercises\\n822: and nothing can falsify; H2 builds it with the H2 name list and its two\\n823: negative tests (below), and H3 extends the name list. In library mode the\\n824: gate takes the H0 closure tool's tagged file list\\n825: for the adopted closure (so out-of-scope files never count), reads each\\n826: file with the Clojure reader per lane feature (so comments and string\\n827: literals, docstrings included, never count), and collects symbols, class\\n828: names and import/require forms; a hit is any such symbol naming\\n829: `BigInteger`, `BigDecimal`, `clojure.lang.Ratio`, `java.text`, `unorm`\\n830: (H2) or `MessageDigest`, `Blake3`, `noble`, `blake3_dart`, `package:crypto`,\\n831: `ed25519_edwards`, `goog.crypt.base64` (H3) in a file outside `dao/host/`\\n832: and, for H3's Ed25519 names, outside `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc` (`generate`,\\n833: deferred). Codec-track files stay on list 1 and are not scanned by this\\n834: mode (their arms are the codec track's). The gate fails distinctly when the\\n835: closure list is empty or a file cannot be read, which is a scan error, not\\n836: \\\"no hits\\\".\\n837: \\n838: ### 8.3 File-disjointness from the codec track, including tests (re-checked, V)\\n839: \\n840: Codec-track source files (`codec.md` §7.1): `dao/stream/ws.cljc`,\\n841: `transit.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`, `cbor/boring.cljc`, `codec.cljc`,\\n842: `remote_channel.cljc`, `jing/stream.cljc`, `data.cljc`, the four ws adapters,\\n843: `yin/repl/{serve,connect}.cljc`. Codec-track test namespaces (`codec.md`\\n844: §7.2): the 22 requiring Transit, including `ws_test`, `ws-codec-test`,\\n845: `remote-route-test`, `loopback-net`, `transit-test`, `dao.stream.cbor-test`,\\n846: `dao.jing.stream-test`, `yin.repl.main-test`.\\n847: \\n848: H0-H4 source files: `dao/host/*` (new), `yin/vm/integer/host.cljc`,\\n849: `dao/jing/cbor.cljc`, `dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc`, `src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd`,\\n850: `dao/jing.cljc`, `yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc`, `yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`,\\n851: `yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc`, `yin/vm/data.cljc`, `yin/vm/values.cljc`,\\n852: `yin/vm.cljc`, `yin/vm/engine.cljc`, `yin/vm/integer.cljc`,\\n853: `dao/stream/chunks.cljc`, `dao/stream/base64.cljc`, `dao/jing/dht.cljc`,\\n854: `yin/vm/linker.cljc`, `dao/stream/datagram.cljc`, `dao/data/arrays.cljc`.\\n855: H0-H4 test files: `dao/host/*_test` (new), `yin/vm/integer_test`,\\n856: `yang/python/antlr/{int_heap,int_literal,int_ops}_test`, `dao/jing/cbor_*`,\\n857: `dao/jing_test`, `yin/vm/linker/sign_test`, `dao/stream/base64_test`,\\n858: `yin/vm/debruijn_code_test`, `yin/vm/data_test`, `dao/data/btree_*`.\\n859: \\n860: Intersection: none, with two recorded deferrals: `dao/stream/codec.cljc:45`\\n861: (`host-bytes?` over `dao.host.bytes`) after C4, and `dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc`\\n862: (the transport writer) is **not** touched by H4. The `dao.stream.cbor-test`\\n863: and `dao.jing.cbor_test` namespaces are distinct files. The deferred H5\\n864: (§9.1) would touch `ws.cljc:122`, `ws_test.cljc:11` and\\n865: `remote_route_test.cljc:24` (V: identity-less ring creation), which is why\\n866: it is deferred behind the codec track as well as behind its own design.\\n867: \\n868: Coordination with a host-lane probe track: its \\\"narrow source adaptations\\\"\\n869: (R: the spike touched `integer/host.cljc`, `jing.cljc`, `cbor.cljc`,\\n870: `cbor/boring.cljc`) are exactly the H1-H4 files; under OQ3 that work is\\n871: paused until H4 lands and needs file-level coordination, not just a rebase.\\n872: \"}]}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"tool\",\"messageId\":\"6c32c1c1-f3e0-464e-9c58-38125c25fff6\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Here I'll read the tools: closure.clj, gate_test.clj, corpus_hashes.clj. These are probably large. Main check items:\\n\\n(a) Fidelity of the closure tool: features per lane, resolution src/<lane> taking precedence over src/cljc, not treating :as-alias/string libspecs as dependencies, handling of #?@ (tools.namespace's read-ns-decl processes reader conditionals with the given features — splicing is also handled by the reader). Verify the strip-nils adaptation. Independency of the second traversal in gate_test: it must not share code with tools.namespace, and must use tools.reader's :preserve and its own arm selection.\\n\\n(b) Gate tests: in-memory negatives, scan-failure, exemption by form, honesty of list 1 (:h0-unlisted 16).\\n\\n(c) corpus_hashes: 18 files, tests assert the digests.\\n\\n(d) Verify F2 myself: grep for random-uuid occurrences within src/cljc; grep for places that require dao.await / yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.\\n\\n(e) Scope: only src/dev/host_boundary, test/dao/host/gate_test.clj, docs/design/host-boundary/* — confirm that deps.edn/bb.edn are unchanged (compared to base? Can't diff without git, but can compare the main tree's deps.edn with what I saw in j0c... the main tree's deps.edn was already read earlier in this session (j0c worktree + main). Check whether the host-h0 worktree's deps.edn matches main. Actually base eacaed90 is the local master; the main tree's deps.edn that I read in a previous turn — the worktree one should be identical. Quick check by grepping for hb alias (should not exist).\\n\\nRead closure.clj and gate_test.clj. gate_test is probably big (10 deftests + traversal B). First read closure.clj and corpus_hashes.clj, then gate_test.clj, after that do targeted greps.\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now the tool sources.\\n\\n\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_a96da9c82ca34cc4a5ec9729\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"paths\":[\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj\",\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj\"]}}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"model\",\"createdAt\":1792522654730,\"messageId\":\"11461243-dd8b-40f3-8173-d080c8cddc9f\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_a96da9c82ca34cc4a5ec9729\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 2/2 files\\n--- File Contents ---\\n\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj (clojure)\\n(ns host-boundary.closure\\n  \\\"The adopted closure of dao.stream.host-boundary.md §3.1, per lane.\\n\\n   A require-form traversal from yin.repl.main over the ns declarations,\\n   parsed by clojure.tools.namespace.parse (read-ns-decl with the lane's\\n   reader features, deps-from-ns-decl for :require, :use and\\n   :require-macros; :as-alias and string (npm, dart:) libspecs are not\\n   dependencies). Lane features: :clj #{:clj}, :cljs #{:cljs},\\n   :cljd #{:cljd :clj} (the cljd build also reads :clj arms; the first\\n   matching arm wins, as in tools.reader). A namespace resolves to\\n   src/<lane>/<path>.<lane> first (the shadow: yin.repl.host is\\n   host.cljc on the JVM, host.cljs and host.cljd elsewhere), then\\n   src/cljc/<path>.cljc; a namespace with neither (clojure.core, a\\n   library) is outside the closure.\\n\\n   It is not a compiler-resolved call graph: it over-includes a namespace\\n   required but unused, and does not see dynamic loading.\\n\\n   Each file is tagged with its §3.1 classes (a set: a file can sit in\\n   several rows of the §3.1 table; :none means no host contact beyond the\\n   §3.3 exempt syntax).\\n\\n   Run from the repo root:\\n     clojure -Sdeps '{:aliases {:hb {:extra-paths [\\\\\\\"src/dev\\\\\\\"]\\n                      :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace\\n                                   {:mvn/version \\\\\\\"1.5.0\\\\\\\"}}}}}' \\\\\\\\\\n       -M:hb -m host-boundary.closure [--check]\\n   writes docs/design/host-boundary/closure-{clj,cljs,cljd}.edn and\\n   prints the totals; --check writes nothing and exits 1 when a committed\\n   file differs from the computed closure.\\\"\\n  (:require\\n    [clojure.java.io :as io]\\n    [clojure.pprint :as pp]\\n    [clojure.set :as set]\\n    [clojure.string :as str]\\n    [clojure.tools.namespace.parse :as parse]\\n    [clojure.walk :as walk]))\\n\\n\\n(def root 'yin.repl.main)\\n(def lanes [:clj :cljs :cljd])\\n(def out-dir \\\"docs/design/host-boundary\\\")\\n\\n\\n(def lane-features\\n  {:clj #{:clj}, :cljs #{:cljs}, :cljd #{:cljd :clj}})\\n\\n\\n(defn ns->path\\n  [ns-sym]\\n  (-> (name ns-sym) (str/replace \\\"-\\\" \\\"_\\\") (str/replace \\\".\\\" \\\"/\\\")))\\n\\n\\n(defn resolve-file\\n  \\\"The repo-relative file for ns-sym on lane, or nil.\\\"\\n  [lane ns-sym]\\n  (let [p (ns->path ns-sym)\\n        lane-dir (name lane)]\\n    (some (fn [f] (when (.isFile (io/file f)) f))\\n          [(str \\\"src/\\\" lane-dir \\\"/\\\" p \\\".\\\" lane-dir)\\n           (str \\\"src/cljc/\\\" p \\\".cljc\\\")])))\\n\\n\\n(defn strip-nils\\n  \\\"Drops the nil a lane's arm leaves in a libspec position\\n   (`#?(:cljd nil :clj [x])` reads as nil on :cljd); deps-from-ns-decl\\n   refuses nil as unparsable, the compilers ignore it.\\\"\\n  [form]\\n  (walk/postwalk (fn [x]\\n                   (cond (vector? x) (vec (remove nil? x))\\n                         (seq? x) (apply list (remove nil? x))\\n                         :else x))\\n                 form))\\n\\n\\n(defn ns-decl\\n  [lane file]\\n  (with-open [r (java.io.PushbackReader. (io/reader file))]\\n    (strip-nils (parse/read-ns-decl r {:read-cond :allow\\n                                       :features (lane-features lane)}))))\\n\\n\\n(defn lane-closure\\n  \\\"{file ns-sym} for every file reachable from root on lane.\\\"\\n  [lane]\\n  (loop [todo [root]\\n         seen #{}\\n         files {}]\\n    (if-let [n (first todo)]\\n      (if (seen n)\\n        (recur (rest todo) seen files)\\n        (let [seen (conj seen n)]\\n          (if-let [f (resolve-file lane n)]\\n            (let [decl (ns-decl lane f)\\n                  deps (sort (parse/deps-from-ns-decl decl))]\\n              (when-not (= n (parse/name-from-ns-decl decl))\\n                (throw (ex-info \\\"ns name does not match its file\\\"\\n                                {:lane lane :ns n :file f\\n                                 :declared (parse/name-from-ns-decl decl)})))\\n              (recur (concat (rest todo) deps) seen (assoc files f n)))\\n            (recur (rest todo) seen files))))\\n      files)))\\n\\n\\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n;; §3.1 classes. Keys are namespaces; a row's namespaces are named exactly as\\n;; the §3.1 table names them, expanded where the table abbreviates (\\\".datagram\\\"\\n;; = dao.stream.datagram, \\\"the seams\\\" = the lane-specific ws/datagram files).\\n;; Files of the §3.2 random-uuid/rand list carry :deferred-entropy.\\n;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\n(def class-rows\\n  [[:profile-internal-pure \\\"H1-H2 (writer H4)\\\"\\n    '[yin.vm.integer.host dao.jing.cbor dao.jing.cbor.boring dao.jing.cbor.cljd\\n      yin.vm.debruijn yin.vm.debruijn-code yin.vm.data yin.vm.values\\n      dao.stream.chunks dao.stream.base64 dao.jing.dht yin.vm.linker\\n      dao.stream.datagram dao.data.arrays]]\\n   [:profile-hash-sign \\\"H3\\\" '[dao.jing yin.vm.linker.sign]]\\n   [:consumer \\\"H2 (require change only)\\\"\\n    '[yin.vm yin.vm.engine yin.vm.values yin.vm.data yin.vm.integer]]\\n   [:external-stream-seam \\\"none (existing streams)\\\"\\n    '[dao.stream.ws dao.stream.datagram dao.stream.udp\\n      dao.stream.ws.jvm dao.stream.ws.node dao.stream.ws.dart\\n      dao.stream.ws.browser dao.stream.datagram.jvm dao.stream.datagram.node\\n      dao.stream.datagram.dart yin.repl.host yin.repl.host.jvm\\n      yin.repl.host.common]]\\n   [:deferred-storage \\\"deferred §9.2\\\"\\n    '[dao.jing.file dao.space.store.fs dao.space.store\\n      dao.stream.journal.file dao.data.btree.storage]]\\n   [:deferred-entropy \\\"deferred §9.1\\\"\\n    '[dao.stream.ringbuffer dao.stream.memory-log dao.stream.ws\\n      dao.stream.remote dao.stream.remote-pair dao.stream.remote-route\\n      dao.stream.journal dao.jing.content.step dao.lease dao.await\\n      dao.space.store.fs yin.vm.linker yin.vm.ucf.custody\\n      yin.vm.ucf.holder.driver yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve yin.vm.telemetry\\n      yin.repl yin.repl.dht dao.stream.rpc dao.jing.dht dao.space.dht\\n      yin.vm.linker.sign]]\\n   [:deferred-timers \\\"deferred §9.1\\\"\\n    '[dao.jing.content.async dao.jing.coordinate dao.jing.content.driver\\n      dao.data.btree.storage]]\\n   [:driver \\\"driver (ambient reads deferred §9.1)\\\"\\n    '[yin.repl.main yin.repl yin.repl.state]]\\n   [:deferred-stage \\\"deferred §9.3\\\"\\n    '[yang.antlr.cst yang.frontend yang.stage yin.repl.frontends]]\\n   [:deferred-gensym \\\"deferred §9.1\\\"\\n    '[yang.clojure yang.php dao.space.transact]]\\n   [:runtime-prereq \\\"table C, no slice\\\"\\n    '[dao.data.btree dao.jing.file dao.stream.journal dao.space.transactor\\n      dao.space.schema yin.vm.ucf.authority]]\\n   ;; §3.1 names transit, cbor and codec; the rest are the codec track's\\n   ;; files by §8.3 (and ws-project by §8.1's codec row) and the lane twins.\\n   [:codec-track \\\"codec track, untouched (§8.3)\\\"\\n    '[dao.stream.transit dao.stream.cbor dao.stream.codec\\n      dao.stream.cbor.boring dao.stream.cbor.cljd dao.stream.transit.cljd\\n      dao.stream.ws dao.stream.remote-channel dao.stream.ws-project\\n      dao.jing.stream dao.data dao.stream.ws.jvm dao.stream.ws.node\\n      dao.stream.ws.dart dao.stream.ws.browser yin.repl.serve\\n      yin.repl.connect]]\\n   [:internal-pure-display \\\"none (list 1, display only)\\\" '[dao.pretty]]])\\n\\n\\n(def prefix-rows\\n  \\\"Rows the §3.1 table names by prefix (`yang.python.antlr.*`).\\\"\\n  [[:deferred-stage \\\"yang.python.antlr.\\\"]])\\n\\n\\n(def lane-rows\\n  \\\"Lane-specific files the §3.1 table does not name in a row but §3.1's\\n   lane-specific list and §8.1's \\\\\\\"Seams and driver\\\\\\\" row place: the\\n   waitset timer drivers (setTimeout, Timer) are seams of dao.stream.waitset.\\\"\\n  '{dao.stream.waitset.driver #{:external-stream-seam}})\\n\\n\\n(defn classes-of\\n  [ns-sym]\\n  (let [s (name ns-sym)\\n        cs (into (set (keep (fn [[c _ nss]] (when (some #{ns-sym} nss) c))\\n                            class-rows))\\n                 (keep (fn [[c pre]] (when (str/starts-with? s pre) c))\\n                       prefix-rows))\\n        cs (into cs (lane-rows ns-sym))]\\n    (if (seq cs) cs #{:none})))\\n\\n\\n(def class-legend\\n  (into (sorted-map) (map (fn [[c slice _]] [c slice]) class-rows)))\\n\\n\\n(defn lane-report\\n  [lane files shared]\\n  {:lane lane\\n   :root root\\n   :features (lane-features lane)\\n   :total (count files)\\n   :shared (count shared)\\n   :lane-specific (count (remove shared (keys files)))\\n   :class-legend (assoc class-legend :none \\\"no host contact beyond §3.3\\\")\\n   :files (vec (for [[f n] (sort-by key files)]\\n                 {:file f\\n                  :ns n\\n                  :shared (contains? shared f)\\n                  :classes (into (sorted-set) (classes-of n))}))})\\n\\n\\n(defn compute\\n  []\\n  (let [closures (into {} (map (fn [l] [l (lane-closure l)]) lanes))\\n        shared (apply set/intersection (map (comp set keys) (vals closures)))]\\n    {:shared shared\\n     :reports (into {} (map (fn [[l fs]] [l (lane-report l fs shared)])\\n                            closures))}))\\n\\n\\n(defn render\\n  [report]\\n  (str \\\";; Generated by src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj (host-boundary H0).\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\";; Do not edit by hand; regenerate with the command in that file's ns doc.\\\\n\\\"\\n       (with-out-str\\n         (binding [*print-namespace-maps* false]\\n           (pp/pprint report)))))\\n\\n\\n(defn out-file\\n  [lane]\\n  (str out-dir \\\"/closure-\\\" (name lane) \\\".edn\\\"))\\n\\n\\n(defn -main\\n  [& args]\\n  (let [check? (some #{\\\"--check\\\"} args)\\n        {:keys [shared reports]} (compute)\\n        stale (atom [])]\\n    (doseq [l lanes]\\n      (let [r (reports l)\\n            text (render r)\\n            f (io/file (out-file l))]\\n        (println (format \\\"%-5s total %d shared %d lane-specific %d\\\"\\n                         (name l) (:total r) (:shared r) (:lane-specific r)))\\n        (if check?\\n          (when-not (and (.isFile f) (= text (slurp f)))\\n            (swap! stale conj (out-file l)))\\n          (do (io/make-parents f)\\n              (spit f text)))))\\n    (println \\\"shared (all three lanes):\\\" (count shared))\\n    (when (seq @stale)\\n      (println \\\"STALE:\\\" (str/join \\\" \\\" @stale))\\n      (System/exit 1))\\n    (shutdown-agents)))\\n\\n\\n// File: .claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj (clojure)\\n(ns host-boundary.corpus-hashes\\n  \\\"The corpus hash set of dao.stream.host-boundary.md H0 (d): the SHA-256\\n   of every file under the Jing corpus (test/resources/dao/jing) and the\\n   codec wire fixtures (test/fixtures/codec), which H1-H4 must keep\\n   byte-identical.\\n\\n   Run from the repo root with babashka:\\n     bb src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj [--check]\\n   writes docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn; --check writes\\n   nothing and exits 1 when a file's bytes, or the file set, differ from\\n   the committed hash set. dao.host.gate-test asserts the same on the JVM\\n   lane.\\\"\\n  (:require\\n    [babashka.fs :as fs]\\n    [clojure.edn :as edn]\\n    [clojure.pprint :as pp]\\n    [clojure.string :as str]))\\n\\n\\n(def roots [\\\"test/resources/dao/jing\\\" \\\"test/fixtures/codec\\\"])\\n(def out-file \\\"docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn\\\")\\n\\n\\n(defn sha-256\\n  [path]\\n  (let [d (java.security.MessageDigest/getInstance \\\"SHA-256\\\")]\\n    (apply str (map #(format \\\"%02x\\\" (bit-and % 0xff))\\n                    (.digest d (fs/read-all-bytes path))))))\\n\\n\\n(defn hash-set*\\n  []\\n  {:algorithm \\\"SHA-256\\\"\\n   :regenerate \\\"bb src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj\\\"\\n   :roots roots\\n   :files (into (sorted-map)\\n                (for [r roots\\n                      p (fs/glob r \\\"**\\\")\\n                      :when (fs/regular-file? p)\\n                      :let [f (str/replace (str p) \\\"\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\"/\\\")]]\\n                  [f (sha-256 p)]))})\\n\\n\\n(defn render\\n  [m]\\n  (str \\\";; Generated by src/dev/host_boundary/corpus_hashes.clj (host-boundary H0).\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\";; Do not edit by hand; H1-H4 keep these bytes identical.\\\\n\\\"\\n       (with-out-str (pp/pprint m))))\\n\\n\\n(defn -main\\n  [& args]\\n  (let [m (hash-set*)\\n        text (render m)]\\n    (println (count (:files m)) \\\"files\\\")\\n    (if (some #{\\\"--check\\\"} args)\\n      (let [committed (when (fs/exists? out-file) (edn/read-string (slurp out-file)))]\\n        (if (= (:files committed) (:files m))\\n          (println \\\"corpus identical to\\\" out-file)\\n          (do (println \\\"CORPUS DIFFERS from\\\" out-file)\\n              (doseq [f (sort (into (set (keys (:files m))) (keys (:files committed))))\\n                      :when (not= (get (:files m) f) (get (:files committed) f))]\\n                (println \\\" \\\" f))\\n              (System/exit 1))))\\n      (spit out-file text))))\\n\\n\\n(when (= *file* (System/getProperty \\\"babashka.file\\\"))\\n  (apply -main *command-line-args*))\\n\\n\"}]}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"tool\",\"messageId\":\"8f350e40-8203-4d56-8a4b-8e87838f5125\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"closure.clj looks fine: lane features are correct (:cljd #{:cljd :clj}), resolution order prioritizes lane and then cljc, tools.namespace's read-ns-decl and deps-from-ns-decl (:as-alias is handled by tools.namespace 1.5.0 — deps-from-ns-decl excludes :as-alias; string libspecs: deps-from-ns-decl maps symbols; strings are… actually deps-from-ns-decl in 1.5.0 only returns symbols; string libspecs like \