e design. If src/clj-only namespaces were reachable from cljd, the design's totals wouldn't match either. Not a flaw relative to the spec; but worth mentioning? The design explicitly states this rule and the totals agree at 142/140/141, and traversal B independently agrees. OK.\\n\\n(5) Traversal B in gate_test — need to read gate_test.clj to verify independence and gate logic. Probably a large file. Let's read it.\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now the gate test — the biggest adversarial target.\\n\\n\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_2cad5919095c4bbca7a595f2\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/test/dao/host/gate_test.clj\"}}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"model\",\"createdAt\":1792522691294,\"messageId\":\"5801e7e8-8738-4dff-ad44-9af381d64d22\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_2cad5919095c4bbca7a595f2\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 1/1 file, 772 lines\\n1: (ns dao.host.gate-test\\n2:   \\\"The H0 freeze gate of docs/design/dao.stream.host-boundary.md (§8 H0,\\n3:    §8.1, §3.2, §3.3), over the adopted closure committed by\\n4:    src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj under docs/design/host-boundary/.\\n5: \\n6:    The gate reads every closure file with tools.reader (:read-cond\\n7:    :preserve, so every lane's arms are seen; comments, strings and\\n8:    docstrings never count) and fails when\\n9:    - a file outside list 1 holds a non-exempt host arm (§3.3 exempts:\\n10:      ns-form arms, catch-type arms, arms equal but for hints, protocol\\n11:      blocks directly inside deftype/defrecord/reify/extend bodies,\\n12:      print-method defmethods, exists? tests, (Object.)/(js-obj)\\n13:      sentinels); a lane-specific file (.clj .cljs .cljd) is a host arm as\\n14:      a whole;\\n15:    - a file holds more resolved effect calls of a kind than list 2\\n16:      permits (the §3.2 kinds, and calls of the §2.4 M entries).\\n17:    Effect calls are resolved lexically: a symbol bound by let, fn, loop,\\n18:    for, doseq, catch, letfn or a deftype method, defined in its file, or\\n19:    excluded by :refer-clojure, is not the core function; quoted forms and\\n20:    (comment ...) are data. Reading zero files, or failing to read one, is\\n21:    a scan failure, distinct from a pass.\\n22: \\n23:    JVM lane only: the gate reads source text from disk; what it checks is\\n24:    the same text on every lane.\\n25: \\n26:    Also here: the independent second traversal of the closure (a\\n27:    reader-form walker that selects reader-conditional arms itself and\\n28:    parses libspecs itself, sharing no code with tools.namespace), which\\n29:    must agree with the committed closure files.\\\"\\n30:   (:require\\n31:     [clojure.edn :as edn]\\n32:     [clojure.java.io :as io]\\n33:     [clojure.set :as set]\\n34:     [clojure.string :as str]\\n35:     [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\\n36:     [clojure.tools.reader :as reader]\\n37:     [clojure.tools.reader.reader-types :as rt])\\n38:   (:import\\n39:     (clojure.lang\\n40:       ReaderConditional)))\\n41: \\n42: \\n43: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n44: ;; Reading\\n45: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n46: \\n47: (defn read-forms\\n48:   \\\"Every top-level form of text, reader conditionals preserved.\\\"\\n49:   [text]\\n50:   (binding [reader/*read-eval* false\\n51:             ;; ::alias/kw needs no real namespace: keywords never count\\n52:             reader/*alias-map* (fn [sym] sym)\\n53:             reader/*default-data-reader-fn* (fn [tag v] (tagged-literal tag v))]\\n54:     (let [rdr (rt/indexing-push-back-reader text 1)]\\n55:       (loop [acc []]\\n56:         (let [form (reader/read {:read-cond :preserve :eof ::eof} rdr)]\\n57:           (if (= ::eof form) acc (recur (conj acc form))))))))\\n58: \\n59: \\n60: (defn rc?\\n61:   [x]\\n62:   (instance? ReaderConditional x))\\n63: \\n64: \\n65: (defn rc-arms\\n66:   \\\"[[feature form] ...] of a reader conditional.\\\"\\n67:   [^ReaderConditional rc]\\n68:   (map vec (partition 2 (.-form rc))))\\n69: \\n70: \\n71: (defn splicing?\\n72:   [^ReaderConditional rc]\\n73:   (boolean (.-splicing rc)))\\n74: \\n75: \\n76: (defn head\\n77:   [x]\\n78:   (when (and (seq? x) (symbol? (first x))) (first x)))\\n79: \\n80: \\n81: (defn line-of\\n82:   [x]\\n83:   (:line (meta x)))\\n84: \\n85: \\n86: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n87: ;; The independent closure traversal (traversal B)\\n88: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n89: \\n90: (def closure-root 'yin.repl.main)\\n91: (def lanes [:clj :cljs :cljd])\\n92: (def lane-features {:clj #{:clj}, :cljs #{:cljs}, :cljd #{:cljd :clj}})\\n93: \\n94: \\n95: (defn select-arms\\n96:   \\\"form with every reader conditional replaced by its lane arm: the first\\n97:    arm whose feature is in features or is :default; a splicing arm's\\n98:    elements spliced into the enclosing collection; no arm, nothing.\\\"\\n99:   [features form]\\n100:   (let [pick (fn [rc]\\n101:                (some (fn [[k v]] (when (or (features k) (= :default k)) [v]))\\n102:                      (rc-arms rc)))\\n103:         expand (fn [xs]\\n104:                  (mapcat (fn [x]\\n105:                            (if (rc? x)\\n106:                              (when-let [[v] (pick x)]\\n107:                                (if (splicing? x)\\n108:                                  (map #(select-arms features %) v)\\n109:                                  [(select-arms features v)]))\\n110:                              [(select-arms features x)]))\\n111:                          xs))]\\n112:     (cond\\n113:       (rc? form) (some->> (pick form) first (select-arms features))\\n114:       (seq? form) (apply list (expand form))\\n115:       (vector? form) (vec (expand form))\\n116:       (map? form) (into {} (map vec (partition 2 (expand (mapcat identity form)))))\\n117:       :else form)))\\n118: \\n119: \\n120: (defn libspec-deps\\n121:   [spec]\\n122:   (cond\\n123:     (symbol? spec) [spec]\\n124:     (or (string? spec) (keyword? spec) (nil? spec)) []\\n125:     (sequential? spec)\\n126:     (let [[a b] spec\\n127:           opts (rest spec)]\\n128:       (cond\\n129:         (string? a) []\\n130:         (and (symbol? a) (or (nil? b) (keyword? b)))\\n131:         (if (and (= :as-alias b) (not-any? #{:as :refer :refer-macros :include-macros} opts))\\n132:           []\\n133:           [a])\\n134:         (symbol? a)\\n135:         (mapcat (fn [s]\\n136:                   (map #(symbol (str a \\\".\\\" %)) (libspec-deps s)))\\n137:                 (remove nil? (rest spec)))\\n138:         :else []))\\n139:     :else []))\\n140: \\n141: \\n142: (defn ns-deps\\n143:   \\\"The namespaces an ns form requires on a lane: :require, :use and\\n144:    :require-macros clauses.\\\"\\n145:   [features ns-form]\\n146:   (let [f (select-arms features ns-form)]\\n147:     (->> (rest f)\\n148:          (filter seq?)\\n149:          (filter #(#{:require :use :require-macros} (first %)))\\n150:          (mapcat rest)\\n151:          (mapcat libspec-deps)\\n152:          set)))\\n153: \\n154: \\n155: (defn lane-file\\n156:   [lane ns-sym]\\n157:   (let [p (-> (name ns-sym) (str/replace \\\"-\\\" \\\"_\\\") (str/replace \\\".\\\" \\\"/\\\"))]\\n158:     (some #(when (.isFile (io/file %)) %)\\n159:           [(str \\\"src/\\\" (name lane) \\\"/\\\" p \\\".\\\" (name lane))\\n160:            (str \\\"src/cljc/\\\" p \\\".cljc\\\")])))\\n161: \\n162: \\n163: (defn traverse\\n164:   \\\"The closure files of lane from closure-root, by traversal B.\\\"\\n165:   [lane]\\n166:   (loop [todo [closure-root] seen #{} files #{}]\\n167:     (if-let [n (first todo)]\\n168:       (if (seen n)\\n169:         (recur (rest todo) seen files)\\n170:         (if-let [f (lane-file lane n)]\\n171:           (let [ns-form (first (filter #(= 'ns (head %)) (read-forms (slurp f))))]\\n172:             (recur (concat (rest todo) (sort (ns-deps (lane-features lane) ns-form)))\\n173:                    (conj seen n)\\n174:                    (conj files f)))\\n175:           (recur (rest todo) (conj seen n) files)))\\n176:       files)))\\n177: \\n178: \\n179: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n180: ;; The committed closure (traversal A, src/dev/host_boundary/closure.clj)\\n181: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n182: \\n183: (defn committed-closure\\n184:   [lane]\\n185:   (edn/read-string (slurp (str \\\"docs/design/host-boundary/closure-\\\" (name lane) \\\".edn\\\"))))\\n186: \\n187: \\n188: (defn closure-files\\n189:   \\\"The union of the three lanes' committed closure files.\\\"\\n190:   []\\n191:   (into (sorted-set) (mapcat #(map :file (:files (committed-closure %))) lanes)))\\n192: \\n193: \\n194: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n195: ;; Host arms (§3.3 exemptions)\\n196: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n197: \\n198: (def deftype-heads\\n199:   '#{deftype defrecord reify extend-type extend-protocol specify specify!})\\n200: \\n201: \\n202: (def sentinels\\n203:   '#{(Object.) (js-obj) (js/Object.) (java.lang.Object.)})\\n204: \\n205: \\n206: (defn exemption\\n207:   \\\"The §3.3 pattern that exempts rc, given its ancestors (outermost first),\\n208:    or nil.\\\"\\n209:   [rc ancestors]\\n210:   (let [parent (peek ancestors)\\n211:         arms (map second (rc-arms rc))\\n212:         catch-form? #(and (seq? %) (= 'catch (first %)))]\\n213:     (cond\\n214:       (some #(= 'ns (head %)) ancestors) :ns-require-arm\\n215:       (and (catch-form? parent) (identical? rc (second parent))) :catch-type\\n216:       (and (< 1 (count arms)) (apply = arms)) :hint-only\\n217:       (and (splicing? rc) (deftype-heads (head parent))) :protocol-block\\n218:       (some #(and (= 'defmethod (head %)) (= 'print-method (second %))) ancestors) :print-method\\n219:       (every? #(and (seq? %) (= 'defmethod (first %)) (= 'print-method (second %))) arms)\\n220:       :print-method\\n221:       (every? #(= 'exists? (head %)) arms) :exists\\n222:       (every? sentinels arms) :sentinel\\n223:       :else nil)))\\n224: \\n225: \\n226: (defn non-exempt-arms\\n227:   \\\"[line ...] of the non-exempt reader conditionals in forms.\\\"\\n228:   [forms]\\n229:   (let [acc (atom [])\\n230:         walk (fn walk\\n231:                [form ancestors]\\n232:                (let [down (conj ancestors form)]\\n233:                  (cond\\n234:                    (rc? form)\\n235:                    (do (when-not (exemption form ancestors)\\n236:                          (swap! acc conj (or (some (comp line-of second) (rc-arms form))\\n237:                                              (some line-of (rseq ancestors)))))\\n238:                        (doseq [[_ arm] (rc-arms form)]\\n239:                          (if (splicing? form)\\n240:                            (doseq [x arm] (walk x down))\\n241:                            (walk arm down))))\\n242:                    (and (seq? form) (= 'comment (first form))) nil\\n243:                    (map? form) (doseq [[k v] form] (walk k down) (walk v down))\\n244:                    (coll? form) (doseq [x form] (walk x down))\\n245:                    :else nil)))]\\n246:     (doseq [f forms] (walk f []))\\n247:     @acc))\\n248: \\n249: \\n250: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n251: ;; Resolved effect calls (§3.2 kinds, §2.4 M entries)\\n252: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n253: \\n254: (def core-ns #{nil \\\"clojure.core\\\" \\\"cljs.core\\\" \\\"cljd.core\\\"})\\n255: \\n256: \\n257: (defn effect-kind\\n258:   \\\"The §3.2 kind of a symbol that names a host effect, or nil. core? is\\n259:    false when an unqualified name is shadowed in its file.\\\"\\n260:   [sym core?]\\n261:   (let [n (name sym)\\n262:         q (namespace sym)\\n263:         core (and (contains? core-ns q) (or q core?))]\\n264:     (cond\\n265:       (and core (= n \\\"random-uuid\\\")) :random-uuid\\n266:       (and core (#{\\\"rand\\\" \\\"rand-int\\\" \\\"rand-nth\\\" \\\"shuffle\\\" \\\"random-sample\\\"} n)) :rand\\n267:       (or (str/includes? n \\\"SecureRandom\\\")\\n268:           (= n \\\"Random.secure\\\")\\n269:           (= n \\\"randomUUID\\\")\\n270:           (and (= q \\\"js\\\") (str/starts-with? n \\\"crypto\\\"))\\n271:           (#{\\\"getRandomValues\\\" \\\"randomBytes\\\" \\\"generateKey\\\"} n)) :secure-random\\n272:       (and core (= n \\\"gensym\\\")) :gensym\\n273:       (or (and (#{\\\"System\\\" \\\"java.lang.System\\\"} q) (#{\\\"currentTimeMillis\\\" \\\"nanoTime\\\"} n))\\n274:           (and (= q \\\"js\\\") (or (str/starts-with? n \\\"Date\\\") (str/starts-with? n \\\"performance\\\")))\\n275:           (str/starts-with? n \\\"DateTime.now\\\")\\n276:           (and q (str/ends-with? q \\\"Instant\\\") (= n \\\"now\\\"))) :clock\\n277:       (or (and (#{\\\"System\\\" \\\"java.lang.System\\\"} q) (#{\\\"getenv\\\" \\\"getProperty\\\" \\\"getProperties\\\"} n))\\n278:           (and (= q \\\"js\\\") (str/starts-with? n \\\"process\\\"))\\n279:           (str/starts-with? n \\\"Platform.\\\")) :ambient\\n280:       (or (and core (#{\\\"println\\\" \\\"print\\\" \\\"prn\\\" \\\"pr\\\" \\\"printf\\\" \\\"newline\\\"} n))\\n281:           (and (= q \\\"js\\\") (str/starts-with? n \\\"console\\\"))) :print\\n282:       (or (and (= q \\\"js\\\") (#{\\\"setTimeout\\\" \\\"setInterval\\\" \\\"setImmediate\\\" \\\"queueMicrotask\\\"} n))\\n283:           (str/starts-with? n \\\"Timer\\\")\\n284:           (and (#{\\\"Thread\\\" \\\"java.lang.Thread\\\"} q) (= n \\\"sleep\\\"))\\n285:           (str/starts-with? n \\\"Future.delayed\\\")) :timer\\n286:       :else nil)))\\n287: \\n288: \\n289: (def m-entry-nss\\n290:   \\\"The namespaces holding §2.4's M entries, now and after H1.\\\"\\n291:   '#{dao.data.arrays dao.host.bytes})\\n292: \\n293: \\n294: (def m-entry-names #{\\\"aset\\\" \\\"acopy\\\" \\\"asort\\\" \\\"set!\\\" \\\"copy!\\\"})\\n295: \\n296: \\n297: (defn all-arms\\n298:   \\\"form with every reader conditional replaced by all its arms, so every\\n299:    lane's text is seen: a splicing conditional's elements are spliced into\\n300:    the enclosing collection; a non-splicing one becomes (do arm ...), or,\\n301:    with splice-all?, is spliced too (for ns clauses, where position does\\n302:    not bind).\\\"\\n303:   ([form] (all-arms false form))\\n304:   ([splice-all? form]\\n305:    (let [expand (fn [xs]\\n306:                   (mapcat (fn [x]\\n307:                             (if (and (rc? x) (or splice-all? (splicing? x)))\\n308:                               (map #(all-arms splice-all? %)\\n309:                                    (mapcat (fn [[_ v]] (if (splicing? x) v [v])) (rc-arms x)))\\n310:                               [(all-arms splice-all? x)]))\\n311:                           xs))]\\n312:      (cond\\n313:        (rc? form) (cons 'do (map #(all-arms splice-all? %)\\n314:                                  (mapcat (fn [[_ v]] (if (splicing? form) v [v]))\\n315:                                          (rc-arms form))))\\n316:        (seq? form) (with-meta (apply list (expand form)) (meta form))\\n317:        (vector? form) (vec (expand form))\\n318:        (map? form) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(all-arms splice-all? k) (all-arms splice-all? v)])\\n319:                                  form))\\n320:        :else form))))\\n321: \\n322: \\n323: (defn file-scope\\n324:   \\\"{:aliases {alias ns} :refers {sym ns} :shadowed #{sym}} of a file:\\n325:    every lane's ns arms, its top-level defs, its :refer-clojure excludes.\\\"\\n326:   [forms]\\n327:   (let [ns-form (all-arms true (first (filter #(= 'ns (head %)) forms)))\\n328:         specs (->> (rest ns-form)\\n329:                    (filter seq?)\\n330:                    (filter #(#{:require :use} (first %)))\\n331:                    (mapcat rest)\\n332:                    (filter vector?))\\n333:         opts (fn [spec] (apply hash-map (rest (if (even? (count spec)) (butlast spec) spec))))\\n334:         excluded (->> (rest ns-form)\\n335:                       (filter #(and (seq? %) (= :refer-clojure (first %))))\\n336:                       (mapcat #(:exclude (apply hash-map (rest %)))))\\n337:         defs (->> forms\\n338:                   (map all-arms)\\n339:                   (mapcat (fn [f] (if (= 'do (head f)) (rest f) [f])))\\n340:                   (keep (fn [f]\\n341:                           (when (#{'def 'defn 'defn- 'defmacro 'defonce 'declare\\n342:                                    'defprotocol 'defmulti} (head f))\\n343:                             (second f)))))]\\n344:     {:aliases (into {} (keep (fn [s] (when-let [a (:as (opts s))] [a (first s)])) specs))\\n345:      :refers (into {} (mapcat (fn [s]\\n346:                                 (let [r (:refer (opts s))]\\n347:                                   (when (sequential? r) (map (fn [x] [x (first s)]) r))))\\n348:                               specs))\\n349:      :shadowed (set (filter symbol? (concat excluded defs)))}))\\n350: \\n351: \\n352: (defn binding-syms\\n353:   \\\"Every symbol in a binding form (destructuring included).\\\"\\n354:   [b]\\n355:   (cond\\n356:     (symbol? b) (if (= '& b) [] [b])\\n357:     (map? b) (mapcat binding-syms (concat (keys b) (vals b)))\\n358:     (coll? b) (mapcat binding-syms b)\\n359:     :else []))\\n360: \\n361: \\n362: (def let-heads\\n363:   '#{let let* loop loop* when-let if-let when-some if-some when-first\\n364:      with-open dotimes for doseq})\\n365: \\n366: \\n367: (def fn-heads '#{fn fn* defn defn- defmacro defmethod})\\n368: \\n369: \\n370: (defn effect-calls\\n371:   \\\"[[kind line] ...] for the resolved effect calls in forms.\\\"\\n372:   [forms]\\n373:   (let [{:keys [aliases refers shadowed]} (file-scope forms)\\n374:         acc (atom [])\\n375:         hit! (fn [kind sym] (swap! acc conj [kind (line-of sym)]))\\n376:         resolve-m (fn [sym]\\n377:                     (if-let [q (namespace sym)]\\n378:                       (get aliases (symbol q) (symbol q))\\n379:                       (get refers sym)))]\\n380:     (letfn [(walk\\n381:               [form bound]\\n382:               (cond\\n383:                 (symbol? form)\\n384:                 (when-not (and (nil? (namespace form)) (bound form))\\n385:                   (if-let [k (effect-kind form (not (shadowed form)))]\\n386:                     (hit! k form)\\n387:                     (when (and (m-entry-nss (resolve-m form)) (m-entry-names (name form)))\\n388:                       (hit! :m-entry form))))\\n389: \\n390:                 (seq? form)\\n391:                 (let [h (head form)]\\n392:                   (cond\\n393:                     (#{'quote 'comment 'ns} h) nil\\n394:                     (let-heads h) (walk-let (second form) (nnext form) bound)\\n395:                     (= 'letfn h) (let [fns (second form)\\n396:                                        b (into bound (map first fns))]\\n397:                                    (doseq [f fns] (walk-fn (rest f) b))\\n398:                                    (walk-all (nnext form) b))\\n399:                     (fn-heads h) (walk-fn (rest form) bound)\\n400:                     (= 'catch h) (walk-all (drop 3 form) (conj bound (nth form 2 nil)))\\n401:                     (deftype-heads h) (let [fields (filter vector? (take 3 form))\\n402:                                             b (into bound (mapcat binding-syms fields))]\\n403:                                         (doseq [x (drop 2 form)]\\n404:                                           (if (and (seq? x) (vector? (second x)))\\n405:                                             (walk-fn x b)\\n406:                                             (walk x b))))\\n407:                     :else (walk-all form bound)))\\n408: \\n409:                 (map? form) (doseq [[k v] form] (walk k bound) (walk v bound))\\n410:                 (coll? form) (walk-all form bound)\\n411:                 :else nil))\\n412:             (walk-all [xs bound] (doseq [x xs] (walk x bound)))\\n413:             (walk-let\\n414:               [bvec body bound]\\n415:               (let [b (reduce (fn [b [lhs rhs]]\\n416:                                 (case lhs\\n417:                                   :let (do (walk-let rhs nil b) (into b (binding-syms (take-nth 2 rhs))))\\n418:                                   (:when :while) (do (walk rhs b) b)\\n419:                                   (do (walk rhs b) (into b (binding-syms lhs)))))\\n420:                               bound\\n421:                               (partition 2 (if (vector? bvec) bvec [])))]\\n422:                 (walk-all body b)))\\n423:             (walk-fn\\n424:               [tail bound]\\n425:               ;; tail: [name? doc? attrs? params body...] or [name? (params body...)...]\\n426:               (let [params (concat (filter vector? tail)\\n427:                                    (keep #(when (and (seq? %) (vector? (first %))) (first %)) tail))\\n428:                     b (into (into bound (filter symbol? (take 1 tail)))\\n429:                             (mapcat binding-syms params))]\\n430:                 (walk-all (remove #(or (vector? %) (symbol? %)\\n431:                                        (and (seq? %) (vector? (first %))))\\n432:                                   tail)\\n433:                           b)\\n434:                 (doseq [x tail :when (and (seq? x) (vector? (first x)))]\\n435:                   (walk-all (rest x) b))))]\\n436:       (doseq [f forms] (walk (all-arms f) #{})))\\n437:     @acc))\\n438: \\n439: \\n440: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n441: ;; List 1 and list 2\\n442: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n443: \\n444: (def list-1\\n445:   \\\"The closure files permitted non-exempt host arms (§8.1), by category.\\n446:    Generated from the H0 tree by the gate and reconciled against the §8.1\\n447:    baseline; :h0-unlisted marks the files with real arms that §8.1 does\\n448:    not name (an H0 finding, to resolve before H1).\\\"\\n449:   {;; H1-H4 migration sources\\n450:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/integer/host.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n451:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n452:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/jing/cbor/boring.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n453:    \\\"src/cljd/dao/jing/cbor/cljd.cljd\\\" :migration-source\\n454:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/jing.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n455:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n456:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n457:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_code.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n458:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/data.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n459:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/values.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n460:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/chunks.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n461:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/base64.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n462:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n463:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n464:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/datagram.cljc\\\" :migration-source\\n465:    ;; Profile\\n466:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/data/arrays.cljc\\\" :profile\\n467:    ;; Retained runtime prerequisites (table C) and display\\n468:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/data/btree.cljc\\\" :runtime-prereq\\n469:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/data/btree/storage.cljc\\\" :runtime-prereq\\n470:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/pretty.cljc\\\" :runtime-prereq\\n471:    ;; Codec-track files\\n472:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc\\\" :codec-track\\n473:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/transit.cljc\\\" :codec-track\\n474:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/cbor.cljc\\\" :codec-track\\n475:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/cbor/boring.cljc\\\" :codec-track\\n476:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/codec.cljc\\\" :codec-track\\n477:    ;; Seams and driver: every lane-specific file, the selector, the driver\\n478:    \\\"src/clj/dao/jing/content/driver.clj\\\" :seam-driver\\n479:    \\\"src/clj/dao/stream/datagram/jvm.clj\\\" :seam-driver\\n480:    \\\"src/clj/dao/stream/waitset/driver.clj\\\" :seam-driver\\n481:    \\\"src/clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj\\\" :seam-driver\\n482:    \\\"src/clj/yang/antlr/cst.clj\\\" :seam-driver\\n483:    \\\"src/clj/yin/repl/host/jvm.clj\\\" :seam-driver\\n484:    \\\"src/cljs/dao/stream/datagram/node.cljs\\\" :seam-driver\\n485:    \\\"src/cljs/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljs\\\" :seam-driver\\n486:    \\\"src/cljs/dao/stream/ws/node.cljs\\\" :seam-driver\\n487:    \\\"src/cljs/yang/antlr/cst.cljs\\\" :seam-driver\\n488:    \\\"src/cljs/yin/repl/host.cljs\\\" :seam-driver\\n489:    \\\"src/cljd/dao/stream/cbor/cljd.cljd\\\" :seam-driver\\n490:    \\\"src/cljd/dao/stream/transit/cljd.cljd\\\" :seam-driver\\n491:    \\\"src/cljd/dao/stream/datagram/dart.cljd\\\" :seam-driver\\n492:    \\\"src/cljd/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljd\\\" :seam-driver\\n493:    \\\"src/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd\\\" :seam-driver\\n494:    \\\"src/cljd/yang/antlr/cst.cljd\\\" :seam-driver\\n495:    \\\"src/cljd/yin/repl/host.cljd\\\" :seam-driver\\n496:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\\\" :seam-driver\\n497:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/repl/host.cljc\\\" :seam-driver\\n498:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/repl/state.cljc\\\" :seam-driver\\n499:    ;; Deferred-scope files (§9)\\n500:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/jing/file.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n501:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n502:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/space/store.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n503:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/journal/file.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n504:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/jing/coordinate.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n505:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n506:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n507:    \\\"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/parser.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n508:    \\\"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n509:    \\\"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/prelude.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n510:    \\\"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/render.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n511:    \\\"src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/repl_probe.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n512:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/journal.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n513:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/space/transactor.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n514:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority.cljc\\\" :deferred-scope\\n515:    ;; H0 finding: real host arms in closure files §8.1 does not name\\n516:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :78 host numeric predicates\\n517:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/space/query.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :808 runtime type name\\n518:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :168 host atom type\\n519:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :114 rand (entropy, §9.1)\\n520:    \\\"src/cljc/yang/antlr/packet.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :67 code points\\n521:    \\\"src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :375 runtime type name\\n522:    \\\"src/cljc/yang/php.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :95,98 number parsing\\n523:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/repl/adapter.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :58 edn reader\\n524:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :104 edn reader\\n525:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/repl/query.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :460 byte length\\n526:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :404 bytes->str decoding\\n527:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_code.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :439 safe integer\\n528:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn_register_effects.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :130 safe integer\\n529:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :929 runtime type name\\n530:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/closure.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :32 byte length\\n531:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc\\\" :h0-unlisted ; :282 byte length\\n532:    })\\n533: \\n534: \\n535: (def list-2\\n536:   \\\"The resolved effect calls permitted, {file {kind count}}: the §3.2\\n537:    sites inside the adopted closure and the callers of §2.4's M entries.\\n538:    A count is a ceiling: one more call of that kind in that file fails.\\\"\\n539:   {;; §3.2 random-uuid: 21 inside the closure (dao.await and\\n540:    ;; yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve are outside it)\\n541:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 2}\\n542:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/memory_log.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n543:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/ws.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n544:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/remote.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n545:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/remote_pair.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n546:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/remote_route.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n547:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/journal.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n548:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/jing/content/step.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n549:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/lease.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n550:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/space/store/fs.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 2, :ambient 4}\\n551:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/linker.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n552:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/custody.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n553:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n554:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/telemetry.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n555:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/repl.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 4, :ambient 3}\\n556:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/repl/dht.cljc\\\" {:random-uuid 1}\\n557:    ;; §3.2 rand, secure generators (sign :79 is jvm-pair's deterministic\\n558:    ;; seed-replay SecureRandom proxy, §2.5), gensym\\n559:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/stream/rpc.cljc\\\" {:rand 3}\\n560:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/jing/dht.cljc\\\" {:rand 1}\\n561:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/space/dht.cljc\\\" {:secure-random 3}\\n562:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/sign.cljc\\\" {:secure-random 3}\\n563:    \\\"src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\\\" {:gensym 2}\\n564:    \\\"src/cljc/yang/php.cljc\\\" {:gensym 1}\\n565:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/space/transact.cljc\\\" {:gensym 1}\\n566:    ;; §3.2 clocks, ambient reads, printing, timers: the driver and the seams\\n567:    \\\"src/cljc/yin/repl/main.cljc\\\" {:ambient 6, :clock 5, :print 13}\\n568:    \\\"src/clj/dao/jing/content/driver.clj\\\" {:clock 2, :timer 1}\\n569:    \\\"src/clj/dao/stream/datagram/jvm.clj\\\" {:timer 1}\\n570:    \\\"src/clj/dao/stream/ws/jvm.clj\\\" {:clock 1}\\n571:    \\\"src/cljs/dao/stream/ws/node.cljs\\\" {:clock 1}\\n572:    \\\"src/cljs/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljs\\\" {:timer 2}\\n573:    \\\"src/cljd/dao/stream/ws/dart.cljd\\\" {:clock 1}\\n574:    \\\"src/cljd/dao/stream/waitset/driver.cljd\\\" {:timer 1}\\n575:    ;; §2.4 M-entry callers resolved today (dao.data.arrays); chunks, cbor\\n576:    ;; and sign mutate host arrays directly and call no M entry yet\\n577:    \\\"src/cljc/dao/data/btree.cljc\\\" {:m-entry 33}})\\n578: \\n579: \\n580: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n581: ;; The gate\\n582: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n583: \\n584: (defn lane-specific?\\n585:   [file]\\n586:   (not (str/ends-with? file \\\".cljc\\\")))\\n587: \\n588: \\n589: (defn scan\\n590:   \\\"{file {:arms [line ...] :effects {kind [line ...]}}} for sources\\n591:    {file text}, or {file {:error msg}} for a file that cannot be read.\\\"\\n592:   [sources]\\n593:   (into (sorted-map)\\n594:         (map (fn [[file text]]\\n595:                [file (try\\n596:                        (let [forms (if text\\n597:                                      (read-forms text)\\n598:                                      (throw (ex-info \\\"cannot read file\\\" {:file file})))]\\n599:                          {:arms (if (lane-specific? file)\\n600:                                   [:whole-file]\\n601:                                   (non-exempt-arms forms))\\n602:                           :effects (reduce (fn [m [k line]] (update m k (fnil conj []) line))\\n603:                                            {}\\n604:                                            (effect-calls forms))})\\n605:                        (catch Exception e {:error (or (ex-message e) (str e))}))]))\\n606:         sources))\\n607: \\n608: \\n609: (defn gate\\n610:   \\\"The gate over sources {file text}: {:verdict :pass|:fail|:scan-failure\\n611:    :scanned n :errors [...] :arm-violations [...] :effect-violations [...]}.\\\"\\n612:   [sources list-1 list-2]\\n613:   (let [scanned (scan sources)\\n614:         errors (vec (keep (fn [[f r]] (when (:error r) [f (:error r)])) scanned))\\n615:         ok (remove (comp :error val) scanned)\\n616:         arm-violations (vec (for [[f r] ok\\n617:                                   :when (and (seq (:arms r)) (not (contains? list-1 f)))]\\n618:                               {:file f :lines (:arms r)}))\\n619:         effect-violations (vec (for [[f r] ok\\n620:                                      [k lines] (:effects r)\\n621:                                      :let [allowed (get-in list-2 [f k] 0)]\\n622:                                      :when (> (count lines) allowed)]\\n623:                                  {:file f :kind k :count (count lines)\\n624:                                   :allowed allowed :lines lines}))]\\n625:     {:verdict (cond (or (empty? scanned) (seq errors)) :scan-failure\\n626:                     (or (seq arm-violations) (seq effect-violations)) :fail\\n627:                     :else :pass)\\n628:      :scanned (count ok)\\n629:      :errors errors\\n630:      :arm-violations arm-violations\\n631:      :effect-violations effect-violations\\n632:      :observed scanned}))\\n633: \\n634: \\n635: (defn read-sources\\n636:   \\\"{file text} for files; an unreadable file maps to nil text, which the\\n637:    gate reports as a scan failure.\\\"\\n638:   [files]\\n639:   (into {} (map (fn [f] [f (when (.isFile (io/file f)) (slurp f))])) files))\\n640: \\n641: \\n642: (def current\\n643:   (delay (gate (read-sources (closure-files)) list-1 list-2)))\\n644: \\n645: \\n646: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n647: ;; Tests\\n648: ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n649: \\n650: (deftest closure-totals-are-the-design-totals\\n651:   (testing \\\"§3.1: 142 / 140 / 141 files, 133 shared\\\"\\n652:     (let [files (into {} (map (fn [l] [l (set (map :file (:files (committed-closure l))))]) lanes))]\\n653:       (is (= 142 (count (files :clj))))\\n654:       (is (= 140 (count (files :cljs))))\\n655:       (is (= 141 (count (files :cljd))))\\n656:       (is (= 133 (count (apply set/intersection (vals files)))))\\n657:       (doseq [l lanes]\\n658:         (is (= (count (files l)) (:total (committed-closure l))))\\n659:         (is (every? #(seq (:classes %)) (:files (committed-closure l))))))))\\n660: \\n661: \\n662: (deftest independent-traversal-agrees-with-the-committed-closure\\n663:   (doseq [l lanes]\\n664:     (testing (str \\\"lane \\\" l)\\n665:       (let [committed (set (map :file (:files (committed-closure l))))\\n666:             walked (traverse l)]\\n667:         (is (= #{} (set/difference committed walked)) \\\"committed, not walked\\\")\\n668:         (is (= #{} (set/difference walked committed)) \\\"walked, not committed\\\")))))\\n669: \\n670: \\n671: (deftest gate-passes-on-the-current-tree\\n672:   (let [r @current]\\n673:     (is (= 155 (count (closure-files))) \\\"the union of the three lanes\\\")\\n674:     (is (= (count (closure-files)) (:scanned r)))\\n675:     (is (= [] (:errors r)))\\n676:     (is (= [] (:arm-violations r)))\\n677:     (is (= [] (:effect-violations r)))\\n678:     (is (= :pass (:verdict r)))))\\n679: \\n680: \\n681: (deftest list-1-equals-the-observed-arms\\n682:   (testing \\\"every list-1 file is in the closure and still holds a host arm\\\"\\n683:     (let [observed (set (keep (fn [[f r]] (when (seq (:arms r)) f)) (:observed @current)))]\\n684:       (is (= (set (keys list-1)) observed)))))\\n685: \\n686: \\n687: (deftest list-2-equals-the-observed-calls\\n688:   (testing \\\"every permitted count is the observed count (no slack)\\\"\\n689:     (let [observed (into {} (keep (fn [[f r]]\\n690:                                     (when (seq (:effects r))\\n691:                                       [f (update-vals (:effects r) count)]))\\n692:                                   (:observed @current)))]\\n693:       (is (= list-2 observed)))))\\n694: \\n695: \\n696: (defn- outside\\n697:   \\\"The first closure .cljc file outside m with no arms and no effect calls.\\\"\\n698:   [m]\\n699:   (first (for [[f r] (:observed @current)\\n700:                :when (and (not (lane-specific? f)) (not (contains? m f))\\n701:                           (empty? (:arms r)) (empty? (:effects r)))]\\n702:            f)))\\n703: \\n704: \\n705: (deftest an-injected-host-arm-outside-list-1-fails-the-gate\\n706:   (let [target (outside list-1)\\n707:         sources (update (read-sources (closure-files)) target str\\n708:                         \\\"\\\\n(def injected #?(:clj (java.lang.Math/abs -1) :cljs 1))\\\\n\\\")\\n709:         r (gate sources list-1 list-2)]\\n710:     (is (some? target))\\n711:     (is (= :fail (:verdict r)))\\n712:     (is (= [target] (map :file (:arm-violations r))))\\n713:     (is (= [] (:effect-violations r)))))\\n714: \\n715: \\n716: (deftest an-injected-random-uuid-outside-list-2-fails-the-gate\\n717:   (let [target (outside list-2)\\n718:         sources (update (read-sources (closure-files)) target str\\n719:                         \\\"\\\\n(def injected (random-uuid))\\\\n\\\")\\n720:         r (gate sources list-1 list-2)]\\n721:     (is (some? target))\\n722:     (is (= :fail (:verdict r)))\\n723:     (is (= [{:file target :kind :random-uuid :count 1 :allowed 0}]\\n724:            (map #(dissoc % :lines) (:effect-violations r))))\\n725:     (is (= [] (:arm-violations r)))))\\n726: \\n727: \\n728: (deftest a-scan-failure-is-not-a-pass\\n729:   (testing \\\"zero files read\\\"\\n730:     (let [r (gate {} list-1 list-2)]\\n731:       (is (= :scan-failure (:verdict r)))\\n732:       (is (= 0 (:scanned r)))))\\n733:   (testing \\\"a closure file that cannot be read\\\"\\n734:     (let [r (gate (assoc (read-sources (closure-files)) \\\"src/cljc/no/such.cljc\\\" nil)\\n735:                   list-1 list-2)]\\n736:       (is (= :scan-failure (:verdict r)))\\n737:       (is (= [\\\"src/cljc/no/such.cljc\\\"] (map first (:errors r)))))))\\n738: \\n739: \\n740: (defn- sha-256\\n741:   [file]\\n742:   (let [d (java.security.MessageDigest/getInstance \\\"SHA-256\\\")]\\n743:     (apply str (map #(format \\\"%02x\\\" (bit-and % 0xff))\\n744:                     (.digest d (java.nio.file.Files/readAllBytes (.toPath (io/file file))))))))\\n745: \\n746: \\n747: (deftest corpus-bytes-match-the-frozen-hash-set\\n748:   (testing \\\"H0 (d): the Jing corpus and codec wire fixtures, byte-identical\\\"\\n749:     (let [{:keys [roots files]} (edn/read-string (slurp \\\"docs/design/host-boundary/corpus-sha256.edn\\\"))\\n750:           on-disk (into (sorted-set)\\n751:                         (for [r roots\\n752:                               f (file-seq (io/file r))\\n753:                               :when (.isFile ^java.io.File f)]\\n754:                           (str/replace (.getPath ^java.io.File f) \\\"\\\\\\\\\\\" \\\"/\\\")))]\\n755:       (is (= 18 (count files)))\\n756:       (is (= (set (keys files)) on-disk))\\n757:       (doseq [[f h] files]\\n758:         (is (= h (sha-256 f)) f)))))\\n759: \\n760: \\n761: (deftest exemptions-and-resolution\\n762:   (testing \\\"§3.3 patterns are exempt; a value arm is not\\\"\\n763:     (is (= [] (non-exempt-arms (read-forms \\\"(try 1 (catch #?(:clj Exception :cljs :default) e e))\\\"))))\\n764:     (is (= [] (non-exempt-arms (read-forms \\\"(ns a (:require #?(:clj [x :as y] :cljs [z :as y])))\\\"))))\\n765:     (is (= [] (non-exempt-arms (read-forms \\\"(def s #?(:clj (Object.) :cljs (js-obj)))\\\"))))\\n766:     (is (= 1 (count (non-exempt-arms (read-forms \\\"(def n #?(:clj 1 :cljs 2))\\\"))))))\\n767:   (testing \\\"locals, file defs and quoted forms are not core calls\\\"\\n768:     (is (= [] (effect-calls (read-forms \\\"(defn f [pr] (pr 1))\\\"))))\\n769:     (is (= [] (effect-calls (read-forms \\\"(let [gensym inc] (gensym 1))\\\"))))\\n770:     (is (= [] (effect-calls (read-forms \\\"(declare gensym) (gensym)\\\"))))\\n771:     (is (= [] (effect-calls (read-forms \\\"(def code '(println 1))\\\"))))\\n772:     (is (= [:random-uuid :print] (map first (effect-calls (read-forms \\\"(random-uuid) (println 1)\\\")))))))\"}]}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"tool\",\"messageId\":\"487004f7-2f79-428d-ace8-f35721c7e255\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"adversarial analysis of the gates:\\n\\n1. Exclusions are applied by reading forms ✓ (read-forms with :preserve, exclusions against ReaderConditional structures, not text). Skipping comments ✓.\\n\\n2. all-arms expansion in effect-calls: non-splicing rc at top level becomes (do arm1 arm2...) — walks all lanes' code ✓. In file-scope, ns-form uses splice-all ✓.\\n\\n3. Potential weakness: `effect-kind`'s `core` logic: `(and (contains? core-ns q) (or q core?))` — for unqualified symbols q is nil, contains? core-ns nil is true, (or nil core?) = core? (not shadowed) ✓. Qualified cljs.core/clojure.core also count. Qualified `js/console...` is handled. `str/includes? n \\\"SecureRandom\\\"` also matches names like `mySecureRandomThing` — over-matching is on the safe side (more detections → gated by list-2 ceilings, and list-2 = observed so no problem).\\n\\n4. Possibility of missing effect calls: symbols via refers — resolve-m handles refers for unqualified symbols; aliases for qualified. However, if a file requires [clojure.string :as str] and calls (str/...), no problem. If a file uses `println` via `:refer` from another ns… refers map handles it. If there's an unqualified call where the name is shadowed by a file's defs (e.g., the file defines its own `println`)? shadowed covers defs ✓.\\n\\n5. walk-fn arity tail parsing: heuristic; may mis-parse exotic fn forms and miss bindings → false positive (extra detections) rather than misses… no wait, missing bindings means a local named `pr` gets counted as core's print → over-count → should fail on list-2 equivalence test (list-2-equals-the-observed-calls asserts exact match with observed counts). Current tree passes with exact counts, so on today's tree resolution is validated. Possibility of under-count: quoted forms are skipped ✓ ('quote is skipped), but syntax-quote (`) is NOT skipped! (#{'quote 'comment 'ns} h) — what about the `` ` `` form? Syntax-quote reads as a seq whose head is…? Does tools.reader return a syntax-quote as a form with `clojure.core/seq`? Actually, syntax-quote expansion happens at read time: `(foo)` reads as (clojure.core/seq (clojure.core/concat ...)) — those contain symbols like 'foo as quoted values… a println inside a syntax-quoted form appears as a quoted symbol within the concat list — a bare symbol within a data list. walk visits symbols anywhere within a seq, so a syntax-quoted `(println 1)` would count as a call. This is a false positive (over-count), in the fail-closed direction; on today's tree the observed counts match the design. No problem — the gate can only over-detect, never under-detect… except: symbols inside vectors within syntax-quote are also walked. OK.\\n\\nDirection of real under-count risk: `walk` skips the entire 'ns form for effects (no problem, ns doesn't contain calls), skips quote/comment. What about method calls like `.println`? Not a core call. `Thread/sleep` is covered by qualified. `(System/currentTimeMillis)` is also covered. `js/Date.now` — does `(= q \\\"js\\\") (str/starts-with? n \\\"Date\\\")` cover js/Date.now? Symbol js/Date.now has name \\\"Date.now\\\", starts-with \\\"Date\\\" ✓.\\n\\n6. Negative tests: NEG1 appends an rc with different arms (:clj (java.lang.Math/abs -1) :cljs 1) — not hint-only (arms differ), not an exclusion target → arm violation exactly 1; asserts effect violations 0 — `(java.lang.Math/abs -1)` is not an effect kind ✓. NEG2 `(random-uuid)` → exactly 1 effect violation allowed 0; arm violations 0 ✓. Targets are programmatically chosen from files with no arms/effects outside the list — in memory only, `(update (read-sources ...) target str ...)` — the actual sources on disk are unmodified ✓. Both assert exact violation lists. Genuine tests.\\n\\n7. Scan failures: empty {} → :scan-failure (empty? scanned) ✓; nil text → error \\\"cannot read file\\\" → scan-failure with filename specified ✓. Distinguished from pass ✓.\\n\\n8. Honesty of list-1: the 16 :h0-unlisted entries each have line comments; the test `list-1-equals-the-observed-arms` asserts set equality between list-1 keys and observed arm files — i.e., list-1 cannot contain stale entries nor miss files with arms. Does this weaken the freeze? The gate's promise (§8.1) is \\\"no non-excluded arms outside list 1\\\" — adding 16 files to list 1 means their existing arms are grandfathered in, and new arms in those files are permitted (because the files are on list 1)! Wait — arm violations are per-file, not per-line: a file on list 1 can later gain new non-excluded arms without failing. That's also the design's granularity (\\\"files permitted to have non-excluded host arms\\\") — list 1 is file-granular by design. Therefore :h0-unlisted files are permitted at the design's own granularity; but the design says list 1 \\\"must match the H0 baseline per category…bidirectional differences are H0 findings to be resolved before H1\\\". The author recorded F1 with bidirectional diffs and tagged 16 as :h0-unlisted to keep the gate green. Is that acceptable H0 behavior? The design says findings should be resolved before H1, and the author escalated to the Architect. The gate still detects new arms in files not on the list, and list-2 caps effect counts per file+kind (effect ceiling is count-granular, so new random-uuids in listed files still fail). For arms, listed files are not line-capped — a design-inherent property. My judgment: acceptable as H0 with F1 explicitly unresolved before H1 (author's own gating). However, the 16 :h0-unlisted files constitute a substantive widening beyond §8.1's baseline — flag for Architect; the report did so.\\n\\nHmm, but a subtle point: is there a risk that these 16 arms should have been excluded (i.e., is the exclusion logic too narrow)? Example: :78 instance? Long/Double is a substantive host arm. No problem.\\n\\n9. Independence of walk B: uses tools.reader + its own select-arms/libspec-deps; shares nothing with tools.namespace (closure.clj uses parse/read-ns-decl + deps-from-ns-decl). The resolution rule (lane-file) is duplicated but that's a design-fixed rule — acceptable, disclosed. Does walk B handle #?@ within ns? select-arms splices ✓ — precisely the r3 defect class. libspec-deps: :as-alias only (no :as/:refer etc.) → not a dep ✓; string libspecs → [] ✓; prefix lists handled ✓. Independence claim holds.\\n\\n10. Closure tool under-inclusion: read-ns-decl with tools.reader's :read-cond :allow handles splicing natively ✓. strip-nils: postwalk removes nils from vectors/lists within ns decls — wait, danger: strip-nils removes nil from any vector in the ns form… `#?(:cljd nil :clj [x])` reads as nil under cljd features. But legitimately… nil cannot be a libspec so removal is safe. But could it remove nils from metadata or change semantics? Only ns decls, only nil removal — matches the compiler (which ignores nil libspecs). OK. However: on the :cljd lane, features #{:cljd :clj} — `#?(:cljd nil :clj [x])` picks the :cljd arm = nil → stripped → dep dropped. Correct (the cljd compiler does the same).\\n\\nAlso read-ns-decl reads the first form that looks like an ns decl; if a file has a shebang or comment… no problem.\\n\\n11. Corpus: 18 files, tests assert exact set and digests ✓, bb script regenerates/checks ✓. SHA-256 vs BLAKE3 rule disclosed.\\n\\nNext (d) self-verify F2: grep random-uuid in the worktree's src/cljc (should be 27 lines in src/cljc; 21 in closures), grep for things that require dao.await / yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.\\n\\n(e) Scope: confirm deps.edn/bb.edn in the host-h0 worktree are unmodified (no :hb alias), nothing else under src/. Quick grep. Also confirm closure output exists.\\n\\nLet me run these greps:\\n- grep \\\"random-uuid\\\" in host-h0/src/cljc → count lines.\\n- grep \\\"dao.await\\\\|dao\\\\.await\\\" requires in src → files that require it.\\n- grep \\\":hb\\\" in host-h0's deps.edn/bb.edn → should not exist.\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Now I'll verify F2 myself and check scope (deps.edn/bb.edn untouched, requirers of dao.await).\\n\\n\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_3d4529fc4d8c40ae928455f9\",\"name\":\"grep\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"random-uuid\",\"path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/cljc\",\"output_mode\":\"count\"}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_5931d93d95524c52945084e7\",\"name\":\"grep\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"\\\\[dao\\\\.await|\\\\[yin\\\\.vm\\\\.ffi\\\\.remote-serve|dao\\\\.await\\\\]|remote-serve\\\\]|:as await|require.*await\",\"path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src\",\"output_mode\":\"content\",\"-n\":true}},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_7a4f138cb8da471cb2d97a75\",\"name\":\"grep\",\"input\":{\"pattern\":\"host_boundary|host-bound