t.cljc:220:     {:type :dao.await/result\\n.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/responder.cljc:1:(ns yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.responder\\n.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve.cljc:41:   (`yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.holder`) reads its grant there through a\\n.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/cljc/yin/vm/ffi/remote_serve/holder.cljc:1:(ns yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve.holder\"}]},{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_f41edb873ca84959b2a326da\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"No matches found\"}]}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"tool\",\"messageId\":\"3d50cfc8-fc44-404c-ad29-33eebc34e410\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Confirmed: within src/cljc, no file requires `dao.await` (there's no `[dao.await` require anywhere), and the only things requiring `yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve` are its own holder/responder sub-namespaces, but those themselves aren't required by anyone within src (grepping for remote-serve.holder/responder only hits their own ns declarations). Also, closure-clj.edn doesn't include any await/remote-serve entries. F2's calculation holds: 27 total within src/cljc − terminal.cljc 1 (out of scope per design) = 26 within the design's closure assertion; 26 − 5 (await 2 + remote_serve 3, both unreachable) = 21 within the actually adopted closure. The author honestly reported this discrepancy rather than fudging the numbers. ✓\\n\\nWait — design §3.2 states \\\"27 lines within src/cljc, 26 within the adopted closure; the 27th is dao/postgraphics/terminal.cljc\\\". My grep: 27 hits, including terminal (1). So the design counts 26 including await (2) + remote_serve (3). The author says these 5 are unreachable from yin.repl.main → within the adopted closure it's 21. Verified that they are actually unreachable: nothing requires dao.await; remote-serve is only required by holder/responder, and nothing requires those. ✓ Honest.\\n\\nScope (e): no host-boundary alias in deps.edn, no gate/probe tasks in bb.edn (the test:cljd hit is a pre-existing docstring). Only src/dev/host_boundary under src/. Files: closure output exists (grep for closure-clj.edn works). The tool is run via inline -Sdeps: acceptable? This avoids modifying deps.edn (broad changes), the command is documented in the docstring; the impact on test:changed is broad (exit 2), and the author has disclosed it. Acceptable at H0; if the tool becomes permanent, a proper alias might be preferable — info.\\n\\nRemaining spot checks: do the closure's edn files show a total of 142/140/141? The orchestrator re-ran --check rc 0 with these counts; confirmed that closure-clj.edn exists. Sufficient. Also spot-check :h0-unlisted — e.g., the arm at dao/space/index.cljc:78. Quick grep for the #? at line 78.\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"One spot-check of an `:h0-unlisted` claim, then I'll write the verdict.\\n\\n\"},{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"call_a02a4cb5d7264279b125f0a6\",\"name\":\"read_file\",\"input\":{\"file_path\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/.claude/worktrees/host-h0/src/cljc/dao/space/index.cljc\",\"offset\":74,\"limit\":10}}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"model\",\"createdAt\":1792522821965,\"messageId\":\"b7277a13-70d5-4e51-beb2-f18eebb8b358\"}},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"tool_use_id\":\"call_a02a4cb5d7264279b125f0a6\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Read 1/1 file, 10 lines\\nNote: showing lines 74-83. More of the file remains. Use offset=84 to continue.\\n74:    JVM and ClojureScript two non-NaN doubles (both compare exactly, with\\n75:    0.0 and -0.0 equal). Dart's double compareTo orders -0.0 below 0.0, so\\n76:    Dart takes the fast path for ints only.\\\"\\n77:   [a b]\\n78:   (if #?(:cljd (and (dart/is? a int) (dart/is? b int))\\n79:          :clj (or (and (instance? Long a) (instance? Long b))\\n80:                   (and (instance? Double a) (instance? Double b)\\n81:                        (not (Double/isNaN ^Double a)) (not (Double/isNaN ^Double b))))\\n82:          :cljs (and (number? a) (number? b)\\n83:                     (not (js/isNaN a)) (not (js/isNaN b))))\"}]}],\"meta\":{\"source\":\"tool\",\"messageId\":\"8951e407-a8f1-444f-80ec-a3e853c31988\"}},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"Confirmed: the actual host arm on line 78 (instance? Long/Double, js/isNaN, dart/is?) matches the :h0-unlisted table entry exactly. Not exempt (the arms differ, it's not a hint, and it's not a catch either).\\n\\nNow going to write the review. Under 700 words. Verdict: SIGNED OFF (F1 was escalated by design; the author's own gate conditions H1 on resolving F1). Or SIGNED OFF WITH CHANGES? The :h0-unlisted mechanism makes the gate green even though §8.1 states that list 1 must match the baseline, and \\\"any difference in either direction is an H0 finding that should be resolved before H1.\\\" The author recorded this and deferred it to the architect—the design's own process. The gate still freezes the tree (new arms outside the list will fail; list 2 is a count ceiling everywhere). My take is SIGNED OFF, with an explicit condition being that F1 must be resolved before H1 (which the design already requires). Findings table: some info items.\\n\\nFindings:\\n- M1 (low/info): due to list 1's file granularity, the 16 :h0-unlisted files can have new non-exempt arms added without the gate failing (only the effect count is ceiling'd). This is inherent to the file-granularity list 1 in §8.1, but it's the :h0-unlisted batch that broadens that allowance. F1 must be resolved before H1 (design's own rule; author also complies). Optionally: record the arm line numbers for :h0-unlisted files and fail on new lines—but that exceeds the design's granularity, so I'll just recommend it to the architect.\\n- M2 info: the tool's location deviates from §8's literal `dev/host_boundary/` → src/dev/host_boundary is legitimate and disclosed. It runs via an inline -Sdeps alias (acceptable: no edits to deps.edn, and the wide-change exit 2 of test:changed is disclosed). Recommend adding a proper alias if the tool becomes permanent from H1 onward.\\n- M3 info: the syntax-quote (`) form is not skipped in the effect-calls walk (only 'quote and comment are)—symbols inside syntax-quoted data end up being counted. The direction is over-counting (fail-closed), and list-2-equals-observed pins the current tree. Mention as a note.\\n- M4 info: the SHA-256 vs BLAKE3 choice is disclosed.\\n\\nChecks (a)–(e) summary and evidence. Things I could not verify: test execution (counts 10/65), --check rc 0, lane counts (the author's quick-tier runs; orchestrator only partially), target/h0 logs, r3 reviewer's totals, whether tools.namespace 1.5.0's deps-from-ns-decl actually excludes :as-alias/string libspecs (from library knowledge; traversal B agrees empirically, and its libspec-deps explicitly handles both—this agreement is cross-validated).\\n\\nWord budget: target around 650 words.\\n\",\"signature\":\"\"},{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Created-GMT: 2026-10-20 18:56:02 GMT\\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-21 01:56:02 +07\\nCoding-Agent: cmd\\nSession-ID: 61966f9d-4875-4b42-9545-b0dc8a2c9891\\n# Review: host-boundary H0 (closure tool, gate, corpus hashes)\\nRole: Reviewer (read-only) | Model: qwen/qwen3.8-max\\n\\n## Verdict: SIGNED OFF\\n\\nCondition the design itself imposes: F1 (list 1 vs §8.1 baseline) must be resolved by the Architect before H1; the author gated exactly that way.\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n| id | sev | file:line | evidence | correction |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| M1 | low | gate_test.clj:515-531 | List 1 is file-granular (§8.1's own design), so the 16 `:h0-unlisted` files may gain NEW non-exempt arms without failing the gate; only effect counts have ceilings. Each entry is line-cited (I verified `dao/space/index.cljc:78` - a genuine `instance? Long/Double`/`js/isNaN`/`dart/is?` arm, non-exempt), and F1 is escalated, not buried. | Acceptable for H0; when the Architect categories the 16, consider line-level pins for any file kept on the list. |\\n| M2 | info | closure.clj ns doc; report §\\\"Location\\\" | Tool lives at `src/dev/host_boundary/` (repo convention; §8's literal `dev/` exists nowhere) and runs via inline `-Sdeps`, so deps.edn/bb.edn stay untouched; `bb test:changed` exits 2 (wide), disclosed. | Fine now; add a real alias if the tool persists past H1. |\\n| M3 | info | gate_test.clj:393 | Only `'quote`/`comment`/`ns` are skipped; syntax-quoted data would count its symbols as calls. Direction is over-counting (fail-closed), and `list-2-equals-the-observed-calls` pins today's tree exactly, so no slack exists. | Note for H2's library mode. |\\n\\n## Checks\\n\\n- (a) **Closure tool faithful**: lane features `#{:clj}/#{:cljs}/#{:cljd :clj}`, first-arm-wins via tools.reader; resolution `src/<lane>` then `src/cljc` exactly as §3.1; ns-name/file mismatch throws (fail-closed). `#?@` is handled natively by `read-ns-decl` with `:read-cond :allow` - the r3 defect class (dropped spliced requires, 141/140/139) cannot recur; `strip-nils` for `#?(:cljd nil :clj [...])` matches compiler behaviour. **Traversal B is genuinely independent**: own tools.reader `:preserve` read, own `select-arms` (splices `#?@` itself), own `libspec-deps` (`:as-alias`-only and string libspecs excluded explicitly); it shares only the design-fixed resolution rule, as disclosed. Agreement is asserted file-by-file both directions (`set/difference` both ways), not by counts - and B's independent handling of `:as-alias`/strings cross-validates tools.namespace's. Under-inclusion would show as B⊄A; over-inclusion as A⊄B; both are tested.\\n- (b) **Gate**: exemptions are applied to read `ReaderConditional` forms with ancestor context (never text); comments skipped; lane-specific files count as one whole-file arm. NEG1/NEG2 are in-memory (`update` on a slurped copy; disk untouched), target chosen programmatically, and each asserts the EXACT violation list plus zero of the other kind - they fail for the right reason only. Zero files and nil-text both give `:scan-failure` with the file named, distinct from `:pass`. `list-1-equals-the-observed-arms` and `list-2-equals-the-observed-calls` assert set/map equality with observations, so no stale entry and no count slack. The `:h0-unlisted` device keeps the gate green on today's tree while still catching any new arm outside list 1 - acceptable H0 behaviour given F1 is escalated (see M1).\\n- (c) **Corpus**: 18 files (6 + 12), `bb ... corpus_hashes.clj [--check]` regenerates/checks, and `corpus-bytes-match-the-frozen-hash-set` asserts both the exact file set and every digest on the JVM lane. SHA-256-vs-BLAKE3 choice disclosed with rationale.\\n- (d) **Findings honest - F2 verified myself**: `random-uuid` occurs exactly 27 times in `src/cljc`; `dao/await.cljc` (2) has no requirer anywhere in `src`, and `yin.vm.ffi.remote-serve` (3) is required only by its own holder/responder, which nothing requires; neither appears in `closure-clj.edn`. 27 − 1 (terminal, design's own exclusion) − 5 = 21, matching list 2's sum. The author reported the design mismatch instead of tuning the tool; F1/F3/F4 are likewise recorded with line cites and left for the Architect (F4's `antlr/repl.cljc:71` quoted-program exclusion is consistent with the gate's quote handling, unit-tested at gate_test.clj:771).\\n- (e) **Scope clean**: no `:hb`/host-boundary additions in deps.edn or bb.edn; nothing under `src/clj{,c,s,d}` touched (the change adds only `src/dev/host_boundary/`, `test/dao/host/`, `docs/design/host-boundary/`); no codec-track, jolt or design-doc edits.\\n\\n## Could not verify\\n\\n- Executing anything: the 10-test/65-assertion run, `--check` rc 0, the 142/140/141/133 totals and the quick-tier lane counts (4121→4131 JVM; Node/Dart single-run argument is sound but unrerun) rest on the orchestrator's re-runs and author logs under gitignored `target/h0/`.\\n- tools.namespace 1.5.