 compile, check `mise ls flutter` first). Tri-host quick tier verified green on 2026-10-29 (see Measured times). |\n443:that is behind origin (shiva: 45 commits behind on 2026-10-11) and belongs to its\n456:ssh shiva.stigmergy.systems 'set -e; mkdir -p ~/ci; cd ~/workspace/datomworld;\n474:export PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"   # mise: ~/.local/bin on shiva, /snap/bin on jupiter\n491:avoidable\"). On shiva (24 cores) and jupiter (48) the cores are not the limit, so\n505:  `min(8, cores)` Flutter processes and shares the host's Flutter cache.\n510:The first run on shiva (2026-10-11) overlapped JVM and Dart in one clone before\n521:(strictly serial), which on jupiter makes the full ~179-namespace lane a\n528:  sit far inside jupiter's 48 cores / 62 GB and shiva's 24 / 62;\n534:- **parallel is unproven until checked once**: the recorded lane evidence\n538:  attribute before its evidence is trusted. Until that first comparison\n608:- Both hosts run other work (a QEMU guest and rustdesk on shiva); idle load is\n611:### The nightly full suite and the branch-testing rule (2026-10-30 owner ruling)\n616:changes\" — and, clarifying the nightly's target: \"it should not be for\n617:only a worktree/branch. the nightly complete test should be for master.\"\n621:- **The nightly full suite runs MASTER ONLY** (`~/ci/nightly-full.sh` on\n622:  shiva, tmux session `nightly`, scheduled 03:00 daily through the\n634:  to master is what puts it under the nightly.\n637:sign-off; the nightly catches what the subset could not see, and a red\n638:nightly owns the follow-up.\n651:First full tri-host verification of jupiter. Prerequisites (npm ci, Node REPL,\n656:laptop — route Node lanes to the laptop or shiva); **Dart quick tier\n659:taken-port/bind-failed signature recorded above). Routing summary: jupiter\n673:### Remote agent execution (delegate CLIs on shiva and jupiter)\n710:Known state: `claude` and `codex` verified working on shiva (2026-10-24, the\n713:the full tri-host suite (jupiter verified 2026-10-29 — see Measured times;\n     1\t(ns cljd-agg\n     2\t  \"Dart test runner that aggregates the generated test files.\n     3\t\n     4\t   `flutter test` loads every generated *_test.dart separately (about 7.5 s\n     5\t   each). This runner compiles the test namespaces through the cljd tool,\n     6\t   groups the generated files into a few shard files that import them and call\n     7\t   each `main`, and runs `flutter test` on the shards only. Shards live under\n     8\t   build/, never under test/, so a plain `cljd test` never runs them twice.\n     9\t\n    10\t   Run with babashka:\n    11\t     bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj [--slow-only | --slow-regex | --only NS,NS...]\n    12\t   --slow-only restricts the run to the namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard.\n    13\t   A namespace in that set with no generated Dart file is fatal.\n    14\t   --only compiles and runs only the given test namespaces (bb test:changed,\n    15\t   bb test:sub); one with no generated Dart file is fatal too, EXCEPT a\n    16\t   JVM-only namespace: one whose every deftest sits behind a reader\n    17\t   conditional that excludes ClojureDart (for example\n    18\t   dao.data.sorted-user-type-test). The cljd tool compiles such a namespace as\n    19\t   a plain library (lib/cljd-out/<ns>.dart exists) and emits no test file;\n    20\t   that is reported and skipped, never fatal. A namespace that produced\n    21\t   neither file is still fatal.\n    22\t   --slow-regex prints, for bb.edn, an anchored alternation of those\n    23\t   namespaces with its dots already escaped for embedding in an EDN string\n    24\t   (shadow-cljs --config-merge); it is not a ready-to-use regex. It exits 1\n    25\t   when no namespace uses the guard, so a slow lane cannot be vacuous.\n    26\t   DATOM_SLOW_TESTS is inherited from the environment.\"\n    27\t  (:require\n    28\t    [babashka.fs :as fs]\n    29\t    [babashka.process :as p]\n    30\t    [clojure.string :as str]))\n    31\t\n    32\t\n    33\t(def test-root \"test\")\n    34\t(def out-root \"test/cljd-out\")\n    35\t(def shard-dir \"build/cljd-agg\")\n    36\t(def max-shards 8)\n    37\t\n    38\t\n    39\t(defn- ns-of\n    40\t  \"The namespace declared by the first ns form of `file`.\"\n    41\t  [file]\n    42\t  (second (re-find #\"\\(ns\\s+\\^?(?:\\{[^}]*\\}\\s+)?([^\\s\\)]+)\" (slurp file))))\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\t(defn- source-files\n    46\t  []\n    47\t  (->> (file-seq (fs/file test-root))\n    48\t       (filter #(re-find #\"_test\\.clj[cd]$\" (str %)))\n    49\t       (remove #(str/includes? (str %) \"cljd-out\"))\n    50\t       (map str)\n    51\t       sort))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn- test-namespaces\n    55\t  \"Distinct: a namespace with both a .cljc and a .cljd source (for example\n    56\t   dao.stream.cbor-test) has one generated Dart file, which must run once.\"\n    57\t  []\n    58\t  (distinct (keep ns-of (source-files))))\n    59\t\n    60\t\n    61\t(defn- slow-namespaces\n    62\t  \"Namespaces whose source uses dao.test-slow/guard, derived from the tree.\"\n    63\t  []\n    64\t  (->> (source-files)\n    65\t       (filter #(re-find #\"slow/guard\" (slurp %)))\n    66\t       (keep ns-of)\n    67\t       distinct\n    68\t       sort))\n    69\t\n    70\t\n    71\t(defn- dart-file\n    72\t  \"Generated file path for namespace `ns-name`.\"\n    73\t  [ns-name]\n    74\t  (str out-root \"/\" (str/replace ns-name \".\" \"/\") \"_test.dart\"))\n    75\t\n    76\t\n    77\t(defn- lib-file\n    78\t  \"Library file the cljd tool writes for a namespace with no Dart tests.\"\n    79\t  [ns-name]\n    80\t  (str \"lib/cljd-out/\" (str/replace ns-name \".\" \"/\") \".dart\"))\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(defn jvm-only?\n    84\t  \"True when `ns-name` compiled to a library but produced no Dart test file:\n    85\t   it has no ClojureDart tests (a JVM-only namespace), as opposed to not\n    86\t   having compiled at all.\"\n    87\t  [ns-name]\n    88\t  (and (not (fs/exists? (dart-file ns-name)))\n    89\t       (fs/exists? (lib-file ns-name))))\n    90\t\n    91\t\n    92\t(defn- run!*\n    93\t  [& args]\n    94\t  (let [{:keys [exit]} (apply p/shell {:continue true} args)]\n    95\t    exit))\n    96\t\n    97\t\n    98\t(defn compile-tests\n    99\t  \"Compile every test namespace through the cljd tool.\"\n   100\t  [namespaces]\n   101\t  (let [exit (apply run!* \"clojure\" \"-M:clojuredart:cljd\" \"compile\"\n   102\t                    namespaces)]\n   103\t    (when-not (zero? exit)\n   104\t      (println \"cljd compile failed, exit\" exit)\n   105\t      (System/exit exit))))\n   106\t\n   107\t\n   108\t(defn shard\n   109\t  \"Greedy balanced partition of `files` into `n` groups by file size.\n   110\t   Deterministic: ties are broken by path.\"\n   111\t  [files n]\n   112\t  (let [sized (sort-by (juxt (comp - fs/size) identity) files)\n   113\t        init  (vec (repeat n {:size 0 :files []}))]\n   114\t    (->> sized\n   115\t         (reduce (fn [shards f]\n   116\t                   (let [i (first (first (sort-by\n   117\t                                           (juxt (comp :size second) first)\n   118\t                                           (map-indexed vector shards))))]\n   119\t                     (-> shards\n   120\t                         (update-in [i :size] + (fs/size f))\n   121\t                         (update-in [i :files] conj f))))\n   122\t                 init)\n   123\t         (map (comp sort :files))\n   124\t         (remove empty?))))\n   125\t\n   126\t\n   127\t(defn- shard-source\n   128\t  \"Dart source of an aggregator importing `files` and calling each main.\n   129\t   Imports are relative to `shard-dir`.\"\n   130\t  [files shard-dir]\n   131\t  (let [rel (fn [f]\n   132\t              (str (fs/relativize (fs/absolutize shard-dir)\n   133\t                                  (fs/absolutize f))))]\n   134\t    (str \"// Generated by src/dev/cljd_agg.clj; do not edit.\\n\"\n   135\t         (apply str\n   136\t                (map-indexed (fn [i f]\n   137\t                               (str \"import '\" (rel f) \"' as m\" i \";\\n\"))\n   138\t                             files))\n   139\t         \"\\nvoid main() {\\n\"\n   140\t         (apply str\n   141\t                (map-indexed (fn [i _] (str \"  m\" i \".main();\\n\")) files))\n   142\t         \"}\\n\")))\n   143\t\n   144\t\n   145\t(defn write-shards!\n   146\t  \"Emit the aggregator files under `shard-dir` (build/cljd-agg by default;\n   147\t   --shard-dir overrides, which lets dart-shard.sh run one directory per\n   148\t   subsystem as parallel flutter processes). Returns the shard paths.\"\n   149\t  ([files] (write-shards! files shard-dir))\n   150\t  ([files shard-dir]\n   151\t   (fs/delete-tree shard-dir)\n   152\t   (fs/create-dirs shard-dir)\n   153\t   (let [n (min max-shards\n   154\t                (.availableProcessors (Runtime/getRuntime))\n   155\t                (count files))]\n   156\t     (vec (map-indexed\n   157\t            (fn [i group]\n   158\t              (let [path (format \"%s/shard_%d_test.dart\" shard-dir i)]\n   159\t                (spit path (shard-source group shard-dir))\n   160\t                path))\n   161\t            (shard files n))))))\n   162\t\n   163\t\n   164\t(defn -main\n   165\t  [& args]\n   166\t  (when (some #{\"--slow-regex\"} args)\n   167\t    (when (empty? (slow-namespaces))\n   168\t      (println \"No namespace uses dao.test-slow/guard.\")\n   169\t      (System/exit 1))\n   170\t    (println (str \"^(\" (str/join \"|\" (map #(str/replace % \".\" \"\\\\\\\\.\")\n   171\t                                          (slow-namespaces)))\n   172\t                  \")$\"))\n   173\t    (System/exit 0))\n   174\t  (let [slow-only? (some #{\"--slow-only\"} args)\n   175\t        only       (when (some #{\"--only\"} args)\n   176\t                     (let [v (second (drop-while #(not= \"--only\" %) args))]\n   177\t                       (vec (remove str/blank? (str/split (str v) #\",\")))))\n   178\t        shard-dir  (or (when (some #{\"--shard-dir\"} args)\n   179\t                         (second (drop-while #(not= \"--shard-dir\" %) args)))\n   180\t                       shard-dir)\n   181\t        no-compile? (some #{\"--no-compile\"} args)\n   182\t        no-run?    (some #{\"--no-run\"} args)\n   183\t        wanted     (cond only only\n   184\t                         slow-only? (slow-namespaces)\n   185\t                         :else (test-namespaces))]\n   186\t    (when (empty? wanted)\n   187\t      (println \"No test namespaces selected.\")\n   188\t      (System/exit 1))\n   189\t    (when-not no-compile?\n   190\t      (compile-tests (or only (test-namespaces))))\n   191\t    (let [files (filter fs/exists? (map dart-file wanted))\n   192\t          missing (remove (comp fs/exists? dart-file) wanted)]\n   193\t      (when (seq missing)\n   194\t        (let [jvm-only (if (and only (not slow-only?))\n   195\t                         (filter jvm-only? missing)\n   196\t                         [])\n   197\t              fatal (remove (set jvm-only) missing)]\n   198\t          (when (seq jvm-only)\n   199\t            (println \"JVM-only namespaces (compiled, no Dart tests; skipped):\"\n   200\t                     (str/join \", \" jvm-only)))\n   201\t          (when (seq fatal)\n   202\t            (println \"No generated Dart test for:\" (str/join \", \" fatal))\n   203\t            (when (or slow-only? only)\n   204\t              (System/exit 1)))))\n   205\t      (when (empty? files)\n   206\t        (println \"No generated test files found.\")\n   207\t        (System/exit 1))\n   208\t      (let [shards (write-shards! files shard-dir)]\n   209\t        (if no-run?\n   210\t          (do (println (format \"Emitted %d test files in %d shards under %s\"\n   211\t                               (count files) (count shards) shard-dir))\n   212\t              (System/exit 0))\n   213\t          (do (println (format \"Running %d test files in %d shards\"\n   214\t                               (count files) (count shards)))\n   215\t              (let [exit (try (apply run!* \"flutter\" \"test\"\n   216\t                                     \"--concurrency\" (str (count shards))\n   217\t                                     shards)\n   218\t                              (finally (fs/delete-tree shard-dir)))]\n   219\t                (System/exit exit))))))))\n   220\t\n   221\t\n   222\t(when (= *file* (System/getProperty \"babashka.file\"))\n   223\t  (apply -main *command-line-args*))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
