{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"ssh -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=10 -o StrictHostKeyChecking=yes shiva.stigmergy.systems 'ls -l ~/ci; cat ~/ci/node-shard.sh ~/ci/dart-shard.sh ~/ci/nightly-full.sh'\"","aggregated_output":"ssh: Could not resolve hostname shiva.stigmergy.systems: nodename nor servname provided, or not known\r\n","exit_code":255,"status":"failed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/agents/build-n-test.md | sed -n '431,670p'; nl -ba deps.edn | sed -n '1,220p'; nl -ba bb.edn | sed -n '225,325p'\"","aggregated_output":"   431\t## Remote test servers: shiva and jupiter\n   432\t\n   433\tTwo Linux x86_64 servers run the full suite faster than a laptop. Both are\n   434\treached over SSH as `sto` with key authentication, and both have `mise`, `tmux`\n   435\tand `git`.\n   436\t\n   437\t| Host | Cores / RAM | Toolchain state (server snapshot checked 2026-10-11; repo selection comes from `mise.toml`) |\n   438\t|---|---|---|\n   439\t| `shiva.stigmergy.systems` | 24 / 62 GB | Server snapshot: java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.1. The repo's `mise.toml` selects Flutter `latest` on beta, not a fixed version. Activate the repo toolchain before running any lane. |\n   440\t| `jupiter.stigmergy.systems` | 48 / 62 GB | Server snapshot (rechecked 2026-10-29): java 21, clojure 1.12.4.1602, node 25.6.1, babashka, cljstyle, zprint, flutter 3.47.8 (the stale hand-symlinked 3.41.9 was replaced via `mise install flutter@3.47.8` after it failed to compile `dart:ui`-using cljd namespaces; if the Dart lane dies in the cljd compile, check `mise ls flutter` first). Tri-host quick tier verified green on 2026-10-29 (see Measured times). |\n   441\t\n   442\t**Never test in `~/workspace/datomworld` on either host.** It is a working copy\n   443\tthat is behind origin (shiva: 45 commits behind on 2026-10-11) and belongs to its\n   444\towner. Use a scratch clone under `~/ci/` and leave the working copy alone.\n   445\t\n   446\t### Get the code there: push to origin, never rsync\n   447\t\n   448\tRsyncing a worktree over the WAN ran at about 150 KB/s (576 MB of tracked files\n   449\twould take about an hour), and an unanchored `--exclude build` also dropped source\n   450\tdirectories named `build`, `out` and `target`. Both hosts reach GitHub, so push the\n   451\tbranch from the laptop (a feature branch, never master), make one scratch clone on\n   452\tthe host from its existing checkout (a local clone takes seconds), and fetch:\n   453\t\n   454\t```sh\n   455\t# once per host: a separate scratch clone, not the working copy\n   456\tssh shiva.stigmergy.systems 'set -e; mkdir -p ~/ci; cd ~/workspace/datomworld;\n   457\t  URL=$(git remote get-url origin);\n   458\t  git clone -q --no-checkout ~/workspace/datomworld ~/ci/datomworld-<name>;\n   459\t  cd ~/ci/datomworld-<name>; git remote set-url origin \"$URL\";\n   460\t  git fetch -q origin; git checkout -q --detach origin/<branch>'\n   461\t```\n   462\t\n   463\tTo test another branch later, fetch and check it out in the scratch clone with\n   464\t`git fetch origin` then `git checkout --detach origin/<branch>`. A branch that\n   465\twas never pushed cannot be tested remotely.\n   466\t\n   467\t### Activate the toolchain in the right order\n   468\t\n   469\tA non-interactive `ssh host cmd` does not load the shell profile, so `mise` and its\n   470\ttools are not on PATH. In a script, do this in exactly this order, after the `cd`\n   471\tinto the clone:\n   472\t\n   473\t```sh\n   474\texport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"   # mise: ~/.local/bin on shiva, /snap/bin on jupiter\n   475\tcd ~/ci/datomworld-<name>\n   476\tmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1                       # trust is per path; a fresh clone is untrusted\n   477\tmise install                                    # install versions selected by this checkout's mise.toml\n   478\teval \"$(mise env -s bash)\"                       # puts the repo-selected tools on PATH\n   479\tmise current flutter                            # verify the selected Flutter version\n   480\t```\n   481\t\n   482\tActivating mise before the `cd` and `mise trust` leaves the repo-selected tools\n   483\t(flutter in particular) off PATH: the Dart lane then dies in seconds with \"Can't\n   484\tfind flutter on PATH\", and so does `bb build:yin-repl-peer`.\n   485\t\n   486\t### Which lanes may overlap (reconciling the one-lane-set rule)\n   487\t\n   488\t\"One lane set at a time\" and \"one Dart lane at a time\" are per-machine rules about\n   489\tCPU: they exist because a laptop has 8 cores. They are not a rule about repos.\n   490\t`test.subsystems.md` section 5 item 6 says the same (\"on one machine where\n   491\tavoidable\"). On shiva (24 cores) and jupiter (48) the cores are not the limit, so\n   492\tlanes may overlap, with these limits:\n   493\t\n   494\t- **JVM and Dart lanes must not share one clone.** `src/dev/affected.clj`\n   495\t  (`serialized-pairs`, the `[:clj :cljd]` pair) serializes them whenever a JVM test\n   496\t  runs the cljd compiler, and some do (`yin.repl.build-test`,\n   497\t  `yin.vm.linker.cross-host-transfer-test`, `dao.stream.ws-project-cross-jvm-test`);\n   498\t  the compiler writes the clone's `lib/cljd-out` and `build/`. A second scratch clone\n   499\t  gives the Dart lane its own copies, so the two lanes then overlap safely. This is\n   500\t  by the design's own reasoning (\"each worktree owns its own `cljd-out`\"), not yet\n   501\t  verified by a measured run.\n   502\t- **JVM and Node may share a clone.** Node writes `target/` and `.shadow-cljs/`; the\n   503\t  JVM lane only reads `target/yin-repl.js`.\n   504\t- **One Dart lane per host at a time**, even across clones: the lane shards up to\n   505\t  `min(8, cores)` Flutter processes and shares the host's Flutter cache.\n   506\t- **Different branches in different clones** are independent, so two branches may\n   507\t  run on one host if its cores and RAM allow (62 GB each).\n   508\t- Do not treat this as permission to overlap lanes on the laptop.\n   509\t\n   510\tThe first run on shiva (2026-10-11) overlapped JVM and Dart in one clone before\n   511\tthis rule was written down; its results are advisory until repeated with a\n   512\tseparate Dart clone.\n   513\t\n   514\t### The jolt J2 lane: run it with `--jobs` on the servers\n   515\t\n   516\tThe jolt lane's core mode (`bb src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj core [--jobs N]\n   517\t[--only re] [--timeout-ms M]`) runs each test namespace as its own child jolt\n   518\tprocess (own Chez VM, own native parser library load, own log under\n   519\t`build/j2-logs/core/`), so the namespaces cannot corrupt one another — the\n   520\tonly thing `--jobs N` overlaps is the waiting. The default is `jobs 1`\n   521\t(strictly serial), which on jupiter makes the full ~179-namespace lane a\n   522\t5-6-hour run.\n   523\t\n   524\tOn the servers, run it with `--jobs 16`:\n   525\t\n   526\t- jolt children are essentially single-threaded (the 16 MiB parse thread\n   527\t  only burns during parses) and cost 1-2 GB each, so 16 concurrent children\n   528\t  sit far inside jupiter's 48 cores / 62 GB and shiva's 24 / 62;\n   529\t- the lane's wall time is dominated by a few long namespaces\n   530\t  (`yin.repl.python-antlr-test` has an explicit 3-hour step,\n   531\t  `yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test` needs one — see\n   532\t  `step-timeout-ms` in `src/dev/jolt_j2_lane.clj`), so beyond ~16 workers\n   533\t  the critical path is the longest child, not the count;\n   534\t- **parallel is unproven until checked once**: the recorded lane evidence\n   535\t  (J2 closure, the safepoint 60/265,225/0 pass) was all produced `jobs 1`.\n   536\t  The first parallel run must be compared per-namespace against a serial\n   537\t  baseline; any namespace that flips red gets one serial re-run to\n   538\t  attribute before its evidence is trusted. Until that first comparison\n   539\t  passes, keep `jobs 1` for anything whose verdict is timing-sensitive —\n   540\t  timeout and wall-time measurements, native-memory/leak gates, and the\n   541\t  merge-decision qualification runs.\n   542\t\n   543\tSuites that exceed the lane's default step budget are pinned in the lane's\n   544\t`step-timeout-ms` map with their measured wall time; a namespace timing out\n   545\tunder the default budget is a reason to measure it serially and add an\n   546\tentry, not to re-run under the same bound.\n   547\t\n   548\t### The full run\n   549\t\n   550\tRun long jobs inside `tmux` so the SSH session can drop. The script below does the\n   551\tserial prerequisites once, then runs the JVM and Node lanes in the first clone and\n   552\tthe Dart lane in a second clone, all concurrently, with the same commands the `bb`\n   553\ttasks use (the `bb test` task runs them one after another), and records each\n   554\tlane's exit code and seconds. Make the Dart clone the same way as the first, at the\n   555\tsame commit, with a name like `~/ci/datomworld-<name>-dart`:\n   556\t\n   557\t```sh\n   558\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n   559\t# ~/ci/run-full.sh <jvm-node-clone> [<dart-clone>]   (both hosts run all three lanes; a second clone for Dart is recommended)\n   560\tset -u\n   561\texport PATH=\"$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:$PATH\"\n   562\tDART=\"${2:-}\"\n   563\tcd \"$1\" || exit 2\n   564\tmise trust >/dev/null 2>&1\n   565\teval \"$(mise env -s bash)\"\n   566\tLOG=\"$1/target-ci\"; mkdir -p \"$LOG\"\n   567\tts() { date +%H:%M:%S; }\n   568\techo \"start $(ts) $(git rev-parse --short HEAD)\" | tee \"$LOG/summary.txt\"\n   569\tnpm ci --silent >\"$LOG/npm.log\" 2>&1               && echo \"npm ok $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"\n   570\tbb build:yin-repl-node >\"$LOG/build-node.log\" 2>&1 && echo \"node repl built $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"\n   571\tbb gen:antlr >\"$LOG/antlr.log\" 2>&1         && echo \"antlr ok $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"\n   572\tbb build:yin-repl-peer >\"$LOG/build-peer.log\" 2>&1 && echo \"dart peer built $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"\n   573\tlane() { name=$1; shift; s=$(date +%s); \"$@\" >\"$LOG/$name.log\" 2>&1; rc=$?\n   574\t         echo \"$name rc=$rc secs=$(( $(date +%s)-s )) $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"; }\n   575\tlane jvm  clojure -M:test -e :slow &\n   576\tlane node clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test &\n   577\tif [ -n \"$DART\" ]; then                            # its own clone (own lib/cljd-out, build/)\n   578\t  ( cd \"$DART\" && mise trust >/dev/null 2>&1 && eval \"$(mise env -s bash)\"\n   579\t    bb build:yin-repl-peer >\"$LOG/build-peer-dart.log\" 2>&1\n   580\t    lane dart bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj ) &\n   581\tfi\n   582\twait\n   583\techo \"done $(ts)\" | tee -a \"$LOG/summary.txt\"\n   584\t```\n   585\t\n   586\t```sh\n   587\tssh <host> 'tmux new-session -d -s ci-full \"bash -lc \\\"~/ci/run-full.sh ~/ci/datomworld-<name> ~/ci/datomworld-<name>-dart > ~/ci/run-full.out 2>&1\\\"\"'\n   588\t```\n   589\t\n   590\tWatch it: `ssh <host>`, then `tmux attach -t ci-full` (detach with `Ctrl-b d`; do not\n   591\tpress Ctrl-C inside it), or `tail -f ~/ci/datomworld-<name>/target-ci/{jvm,node,dart}.log`\n   592\tand `cat .../summary.txt` (all logs and the summary are in the first clone). The session's own output is empty by design: the lanes\n   593\twrite to the logs. The JVM lane uses `-e :slow`, so it skips `^:slow` tests, like\n   594\t`bb test:clj`. For the slow set use `-i :slow` (or `bb test:slow`); the slow C4\n   595\tscanner row took about 11-19 minutes on the JVM and about 79 minutes on Node\n   596\t(measured 2026-10-11).\n   597\t\n   598\t### Known differences from the laptop\n   599\t\n   600\t- **`dao.stream.datagram.dart-test/refusals-and-lifecycle-events` fails on Linux.**\n   601\t  The assertion \"a bind on a taken port deposits bind-failed\" gets no `bind-failed`\n   602\t  event. A second UDP bind on a taken port evidently behaves differently on Linux\n   603\t  than on macOS (inferred, not confirmed). The test is in `dao.stream`, which the\n   604\t  semantic-register slices do not touch: treat it as a known Linux-only failure,\n   605\t  not a regression, until it is fixed or guarded.\n   606\t- A JVM lane started before the Dart peer is built skips the Dart-peer tests with a\n   607\t  printed notice. The script builds the peer first so they run.\n   608\t- Both hosts run other work (a QEMU guest and rustdesk on shiva); idle load is\n   609\t  under 1, but timings are not a clean benchmark.\n   610\t\n   611\t### The nightly full suite and the branch-testing rule (2026-10-30 owner ruling)\n   612\t\n   613\tOwner, verbatim: \"since the complete test can take a good 7-8hrs to run\n   614\tcompletely, it should be schedule to run once a day at 3am. while\n   615\tbranch/worktree test should only run test that are targeting code\n   616\tchanges\" — and, clarifying the nightly's target: \"it should not be for\n   617\tonly a worktree/branch. the nightly complete test should be for master.\"\n   618\t\n   619\tTwo tiers, by target and purpose:\n   620\t\n   621\t- **The nightly full suite runs MASTER ONLY** (`~/ci/nightly-full.sh` on\n   622\t  shiva, tmux session `nightly`, scheduled 03:00 daily through the\n   623\t  orchestrator's automation; it fetches and checks out origin/master\n   624\t  before anything runs). Every lane, every host target: the JVM full\n   625\t  suite, the full Node suite, the full Dart suite. Its results are a\n   626\t  post-hoc integrity net for master, NOT a landing gate. Failures it\n   627\t  finds route to fix rounds the next morning.\n   628\t- **Branch/worktree testing runs only the namespaces that target the\n   629\t  changed code** (the diff's own tests plus the surfaces the diff\n   630\t  touches), one JVM per namespace, plus one cheap portable lane (Node)\n   631\t  when cljc goldens or fixtures moved. Never the full tier on a branch:\n   632\t  a branch gate needs the changed code proven, not the whole tree\n   633\t  re-proven. A branch is never promoted by its own testing — the merge\n   634\t  to master is what puts it under the nightly.\n   635\t\n   636\tAn orchestrator landing a slice cites the subset runs plus the gate\n   637\tsign-off; the nightly catches what the subset could not see, and a red\n   638\tnightly owns the follow-up.\n   639\t\n   640\t### Measured times (first runs, 2026-10-11, commit 84c7c9b7, all lanes concurrent)\n   641\t\n   642\tShiva, Dart lane: 1054 s (17.5 min) cold, with the JVM and Node lanes running beside\n   643\tit, against about 9 minutes on the 8-core laptop run alone. Prerequisites (`npm ci`,\n   644\tNode REPL, ANTLR) took about 30 s; the Dart peer 91 s. JVM and Node lane times are\n   645\tnot recorded yet: fill them in from `summary.txt` after a completed run. Running the\n   646\tlanes concurrently on one host did not make the Dart lane faster, so count on the\n   647\textra cores and a free laptop, and measure before relying on a speedup.\n   648\t\n   649\t### Jupiter verification run (2026-10-29, commit 7c0a078f, scratch clone, sequential lanes)\n   650\t\n   651\tFirst full tri-host verification of jupiter. Prerequisites (npm ci, Node REPL,\n   652\tANTLR via `gen:antlr`, Dart peer) all succeeded; the stale 3.41.9 Flutter was\n   653\treplaced with 3.47.8 before the Dart lane. Results: **JVM quick tier\n   654\t(`test:quick-sharded`, 12 workers) rc=0 in 702 s** (cold, every shard green);\n   655\t**Node quick tier rc=0 in 4583 s** (all tests pass, but roughly 15x the\n   656\tlaptop — route Node lanes to the laptop or shiva); **Dart quick tier\n   657\trc=1 in 1495 s with the ONLY failure the documented known Linux-only red**\n   658\t(`dao.stream.datagram.dart-test/refusals-and-lifecycle-events`, same\n   659\ttaken-port/bind-failed signature recorded above). Routing summary: jupiter\n   660\tis the preferred JVM/sharding box (48 cores); Node stays off it when wall\n   661\ttime matters; Dart works on either host. Timings are single cold runs, not\n   662\tmedians, and two foreign QEMU guests idle on the host.\n   663\t\n   664\tOne exception to the concurrency above: never run two lanes that both trigger\n   665\t`gen:antlr` (the quick `test:cljs`/`test:cljd` tasks) in the SAME worktree at the\n   666\tsame time — they race on `build/antlr` and `lib/antlr` and fail with\n   667\t\"Patch does not apply\" or \"Generated sources differ from the recorded digests\".\n   668\tRun them sequentially, or in separate clones (as the slow-tier harness does).\n   669\tThe fix after a collision is `rm -rf build/antlr lib/antlr` and a rerun; the\n   670\tgenerator is not idempotent over an already-patched tree. Corroborated twice in\n     1\t{:deps {org.clojure/core.async {:mvn/version \"1.8.741\"}\n     2\t        org.clojure/tools.reader {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n     3\t        ring/ring {:mvn/version \"1.14.1\"}\n     4\t        com.cognitect/transit-clj {:mvn/version \"1.0.333\"}\n     5\t        org.replikativ/boring {:mvn/version \"0.1.30\"}\n     6\t        com.datomic/peer {:mvn/version \"1.0.7364\"}\n     7\t        org.postgresql/postgresql {:mvn/version \"42.7.3\"}\n     8\t        org.clojure/data.json {:mvn/version \"2.5.0\"}\n     9\t        http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}\n    10\t        org.jsoup/jsoup {:mvn/version \"1.18.3\"}\n    11\t        instaparse/instaparse {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}\n    12\t        ;; yang.python.antlr: the runtime the generated Python3 parser runs\n    13\t        ;; on; pinned to the tool version in :antlr-gen (they are one release)\n    14\t        org.antlr/antlr4-runtime {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}\n    15\t        criterium/criterium {:mvn/version \"0.4.6\"}\n    16\t        io.github.rctcwyvrn/blake3 {:mvn/version \"1.3\"}\n    17\t        stigmergy/chp {:mvn/version \"0.1.0-SNAPSHOT\"\n    18\t                       :exclusions [refactor-nrepl/refactor-nrepl]}}\n    19\t :cljd/opts {}\n    20\t ;; build/antlr/python3/classes: the generated Python3 parser, produced by\n    21\t ;; `clj -M:antlr-gen` (antlr/python3/manifest.edn); absent until generated\n    22\t :paths [\"src/clj\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/cljs\" \"src/cljd\"\n    23\t         \"build/antlr/python3/classes\" \"build/antlr/php/classes\"\n    24\t         \"build/antlr/typescript/classes\"]\n    25\t :aliases {:clean {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n    26\t                   :exec-fn clean/clean}\n    27\t           :profile-btree {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n    28\t                           :extra-deps {persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n    29\t                                        {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n    30\t                           :main-opts [\"-m\" \"btree-bench\"]}\n    31\t           :test {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n    32\t                  :extra-deps {io.github.cognitect-labs/test-runner\n    33\t                               {:git/tag \"v0.5.1\" :git/sha \"dfb30dd\"}\n    34\t                               ;; latte-kernel: the LaTTe proof assistant's kernel,\n    35\t                               ;; the differential oracle for the yang.clojure gap\n    36\t                               ;; program (pinned; MIT; dependency-free)\n    37\t                               latte-kernel/latte-kernel\n    38\t                               {:git/url \"https://github.com/latte-central/latte-kernel\"\n    39\t                                :git/sha \"86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279\"}}\n    40\t                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cognitect.test-runner\"]\n    41\t                  :exec-fn cognitect.test-runner.api/test}\n    42\t           :nREPL {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n    43\t                   :extra-deps {nrepl/nrepl {:mvn/version \"1.0.0\"}\n    44\t                                cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}}\n    45\t                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"nrepl.cmdline\" \"--middleware\" \"[cider.nrepl/cider-middleware]\"]}\n    46\t           :cljs {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\" \"build/antlr/python3/js\"]\n    47\t                  :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n    48\t                               reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n    49\t                               com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}}\n    50\t           :dev {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n    51\t                 :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n    52\t                              cider/cider-nrepl {:mvn/version \"0.58.0\"}\n    53\t                              reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n    54\t                              com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}\n    55\t                              ;; benchmark baseline + psset-fixtures\n    56\t                              ;; generator only; production uses\n    57\t                              ;; dao.data.btree\n    58\t                              persistent-sorted-set/persistent-sorted-set\n    59\t                              {:mvn/version \"0.3.0\"}}\n    60\t                 :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]}\n    61\t           ;; The one ClojureDart pin. Compose it with the build aliases:\n    62\t           ;; clj -M:clojuredart:cljd ..., clj -M:clojuredart:cljd-yin-repl-build ...\n    63\t           :clojuredart {:extra-deps {sonwh98/clojuredart\n    64\t                                      {:git/url \"https://github.com/sonwh98/ClojureDart.git\"\n    65\t                                       :sha \"7d00ee2aa7fa9d990581e78ebc4a66b93cb70a31\"}\n    66\t                                      }}\n    67\t           :cljd {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n    68\t                  :main-opts [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n    69\t                  :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n    70\t           :server {:extra-deps {http-kit/http-kit {:mvn/version \"2.8.0\"}}\n    71\t                    :jvm-opts [\"-Dconfig=config.clj\"]\n    72\t                    :main-opts [\"-m\" \"world.server\"]}\n    73\t           :clj-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n    74\t           ;; jolt host configuration (docs/design/yin.repl-jolt-implementation.md\n    75\t           ;; §4.2-4.3), run through build/tools/jolt/bin/jolt -Srepro -M:jolt.\n    76\t           ;; src/jolt precedes src/cljc so a host override wins; src/clj is\n    77\t           ;; listed for audited portable namespaces only (its JVM namespaces\n    78\t           ;; are selected away by :jolt reader branches, never loaded). No\n    79\t           ;; generated Java parser classes, no JS/Dart roots, and no\n    80\t           ;; dependency coordinate is fetched until a jolt-loaded namespace\n    81\t           ;; needs one.\n    82\t           :jolt {:replace-paths [\"src/jolt\" \"src/cljc\" \"src/clj\"]\n    83\t                  :replace-deps {}}\n    84\t           :jolt-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.main\"]}\n    85\t           ;; composed after :jolt (-M:jolt:jolt-test): the oracle tests and\n    86\t           ;; src/dev (src/dev/jolt_test_runner.clj and its sentinel)\n    87\t           :jolt-test {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]}\n    88\t           ;; DIAGNOSTIC only (-M:jolt:jolt-diag:jolt-test): a jolt stand-in\n    89\t           ;; for the corpus loader dao.jing.cbor-fixtures, whose root must\n    90\t           ;; precede test (src/dev/jolt_diag/dao/jing/cbor_fixtures.cljc);\n    91\t           ;; jolt puts :extra-paths roots first, in alias order (-Spath)\n    92\t           :jolt-diag {:extra-paths [\"src/dev/jolt_diag\"]}\n    93\t           :cljs-yin-repl\n    94\t           {:extra-paths [\"test\" \"src/dev\"]\n    95\t            :extra-deps {thheller/shadow-cljs {:mvn/version \"3.3.5\"}\n    96\t                         reagent/reagent {:mvn/version \"2.0.1\"}\n    97\t                         com.cognitect/transit-cljs {:mvn/version \"0.8.280\"}}\n    98\t            :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.node-runner\"]}\n    99\t           :fmt {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n   100\t                 :exec-fn tasks/fix-all}\n   101\t           ;; Build-time generation of the grammars-v4 Python3 parser.\n   102\t           ;; The tool version must equal the antlr4-runtime above.\n   103\t           :antlr-gen {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n   104\t                       :extra-deps {org.antlr/antlr4 {:mvn/version \"4.13.2\"}}\n   105\t                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"yang-antlr-gen\"]}\n   106\t           :kondo {:extra-deps {clj-kondo/clj-kondo {:mvn/version \"2026.01.19\"}}\n   107\t                   :main-opts [\"-m\" \"clj-kondo.main\"]}\n   108\t           ;; Development/oracle only (datomic-q-v1 Client oracle runner,\n   109\t           ;; docs/design/dao.space.query.datomic-compat.md); never a production\n   110\t           ;; dependency. Backend deps/config are pinned separately once selected.\n   111\t           :oracle {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\" \"test\"]\n   112\t                    :extra-deps {com.datomic/client-api {:mvn/version \"1.0.69\"}\n   113\t                                 ;; oracle backend: Datomic Local, in-process,\n   114\t                                 ;; run in docker/oracle (dev-scope only)\n   115\t                                 com.datomic/local {:mvn/version \"1.0.301\"}}}\n   116\t           :dbg {:extra-paths [\"test\"]\n   117\t                 :main-opts [\"-m\" \"debug-cljd\"]\n   118\t                 :cljd/opts {:kind :flutter :main datomworld.demo.main}}\n   119\t           :cljd-yin-repl {:main-opts [\"-m\" \"yin.repl.runner\"]}\n   120\t           :cljd-yin-repl-build\n   121\t           {:main-opts  [\"-m\" \"cljd.build\"]\n   122\t            :cljd/opts  {:kind       :dart\n   123\t                         :main       yin.repl.main\n   124\t                         :output-dir \"build/yin-repl\"\n   125\t                         :output-to  \"build/yin-repl/yin_repl.dart\"}}\n   126\t           :dep-graph {:extra-paths [\"src/dev\"]\n   127\t                       :extra-deps {org.clojure/tools.namespace {:mvn/version \"1.5.0\"}}\n   128\t                       :main-opts [\"-m\" \"dep-graph\"]}}}\n   129\t\n   130\t\n   131\t;; clj -X:fmt\n   132\t\n   133\t;; clj -M:nREPL\n   134\t\n   135\t;; clj -M:nREPL:server\n   136\t;; clj -M:test\n   137\t;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-literal-test\n   138\t;; clj -M:test -n yin.vm-continuation-test\n   139\t;; clj -M:test -n yin.repl.python-antlr-test\n   140\t;; clj -X:test :nses '[yin.vm-literal-test yin.vm-test]'\n   141\t;; clj -M:test -v yin.vm-addition-test/test-lambda-with-multiple-operations\n   142\t\n   143\t;; clj -X:clean\n   144\t\n   145\t;; npx shadow-cljs compile test && node target/node-tests.js\n   146\t;; npx shadow-cljs release demo\n   147\t;; clj -M:dev -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n   148\t;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli watch demo\n   149\t;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile demo\n   150\t;; clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release demo\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t;; mise exec -- clj -M:clojuredart:cljd watch \n   154\t;; mise exec -- flutter run \n   155\t\n   156\t;; To start the emulator:                                                                                              ;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34\n   157\t;; flutter emulators --launch Pixel_3_API_34\n   158\t;; emulator -avd Pixel_3_API_34 -no-snapshot-load  \n   159\t;; emulator -list-avds\n   160\t\n   161\t;;  clj -M:dep-graph                    # full report + dep-graph.dot + dep-graph.svg\n   162\t;;  clj -M:dep-graph --filter \"yin.*\"   # only yin namespaces\n   163\t;;  clj -M:dep-graph --layout circo     # choose graphviz layout engine\n   225\t  {:doc \"Run the bootstrapped jolt with build/tools/jolt-env.sh, passing every argument through (e.g. bb jolt:run -Srepro -M:jolt src/dev/jolt_j0c_workers.clj)\"\n   226\t   :task (System/exit\n   227\t           (:exit (apply shell {:continue true} \"sh\" \"-c\"\n   228\t                         \". build/tools/jolt-env.sh && exec \\\"$JOLT_HOME/bin/jolt\\\" \\\"$@\\\"\" \"jolt\"\n   229\t                         *command-line-args*)))}\n   230\t\n   231\t  build:yin-repl-node\n   232\t  {:doc \"Compile the Node yin.repl (shadow-cljs build :yin-repl) to target/yin-repl.js\"\n   233\t   ;; The Node lanes (test:cljs and its variants) depend on this task, so the\n   234\t   ;; generated JavaScript parser reaches them through it.\n   235\t   :depends [deps:npm gen:antlr]\n   236\t   ;; yin.repl.dht-process-test spawns it as the JVM-to-Node reader of\n   237\t   ;; DHT epic S5, a required leg: a missing build fails that test.\n   238\t   :task (shell \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile yin-repl\")}\n   239\t\n   240\t  build:yin-repl-peer\n   241\t  {:doc \"Compile the yin.repl R5 cross-host peer (client role and --serve server role) as a Dart exe\"\n   242\t   ;; The Dart lanes depend on this task, so the generated Dart parser\n   243\t   ;; reaches them through it.\n   244\t   :depends [gen:antlr]\n   245\t   ;; Process B of the R5 slice is a whole program rather than a test\n   246\t   ;; namespace, and this project's cljd.core carries the Flutter extensions,\n   247\t   ;; so only an ahead-of-time build is a peer the plain Dart VM can start.\n   248\t   ;; It is compiled alone and first: the test build rewrites the same\n   249\t   ;; cljd-out tree, so a peer built after it would import a tree it does\n   250\t   ;; not match.  The R5 cross-host tests spawn this one exe from the JVM\n   251\t   ;; and Node lanes, so `bb test` builds it first; a bare `bb test:clj` or\n   252\t   ;; `bb test:cljs` without it skips those tests with a printed notice\n   253\t   ;; rather than failing.\n   254\t   :task (do (shell \"mkdir -p build\")\n   255\t             (shell \"clojure -M:clojuredart:cljd compile yin.repl.slice-peer\")\n   256\t             (shell \"dart compile exe lib/cljd-out/yin/repl/slice-peer.dart -o build/yin-repl-peer\"))}\n   257\t\n   258\t  build:demo\n   259\t  {:doc \"Release-compile the browser demo (shadow-cljs build :demo) to public/js/main.js\"\n   260\t   ;; The demo pulls in yang.python.antlr.parser, whose JavaScript\n   261\t   ;; recognizers live in build/antlr/python3/js (a :cljs classpath root),\n   262\t   ;; so a clean checkout generates them before compiling.\n   263\t   :depends [deps:npm gen:antlr]\n   264\t   :task (shell \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli release demo\")}\n   265\t\n   266\t  ;; Fast default lanes: no ^:slow test, no dao.test-slow/guard body.\n   267\t  test:clj {:doc \"JVM tests, fast: skips ^:slow ones; the DHT process test needs the Node REPL build\"\n   268\t            :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\n   269\t            :task (shell \"clojure -M:test -e :slow\")}\n   270\t\n   271\t  check:node-discovery\n   272\t  {:doc \"Babashka-only, no natives: scan deps.edn :paths + :cljs :extra-paths for .cljc/.cljs namespaces outside test/ matching shadow-cljs.edn :test :ns-regexp (default -test$); fail before Node discovery can load JVM-only code. Rename the ns or guard it with reader conditionals. Self-test: bb src/dev/check_node_discovery_test.clj\"\n   273\t   :task (shell {:shutdown nil} \"bb src/dev/check_node_discovery.clj\")}\n   274\t\n   275\t  test:cljs {:doc \"Node tests, fast: dao.test-slow guarded bodies print SKIP; needs the Node REPL build\"\n   276\t             :depends [check:node-discovery build:yin-repl-node]\n   277\t             :task (shell \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test\")}\n   278\t\n   279\t  test:cljd {:doc \"Dart tests, fast: aggregated shards via src/dev/cljd_agg.clj; guarded bodies print SKIP\"\n   280\t             :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\n   281\t             :task (shell \"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\")}\n   282\t\n   283\t  ;; Every test, slow ones included (about 20+ minutes on the JVM).\n   284\t  test:all:clj {:doc \"Every JVM test, ^:slow included (20+ minutes); for unattended runs\"\n   285\t                :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\n   286\t                :task (shell \"clojure -M:test\")}\n   287\t\n   288\t  test:all:cljs {:doc \"Every Node test, guarded slow bodies included (sets DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\n   289\t                 :depends [check:node-discovery build:yin-repl-node]\n   290\t                 :task (shell {:extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}}\n   291\t                              \"clj -M:cljs -m shadow.cljs.devtools.cli compile test\")}\n   292\t\n   293\t  test:all:cljd {:doc \"Every Dart test, guarded slow bodies included (sets DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\n   294\t                 :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\n   295\t                 :task (shell {:extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}}\n   296\t                              \"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj\")}\n   297\t\n   298\t  ;; Only the slow tests. Node and Dart select by namespace, so the other\n   299\t  ;; tests inside the nine namespaces that use dao.test-slow/guard also run.\n   300\t  test:slow:clj {:doc \"Only the ^:slow JVM tests (about 14 minutes for long-loops-test); for unattended runs\"\n   301\t                 :depends [build:yin-repl-node gen:antlr]\n   302\t                 :task (shell \"clojure -M:test -i :slow\")}\n   303\t\n   304\t  test:slow:cljs {:doc \"Node: only namespaces with dao.test-slow/guard, bodies enabled (DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\n   305\t                  :depends [check:node-discovery build:yin-repl-node]\n   306\t                  :task (let [re (-> (shell {:out :string}\n   307\t                                            \"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --slow-regex\")\n   308\t                                     :out\n   309\t                                     clojure.string/trim)]\n   310\t                          (shell {:extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}}\n   311\t                                 \"clj\" \"-M:cljs\" \"-m\" \"shadow.cljs.devtools.cli\"\n   312\t                                 \"compile\" \"test\" \"--config-merge\"\n   313\t                                 (str \"{:ns-regexp \\\"\" re \"\\\"}\")))}\n   314\t\n   315\t  test:slow:cljd {:doc \"Dart: only generated tests of namespaces with dao.test-slow/guard, bodies enabled (DATOM_SLOW_TESTS=1)\"\n   316\t                  :depends [build:yin-repl-peer]\n   317\t                  :task (shell {:extra-env {\"DATOM_SLOW_TESTS\" \"1\"}}\n   318\t                               \"bb src/dev/cljd_agg.clj --slow-only\")}\n   319\t\n   320\t  test:slow {:doc \"Only the slow tests on every lane: JVM by tag, Node and Dart by namespace\"\n   321\t             :depends [test:slow:clj test:slow:cljs test:slow:cljd]}\n   322\t\n   323\t  test:all {:doc \"Every test on every lane, slow ones included (JVM, Node, Dart)\"\n   324\t            :depends [test:all:clj test:all:cljs test:all:cljd]}\n   325\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
